{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-020", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Smallest number above 10,000 from remainders", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5026, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 363, "reasoning_tokens": 116, "input_tokens": 74, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 531, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "10223", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "10223"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdf85cef9-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d83-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:44-0500", "answer": "First combine the conditions modulo 7 and 11. Write \\(n=7a+3\\). Then\n\\[\n7a+3\\equiv4\\pmod{11},\n\\]\nso \\(a\\equiv8\\pmod{11}\\). Thus \\(n=59+77b\\).\n\nNow impose the condition modulo 13:\n\\[\n59+77b\\equiv7-b\\equiv5\\pmod{13},\n\\]\ngiving \\(b\\equiv2\\pmod{13}\\). Hence \\(n=213+1001c\\).\n\nFinally, modulo 3,\n\\[\n213+1001c\\equiv2c\\equiv2\\pmod3,\n\\]\nso \\(c\\equiv1\\pmod3\\). Therefore all solutions are\n\\[\nn=1214+3003k,\\qquad k\\in\\mathbb Z.\n\\]\n\nFor \\(n>10{,}000\\), the smallest possible \\(k\\) is \\(3\\), yielding\n\\[\nn=1214+3003(3)=10223.\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 10223"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-017", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Sydney call in three other time zones", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6152, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 628, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 124, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1756, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "2026-10-29 21:00, 2026-10-30 04:00, 2026-10-30 13:00", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "2026-10-29 21:00, 2026-10-30 04:00, 2026-10-30 13:00"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdf73fdad-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d81-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:45-0500", "answer": "To determine the local times in Los Angeles, London, and Tokyo for the video call scheduled at 15:00 on Friday, October 30, 2026, in Sydney, we need to account for the time differences between these cities and Sydney on that date.\n\n### Time Zones on October 30, 2026:\n1. **Sydney (AEDT - Australian Eastern Daylight Time)**: UTC+11\n   - Note: On October 30, 2026, Sydney is observing daylight saving time (AEDT, UTC+11), which starts on the first Sunday of October in Australia.\n\n2. **Los Angeles (PDT - Pacific Daylight Time)**: UTC-7\n   - On October 30, 2026, Los Angeles is observing daylight saving time (PDT, UTC-7), which ends on the first Sunday of November in the US. So, PDT is still in effect.\n\n3. **London (GMT - Greenwich Mean Time)**: UTC+0\n   - On October 30, 2026, London is observing standard time (GMT, UTC+0), as daylight saving time (BST, UTC+1) ends on the last Sunday of October in the UK. So, GMT is in effect.\n\n4. **Tokyo (JST - Japan Standard Time)**: UTC+9\n   - Tokyo does not observe daylight saving time, so it is always UTC+9.\n\n### Time Differences:\n- Sydney (UTC+11) to Los Angeles (UTC-7): 18-hour difference (Sydney is ahead)\n- Sydney (UTC+11) to London (UTC+0): 11-hour difference (Sydney is ahead)\n- Sydney (UTC+11) to Tokyo (UTC+9): 2-hour difference (Sydney is ahead)\n\n### Calculations:\n1. **Los Angeles**:\n   - Sydney time: 15:00 (October 30)\n   - Subtract 18 hours: 15:00 - 18:00 = 21:00 on October 29 (previous day)\n\n2. **London**:\n   - Sydney time: 15:00 (October 30)\n   - Subtract 11 hours: 15:00 - 11:00 = 04:00 on October 30\n\n3. **Tokyo**:\n   - Sydney time: 15:00 (October 30)\n   - Subtract 2 hours: 15:00 - 2:00 = 13:00 on October 30\n\n### Final Answer:\nANSWER: 2026-10-29 21:00, 2026-10-30 04:00, 2026-10-30 13:00"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-018", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Two pipes, a drain and a 3/4 tank", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3108, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 358, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 106, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 907, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "540", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "540"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0dbae4f-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d82-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:45-0500", "answer": "I need to find when the tank is exactly 3/4 full, considering the different phases of operation.\n\n## Setting Up Rates\n\n- Pipe A fills at rate: 1/6 tank per hour\n- Pipe B fills at rate: 1/9 tank per hour\n- Drain C empties at rate: 1/12 tank per hour\n\n## Phase 1: Pipes A and B together for 2 hours\n\nCombined rate: 1/6 + 1/9 = 3/18 + 2/18 = 5/18 tank per hour\n\nIn 2 hours: 2 \u00d7 (5/18) = 10/18 = 5/9 of the tank\n\nAfter 2 hours, the tank is 5/9 full.\n\n## Phase 2: Pipe B running, Drain C open (Pipe A shut off)\n\nNet rate: 1/9 - 1/12 = 4/36 - 3/36 = 1/36 tank per hour (filling)\n\nI need to find when the tank reaches 3/4 full.\n\nAmount needed: 3/4 - 5/9 = 27/36 - 20/36 = 7/36 of the tank\n\nTime needed in Phase 2: (7/36) \u00f7 (1/36) = 7 hours\n\n## Total Time\n\nTotal time = 2 hours + 7 hours = 9 hours = 540 minutes\n\nLet me verify: After 9 hours total, we have 5/9 + 7\u00d7(1/36) = 20/36 + 7/36 = 27/36 = 3/4 \u2713\n\nANSWER: 540"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-020", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Smallest number above 10,000 from remainders", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 7308, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 498, "reasoning_tokens": 264, "input_tokens": 74, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 503, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "10223", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "10223"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdf85f60c-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d83-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:46-0500", "answer": "Combine the congruences step by step:\n\n- Write \\(n=7a+3\\). Modulo \\(11\\), \\(7a+3\\equiv4\\), so \\(a\\equiv8\\pmod{11}\\). Thus \\(n=77b+59\\).\n- Modulo \\(13\\), \\(77b+59\\equiv-b+7\\equiv5\\), so \\(b\\equiv2\\pmod{13}\\). Thus \\(n=1001c+213\\).\n- Modulo \\(3\\), \\(1001c+213\\equiv2c\\equiv2\\), so \\(c\\equiv1\\pmod3\\).\n\nTherefore all solutions are\n\\[\nn=3003k+1214,\\qquad k\\in\\mathbb Z.\n\\]\nFor \\(k=2\\), \\(n=7220\\); for \\(k=3\\), \\(n=10223\\). Hence the latter is the smallest solution greater than \\(10{,}000\\).\n\nANSWER: 10223"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-018", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Two pipes, a drain and a 3/4 tank", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4766, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 784, "reasoning_tokens": 517, "input_tokens": 106, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 646, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1575, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "540", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "540"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0dbae4d-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d82-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:46-0500", "answer": "Pipe A rate: \\( \\frac{1}{6} \\) tank/hour  \nPipe B rate: \\( \\frac{1}{9} \\) tank/hour  \nDrain C rate: \\( -\\frac{1}{12} \\) tank/hour  \n\nFirst 2 hours with A and B running:\n\n\\[\n2\\left(\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{9}\\right)\n= 2\\left(\\frac{5}{18}\\right)\n= \\frac{5}{9}\n\\]\n\nSo the tank is \\( \\frac{5}{9} \\) full after 2 hours.\n\nThen B and drain C run together:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{9}-\\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{1}{36}\n\\]\n\nAmount needed to reach \\( \\frac{3}{4} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{5}{9}\n= \\frac{27}{36}-\\frac{20}{36}\n= \\frac{7}{36}\n\\]\n\nTime needed:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{7/36}{1/36} = 7 \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nTotal time:\n\n\\[\n2 + 7 = 9 \\text{ hours} = 540 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 540"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-019", "category": "reasoning", "title": "ABC strings with no repeats, each letter twice", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 7416, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 370, "reasoning_tokens": 141, "input_tokens": 59, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 811, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "294", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "294"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje08034af-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d84-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:47-0500", "answer": "There are \\(3\\cdot 2^7=384\\) strings with no equal adjacent letters.\n\nSubtract those in which some letter appears fewer than twice. For a fixed letter, say A:\n\n- **No A:** The string must alternate B and C, giving \\(2\\) strings.\n- **Exactly one A:** If A is at either endpoint, there are \\(2\\) choices for the alternating remaining letters, giving \\(2\\cdot2=4\\). If A is at one of the \\(6\\) interior positions, the alternating blocks on either side each have \\(2\\) choices, giving \\(6\\cdot4=24\\).\n\nThus there are \\(2+4+24=30\\) bad strings for each letter.\n\nThese bad cases cannot overlap: if two letters each appeared at most once, the third would appear at least \\(6\\) times, impossible without equal adjacent letters in a length-\\(8\\) string.\n\nTherefore the required count is\n\\[\n384-3(30)=294.\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 294"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-018", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Two pipes, a drain and a 3/4 tank", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3831, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 234, "reasoning_tokens": 78, "input_tokens": 107, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 397, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "540", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "540"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0dbae4e-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d82-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:48-0500", "answer": "In the first 2 hours, pipes A and B fill\n\\[\n2\\left(\\frac16+\\frac19\\right)=\\frac59\n\\]\nof the tank.\n\nAfter A is shut off and C is opened, the net filling rate is\n\\[\n\\frac19-\\frac1{12}=\\frac1{36}\n\\]\nof the tank per hour.\n\nTo reach \\(\\frac34\\), the tank needs another\n\\[\n\\frac34-\\frac59=\\frac7{36},\n\\]\nwhich takes \\(\\frac{7/36}{1/36}=7\\) hours.\n\nTotal time: \\((2+7)\\times60=540\\) minutes.\n\nANSWER: 540"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-020", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Smallest number above 10,000 from remainders", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 11519, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1635, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 73, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3293, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "10223", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "10223"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdf85cef8-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d83-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:50-0500", "answer": "I need to find the smallest integer n > 10,000 satisfying:\n- n \u2261 3 (mod 7)\n- n \u2261 4 (mod 11)\n- n \u2261 5 (mod 13)\n- n \u2261 2 (mod 3)\n\nFirst, let me check if these congruences are consistent. Note that 3, 4, 5 are each 4 less than 7, 11, 13 respectively. So n \u2261 -4 (mod 7), n \u2261 -4 (mod 11), n \u2261 -4 (mod 13).\n\nThis means n + 4 is divisible by 7, 11, and 13. Since these are pairwise coprime, n + 4 is divisible by 7 \u00d7 11 \u00d7 13 = 1001.\n\nSo n \u2261 -4 \u2261 997 (mod 1001), meaning n = 1001k - 4 for some integer k.\n\nNow I need n \u2261 2 (mod 3):\n1001k - 4 \u2261 2 (mod 3)\n\nSince 1001 = 999 + 2 \u2261 2 (mod 3), and -4 \u2261 -1 \u2261 2 (mod 3):\n2k + 2 \u2261 2 (mod 3)\n2k \u2261 0 (mod 3)\nk \u2261 0 (mod 3)\n\nSo k = 3m for some integer m, and n = 1001(3m) - 4 = 3003m - 4.\n\nNow I need n > 10,000:\n3003m - 4 > 10000\n3003m > 10004\nm > 10004/3003 \u2248 3.331\n\nSo the smallest integer m is 4.\n\nn = 3003(4) - 4 = 12012 - 4 = 12008.\n\nLet me verify:\n- 12008 \u00f7 7 = 1715 remainder 3 \u2713 (7 \u00d7 1715 = 12005, 12008 - 12005 = 3)\n- 12008 \u00f7 11 = 1091 remainder 7... wait, let me check: 11 \u00d7 1091 = 12001, 12008 - 12001 = 7. That's not 4!\n\nLet me recheck. I said n \u2261 -4 (mod 11), so n + 4 should be divisible by 11. 12008 + 4 = 12012. 12012 \u00f7 11 = 1092. Yes! So 12008 = 11 \u00d7 1092 - 4 = 12012 - 4 = 12008. Remainder when dividing by 11: 12008 = 11 \u00d7 1091 + 7? No wait: 11 \u00d7 1091 = 12001, remainder 7. But 11 \u00d7 1092 = 12012, so 12008 = 12012 - 4 = 11 \u00d7 1092 - 4. To get positive remainder: 12008 = 11 \u00d7 1091 + 7? That's wrong too.\n\nActually: 12008 = 11 \u00d7 1091 + r where 0 \u2264 r < 11. 11 \u00d7 1091 = 12001. 12008 - 12001 = 7. So remainder is 7, not 4.\n\nHmm, but n \u2261 -4 (mod 11) means n = 11q - 4 for some q. Then n = 11(q-1) + 7, so remainder is 7, not 4. I made an error!\n\nLet me recheck: n \u2261 4 (mod 11) means n = 11q + 4. And n \u2261 -4 (mod 11) means n = 11q - 4 = 11(q-1) + 7. These are different! -4 \u2261 7 (mod 11), not 4.\n\nSo my observation was wrong. Let me recheck: 3 = 7 - 4, so 3 \u2261 -4 (mod 7). \u2713\n4 = 11 - 7, not 11 - 4. So 4 \u2262 -4 (mod 11). Indeed -4 \u2261 7 (mod 11).\n\nLet me redo this properly using CRT.\n\nn \u2261 3 (mod 7)\nn \u2261 4 (mod 11)\nn \u2261 5 (mod 13)\nn \u2261 2 (mod 3)\n\nFrom n \u2261 3 (mod 7): n = 7a + 3\n\nSubstitute into n \u2261 4 (mod 11):\n7a + 3 \u2261 4 (mod 11)\n7a \u2261 1 (mod 11)\n\n7 \u00d7 8 = 56 \u2261 1 (mod 11), so a \u2261 8 (mod 11). Thus a = 11b + 8.\n\nn = 7(11b + 8) + 3 = 77b + 56 + 3 = 77b + 59.\n\nCheck: 77b + 59 \u2261 3 (mod 7)? 77b \u2261 0, 59 = 56 + 3 \u2261 3. \u2713\n77b + 59 \u2261 4 (mod 11)? 77b \u2261 0, 59 = 55 + 4 \u2261 4. \u2713\n\nNow n \u2261 5 (mod 13):\n77b + 59 \u2261 5 (mod 13)\n\n77 = 5 \u00d7 13 + 12 \u2261 12 \u2261 -1 (mod 13)\n59 = 4 \u00d7 13 + 7 \u2261 7 (mod 13)\n\nSo: -b + 7 \u2261 5 (mod 13)\n-b \u2261 -2 (mod 13)\nb \u2261 2 (mod 13)\n\nSo b = 13c + 2.\n\nn = 77(13c + 2) + 59 = 1001c + 154 + 59 = 1001c + 213.\n\nCheck n \u2261 5 (mod 13): 1001 = 77 \u00d7 13 \u2261 0, 213 = 16 \u00d7 13 + 5 = 208 + 5 \u2261 5. \u2713\n\nNow n \u2261 2 (mod 3):\n1001c + 213 \u2261 2 (mod 3)\n\n1001 = 999 + 2 \u2261 2 (mod 3)\n213 = 210 + 3 \u2261 0 (mod 3)\n\nSo: 2c \u2261 2 (mod 3)\nc \u2261 1 (mod 3)\n\nSo c = 3d + 1.\n\nn = 1001(3d + 1) + 213 = 3003d + 1001 + 213 = 3003d + 1214.\n\nNow find smallest n > 10000:\n3003d + 1214 > 10000\n3003d > 8786\nd > 8786/3003 \u2248 2.925\n\nSo d = 3.\n\nn = 3003(3) + 1214 = 9009 + 1214 = 10223.\n\nLet me verify:\n- 10223 \u00f7 7: 7 \u00d7 1460 = 10220, remainder 3 \u2713\n- 10223 \u00f7 11: 11 \u00d7 929 = 10219, remainder 4 \u2713\n- 10223 \u00f7 13: 13 \u00d7 786 = 10218, remainder 5 \u2713\n- 10223 \u00f7 3: 3 \u00d7 3407 = 10221, remainder 2 \u2713\n\nAll check out!\n\nANSWER: 10223"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-018", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Two pipes, a drain and a 3/4 tank", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3539, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 223, "reasoning_tokens": 41, "input_tokens": 107, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 473, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "540", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "540"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0dbae50-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d82-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:52-0500", "answer": "Pipes A and B together fill the tank at\n\\[\n\\frac16+\\frac19=\\frac5{18}\n\\]\nof the tank per hour. After 2 hours, the tank is \\(2\\cdot\\frac5{18}=\\frac59\\) full.\n\nWith A shut off and drain C opened, the net filling rate is\n\\[\n\\frac19-\\frac1{12}=\\frac1{36}\n\\]\nof the tank per hour.\n\nThe remaining amount needed to reach \\(\\frac34\\) is\n\\[\n\\frac34-\\frac59=\\frac7{36},\n\\]\nwhich takes \\(\\frac{7/36}{1/36}=7\\) more hours.\n\nTotal time: \\(2+7=9\\) hours, or \\(540\\) minutes.\n\nANSWER: 540"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-019", "category": "reasoning", "title": "ABC strings with no repeats, each letter twice", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 11244, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 543, "reasoning_tokens": 294, "input_tokens": 59, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 889, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "294", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "294"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje08034b1-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d84-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:52-0500", "answer": "Without the minimum-frequency condition, there are\n\\[\n3\\cdot 2^7=384\n\\]\nstrings with no equal adjacent letters.\n\nNow count strings in which a particular letter, say \\(A\\), appears fewer than twice:\n\n- **No \\(A\\):** The string must alternate between \\(B\\) and \\(C\\), giving \\(2\\) strings.\n- **Exactly one \\(A\\):**\n  - If \\(A\\) is at either endpoint, the remaining letters alternate: \\(2\\cdot2=4\\) strings.\n  - If \\(A\\) is at one of the six interior positions, the blocks on either side independently alternate, each with two choices: \\(6\\cdot2\\cdot2=24\\) strings.\n\nThus there are \\(2+4+24=30\\) invalid strings for each chosen letter.\n\nThese invalid sets do not overlap: if two letters each appeared at most once, the third would appear at least six times, impossible without equal adjacent letters in a length-eight string.\n\nTherefore the required count is\n\\[\n384-3(30)=294.\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 294"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-003", "category": "coding", "title": "Merge labeled intervals", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2577, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 208, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 191, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 880, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 12, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 12}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0edfde0-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba7-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:52-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef merge_intervals(\n    intervals: list[tuple[int, int, str]],\n) -> list[tuple[int, int, list[str]]]:\n    for start, end, _ in intervals:\n        if start >= end:\n            raise ValueError(\"Each interval must have start < end\")\n\n    if not intervals:\n        return []\n\n    ordered = sorted(intervals, key=lambda interval: interval[0])\n    merged: list[tuple[int, int, list[str]]] = []\n\n    current_start, current_end, label = ordered[0]\n    labels = {label}\n\n    for start, end, label in ordered[1:]:\n        if start <= current_end:\n            current_end = max(current_end, end)\n            labels.add(label)\n        else:\n            merged.append((current_start, current_end, sorted(labels)))\n            current_start, current_end = start, end\n            labels = {label}\n\n    merged.append((current_start, current_end, sorted(labels)))\n    return merged\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-020", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Smallest number above 10,000 from remainders", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 15085, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1987, "reasoning_tokens": 1551, "input_tokens": 73, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 958, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 3589, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "10223", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "10223"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdf85f60b-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d83-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:54-0500", "answer": "Solve the congruences step by step.\n\nFrom \\(n \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7}\\) and \\(n \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\\):\n\\[\nn = 3 + 7a\n\\]\n\\[\n3 + 7a \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11} \\implies 7a \\equiv 1 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\nSince \\(7^{-1} \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\\), we get \\(a \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\\), so\n\\[\nn \\equiv 59 \\pmod{77}\n\\]\n\nNow combine with \\(n \\equiv 5 \\pmod{13}\\):\n\\[\nn = 59 + 77b\n\\]\n\\[\n59 + 77b \\equiv 5 \\pmod{13}\n\\]\n\\[\n7 + 12b \\equiv 5 \\pmod{13} \\implies 12b \\equiv 11 \\pmod{13}\n\\]\nSince \\(12 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{13}\\), we get \\(b \\equiv 2 \\pmod{13}\\), so\n\\[\nn \\equiv 213 \\pmod{1001}\n\\]\n\nFinally combine with \\(n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\\):\n\\[\nn = 213 + 1001c\n\\]\n\\[\n213 + 1001c \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\n\\]\nSince \\(213 \\equiv 0\\) and \\(1001 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\\):\n\\[\n2c \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3} \\implies c \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\n\\]\nThus\n\\[\nn \\equiv 1214 \\pmod{3003}\n\\]\n\nSo all solutions are:\n\\[\nn = 1214 + 3003k\n\\]\nFor \\(k=2\\), \\(n = 7220\\), which is not greater than 10000.  \nFor \\(k=3\\), \\(n = 1214 + 9009 = 10223\\).\n\nANSWER: 10223"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-003", "category": "coding", "title": "Merge labeled intervals", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6679, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 397, "reasoning_tokens": 185, "input_tokens": 191, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 885, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 12, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 12}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0edfde1-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba7-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:58-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef merge_intervals(\n    intervals: list[tuple[int, int, str]],\n) -> list[tuple[int, int, list[str]]]:\n    for start, end, _ in intervals:\n        if start >= end:\n            raise ValueError(\"Each interval must have start < end.\")\n\n    if not intervals:\n        return []\n\n    ordered = iter(sorted(intervals, key=lambda interval: interval[0]))\n    current_start, current_end, label = next(ordered)\n    labels = {label}\n    merged: list[tuple[int, int, list[str]]] = []\n\n    for start, end, label in ordered:\n        if start <= current_end:\n            current_end = max(current_end, end)\n            labels.add(label)\n        else:\n            merged.append((current_start, current_end, sorted(labels)))\n            current_start, current_end = start, end\n            labels = {label}\n\n    merged.append((current_start, current_end, sorted(labels)))\n    return merged\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-020", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Smallest number above 10,000 from remainders", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 18936, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2066, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 79, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 4309, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "10223", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "10223"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdf85f60a-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d83-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:58-0500", "answer": "Alright, I have this problem:\n\n**Find the smallest integer n greater than 10,000 such that:**\n1. n leaves remainder 3 when divided by 7 (n \u2261 3 mod 7)\n2. n leaves remainder 4 when divided by 11 (n \u2261 4 mod 11)\n3. n leaves remainder 5 when divided by 13 (n \u2261 5 mod 13)\n4. n leaves remainder 2 when divided by 3 (n \u2261 2 mod 3)\n\n### Understanding the Problem\nFirst, I need to find the smallest integer n > 10,000 that satisfies all four congruence conditions. This is a system of congruences, and I think the Chinese Remainder Theorem (CRT) might be applicable here.\n\n### Step 1: Solve the First Three Congruences\nThe first three conditions are:\n1. n \u2261 3 mod 7\n2. n \u2261 4 mod 11\n3. n \u2261 5 mod 13\n\nI recall that CRT can be used to find a common solution to multiple congruences with pairwise coprime moduli. Since 7, 11, and 13 are all primes, they are pairwise coprime.\n\n#### Step 1.1: Solve n \u2261 3 mod 7 and n \u2261 4 mod 11\nFirst, I need to find numbers that satisfy both n \u2261 3 mod 7 and n \u2261 4 mod 11.\n\nLet's express n as:\nn = 7k + 3, for some integer k.\n\nNow, substitute into the second congruence:\n7k + 3 \u2261 4 mod 11\n=> 7k \u2261 1 mod 11\n\nNow, I need to find the multiplicative inverse of 7 modulo 11, i.e., a number x such that 7x \u2261 1 mod 11.\n\nLet's test:\n7 * 8 = 56 \u2261 1 mod 11 (since 55 is divisible by 11, 56 mod 11 is 1).\n\nThus, the inverse of 7 mod 11 is 8.\n\nMultiply both sides of 7k \u2261 1 mod 11 by 8:\nk \u2261 8 mod 11.\n\nSo, k can be written as:\nk = 11m + 8, for some integer m.\n\nNow, substitute back into n:\nn = 7(11m + 8) + 3 = 77m + 56 + 3 = 77m + 59.\n\nThus, n \u2261 59 mod 77.\n\n#### Step 1.2: Incorporate the Third Congruence n \u2261 5 mod 13\nNow, we have n \u2261 59 mod 77 and n \u2261 5 mod 13.\n\nAgain, express n as:\nn = 77m + 59.\n\nSubstitute into the third congruence:\n77m + 59 \u2261 5 mod 13.\n\nFirst, simplify 77 mod 13 and 59 mod 13:\n- 77 \u00f7 13 = 5 * 13 = 65, remainder 12. So, 77 \u2261 12 mod 13.\n- 59 \u00f7 13 = 4 * 13 = 52, remainder 7. So, 59 \u2261 7 mod 13.\n\nThus:\n12m + 7 \u2261 5 mod 13\n=> 12m \u2261 -2 mod 13\nBut -2 mod 13 is 11, so:\n12m \u2261 11 mod 13.\n\nAgain, find the inverse of 12 mod 13. Since 12 * 12 = 144 \u2261 1 mod 13 (because 143 is divisible by 13), the inverse of 12 mod 13 is 12.\n\nMultiply both sides by 12:\nm \u2261 11 * 12 mod 13\n=> m \u2261 132 mod 13.\n\nNow, simplify 132 mod 13:\n132 \u00f7 13 = 10 * 13 = 130, remainder 2. So, 132 \u2261 2 mod 13.\n\nThus, m \u2261 2 mod 13.\n\nSo, m can be written as:\nm = 13p + 2, for some integer p.\n\nSubstitute back into n:\nn = 77(13p + 2) + 59 = 1001p + 154 + 59 = 1001p + 213.\n\nThus, n \u2261 213 mod 1001.\n\n### Step 2: Incorporate the Fourth Congruence n \u2261 2 mod 3\nNow, we have n \u2261 213 mod 1001 and n \u2261 2 mod 3.\n\nAgain, express n as:\nn = 1001p + 213.\n\nSubstitute into the fourth congruence:\n1001p + 213 \u2261 2 mod 3.\n\nFirst, simplify 1001 mod 3 and 213 mod 3:\n- Sum of digits of 1001: 1 + 0 + 0 + 1 = 2 \u2261 2 mod 3.\n- Sum of digits of 213: 2 + 1 + 3 = 6 \u2261 0 mod 3.\n\nThus:\n2p + 0 \u2261 2 mod 3\n=> 2p \u2261 2 mod 3.\n\nMultiply both sides by the inverse of 2 mod 3. The inverse of 2 mod 3 is 2, because 2 * 2 = 4 \u2261 1 mod 3.\n\nThus:\np \u2261 2 * 2 mod 3\n=> p \u2261 4 mod 3\n=> p \u2261 1 mod 3.\n\nSo, p can be written as:\np = 3q + 1, for some integer q.\n\nSubstitute back into n:\nn = 1001(3q + 1) + 213 = 3003q + 1001 + 213 = 3003q + 1214.\n\nThus, the general solution is:\nn \u2261 1214 mod 3003.\n\n### Step 3: Find the Smallest n > 10,000\nWe need the smallest n > 10,000 that satisfies n \u2261 1214 mod 3003.\n\nThe general form is:\nn = 3003q + 1214.\n\nWe need to find the smallest q such that n > 10,000.\n\nLet's solve:\n3003q + 1214 > 10,000\n=> 3003q > 10,000 - 1214\n=> 3003q > 8786\n=> q > 8786 / 3003 \u2248 2.9257.\n\nSince q must be an integer, the smallest integer q satisfying this is q = 3.\n\nNow, plug q = 3 into the equation:\nn = 3003 * 3 + 1214 = 9009 + 1214 = 10223.\n\nBut we need to verify if q=3 gives n > 10,000 and if q=2 gives n \u2264 10,000.\n\nFor q=2:\nn = 3003 * 2 + 1214 = 6006 + 1214 = 7220 \u2264 10,000.\n\nFor q=3:\nn = 10223 > 10,000.\n\nThus, the smallest n > 10,000 is 10223.\n\n### Verification\nLet's verify all the conditions for n = 10223.\n\n1. 10223 \u00f7 7 = 1460 * 7 = 10"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-002", "category": "coding", "title": "Semantic version range check", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 10309, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1480, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 520, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 5262, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 19, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 19}, "workflow_id": "0sfje19a576d-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba8-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:58-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom functools import total_ordering\n\n_VERSION_RE = re.compile(\n    r'^(0|[1-9]\\d*)\\.(0|[1-9]\\d*)\\.(0|[1-9]\\d*)'\n    r'(?:-((?:0|[1-9]\\d*|\\d*[A-Za-z-][0-9A-Za-z-]*)'\n    r'(?:\\.(?:0|[1-9]\\d*|\\d*[A-Za-z-][0-9A-Za-z-]*))*))?'\n    r'(?:\\+([0-9A-Za-z-]+(?:\\.[0-9A-Za-z-]+)*))?$'\n)\n\n_IDENT_RE = re.compile(r'^[0-9A-Za-z-]+$')\n\n@total_ordering\nclass SemVer:\n    __slots__ = ('major', 'minor', 'patch', 'prerelease')\n\n    def __init__(self, major: int, minor: int, patch: int, prerelease: tuple[str, ...] | None):\n        self.major = major\n        self.minor = minor\n        self.patch = patch\n        self.prerelease = prerelease  # None means no prerelease\n\n    @classmethod\n    def parse(cls, s: str) -> 'SemVer':\n        m = _VERSION_RE.match(s)\n        if not m:\n            raise ValueError(f\"malformed version: {s!r}\")\n        major = int(m.group(1))\n        minor = int(m.group(2))\n        patch = int(m.group(3))\n        pre = m.group(4)\n        # build = m.group(5)  # ignored\n        if pre is None:\n            prerelease = None\n        else:\n            parts = pre.split('.')\n            for p in parts:\n                if not _IDENT_RE.match(p):\n                    raise ValueError(f\"malformed prerelease identifier: {p!r}\")\n            prerelease = tuple(parts)\n        return cls(major, minor, patch, prerelease)\n\n    def _key(self):\n        # For comparison: no prerelease > any prerelease\n        if self.prerelease is None:\n            pre_key = (1,)  # greater than any prerelease tuple\n        else:\n            pre_key = (0,) + tuple(\n                (0, int(p)) if p.isdigit() else (1, p)\n                for p in self.prerelease\n            )\n        return (self.major, self.minor, self.patch, pre_key)\n\n    def __eq__(self, other):\n        if not isinstance(other, SemVer):\n            return NotImplemented\n        return self._key() == other._key()\n\n    def __lt__(self, other):\n        if not isinstance(other, SemVer):\n            return NotImplemented\n        return self._key() < other._key()\n\n    def __hash__(self):\n        return hash(self._key())\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        s = f\"{self.major}.{self.minor}.{self.patch}\"\n        if self.prerelease is not None:\n            s += \"-\" + \".\".join(self.prerelease)\n        return s\n\n\n_OPS = ('>=', '<=', '>', '<', '=', '^', '~')\n\ndef _parse_comparator(comp: str) -> tuple[str, SemVer] | None:\n    \"\"\"Parse a single comparator. Returns (op, version) or None for '*'.\"\"\"\n    comp = comp.strip()\n    if comp == '*':\n        return None\n    op = ''\n    for candidate in _OPS:\n        if comp.startswith(candidate):\n            op = candidate\n            rest = comp[len(candidate):]\n            break\n    else:\n        # no operator means '='\n        op = '='\n        rest = comp\n    rest = rest.strip()\n    if not rest:\n        raise ValueError(f\"malformed comparator: {comp!r}\")\n    ver = SemVer.parse(rest)\n    return (op, ver)\n\n\ndef _expand_caret(ver: SemVer) -> list[tuple[str, SemVer]]:\n    x, y, z = ver.major, ver.minor, ver.patch\n    lower = SemVer(x, y, z, ver.prerelease)\n    if x > 0:\n        upper = SemVer(x + 1, 0, 0, None)\n    elif y > 0:\n        upper = SemVer(0, y + 1, 0, None)\n    else:\n        upper = SemVer(0, 0, z + 1, None)\n    return [('>=', lower), ('<', upper)]\n\n\ndef _expand_tilde(ver: SemVer) -> list[tuple[str, SemVer]]:\n    x, y, z = ver.major, ver.minor, ver.patch\n    lower = SemVer(x, y, z, ver.prerelease)\n    upper = SemVer(x, y + 1, 0, None)\n    return [('>=', lower), ('<', upper)]\n\n\ndef _satisfies_one(version: SemVer, op: str, target: SemVer) -> bool:\n    if op == '=':\n        return version == target\n    if op == '>':\n        return version > target\n    if op == '>=':\n        return version >= target\n    if op == '<':\n        return version < target\n    if op == '<=':\n        return version <= target\n    raise ValueError(f\"unknown operator: {op!r}\")\n\n\ndef satisfies(version: str, range_expr: str) -> bool:\n    ver = SemVer.parse(version)\n\n    if not isin"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-017", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Sydney call in three other time zones", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 20458, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 3397, "reasoning_tokens": 3150, "input_tokens": 111, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 736, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 8816, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "2026-10-29 21:00, 2026-10-30 04:00, 2026-10-30 13:00", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "2026-10-29 21:00, 2026-10-30 04:00, 2026-10-30 13:00"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdf73fdae-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d81-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:59-0500", "answer": "On Friday, 30 October 2026, Sydney is observing daylight saving time (AEDT, UTC+11). Converting 15:00 AEDT to UTC gives 04:00 UTC on the same day.\n\n- **Los Angeles** is on Pacific Daylight Time (PDT, UTC\u22127) until 1 November 2026. Subtracting 7 hours from 04:00 UTC yields **21:00 on Thursday, 29 October 2026**.\n- **London** switches from British Summer Time (BST) back to Greenwich Mean Time (GMT, UTC+0) on Sunday, 25 October 2026. Thus, 04:00 UTC corresponds to **04:00 on Friday, 30 October 2026**.\n- **Tokyo** does not observe daylight saving time and remains on Japan Standard Time (JST, UTC+9). Adding 9 hours to 04:00 UTC yields **13:00 on Friday, 30 October 2026**.\n\nANSWER: 2026-10-29 21:00, 2026-10-30 04:00, 2026-10-30 13:00"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-002", "category": "coding", "title": "Semantic version range check", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 14571, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1029, "reasoning_tokens": 205, "input_tokens": 524, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3307, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 19, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 19}, "workflow_id": "0sfje19a576f-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba8-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:16:59-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\n\n_VERSION_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\"\n    r\"(?:-([A-Za-z0-9-]+(?:\\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)*))?\"\n    r\"(?:\\+([A-Za-z0-9-]+(?:\\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)*))?\",\n    re.ASCII,\n)\n_COMPARATOR_RE = re.compile(r\"(>=|<=|=|>|<|\\^|~)?(.+)\", re.ASCII)\n\n\ndef _numeric_key(digits: str) -> tuple[int, str]:\n    # String-based numeric comparison avoids Python's integer-string size limit.\n    normalized = digits.lstrip(\"0\") or \"0\"\n    return len(normalized), normalized\n\n\ndef _increment(digits: str) -> str:\n    chars = list(digits)\n    for i in range(len(chars) - 1, -1, -1):\n        if chars[i] != \"9\":\n            chars[i] = chr(ord(chars[i]) + 1)\n            return \"\".join(chars)\n        chars[i] = \"0\"\n    return \"1\" + \"\".join(chars)\n\n\ndef _version_key(core: tuple[str, str, str], prerelease: str | None):\n    core_key = tuple(_numeric_key(part) for part in core)\n    if prerelease is None:\n        return core_key + ((1,),)\n\n    identifiers = tuple(\n        (0, _numeric_key(part)) if part.isascii() and part.isdigit()\n        else (1, part)\n        for part in prerelease.split(\".\")\n    )\n    return core_key + ((0, identifiers),)\n\n\ndef _parse_version(text: str):\n    match = _VERSION_RE.fullmatch(text)\n    if match is None:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Malformed version: {text!r}\")\n    major, minor, patch, prerelease, _build = match.groups()\n    core = (major, minor, patch)\n    return core, _version_key(core, prerelease)\n\n\ndef satisfies(version: str, range_expr: str) -> bool:\n    _, candidate = _parse_version(version)\n    results = []\n\n    # Validate every comparator, even if an earlier set already matches.\n    for comparator_set in range_expr.split(\"||\"):\n        tokens = comparator_set.split()\n        if not tokens:\n            raise ValueError(\"Range contains an empty comparator set\")\n\n        set_matches = True\n        for token in tokens:\n            if token == \"*\":\n                continue\n\n            match = _COMPARATOR_RE.fullmatch(token)\n            if match is None:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Malformed comparator: {token!r}\")\n\n            operator, operand = match.groups()\n            operator = operator or \"=\"\n            core, target = _parse_version(operand)\n\n            if operator == \"=\":\n                matches = candidate == target\n            elif operator == \">\":\n                matches = candidate > target\n            elif operator == \">=\":\n                matches = candidate >= target\n            elif operator == \"<\":\n                matches = candidate < target\n            elif operator == \"<=\":\n                matches = candidate <= target\n            else:\n                major, minor, patch = core\n                if operator == \"~\":\n                    upper_core = (major, _increment(minor), \"0\")\n                elif major != \"0\":\n                    upper_core = (_increment(major), \"0\", \"0\")\n                elif minor != \"0\":\n                    upper_core = (\"0\", _increment(minor), \"0\")\n                else:\n                    upper_core = (\"0\", \"0\", _increment(patch))\n\n                upper = _version_key(upper_core, None)\n                matches = target <= candidate < upper\n\n            set_matches = set_matches and matches\n\n        results.append(set_matches)\n\n    return any(results)\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-002", "category": "coding", "title": "Semantic version range check", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 14122, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1455, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 534, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 5235, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 19, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 19}, "workflow_id": "0sfje19a5770-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba8-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:01-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Optional\n\ndef satisfies(version: str, range_expr: str) -> bool:\n    # Parse the version\n    v = _parse_version(version)\n\n    # Parse the range expression\n    range_expr = range_expr.strip()\n    if not range_expr:\n        raise ValueError(\"empty range expression\")\n\n    # Split into comparator sets\n    comparator_sets = [s.strip() for s in range_expr.split('||')]\n    if not all(comparator_sets):\n        raise ValueError(\"empty comparator set\")\n\n    # Check if any comparator set is satisfied\n    for comparator_set in comparator_sets:\n        if _satisfies_comparator_set(v, comparator_set):\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef _parse_version(version: str) -> Tuple[int, int, int, Optional[List[str]], Optional[List[str]]]:\n    # Regex for semantic version\n    pattern = r'^(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)(?:-([0-9A-Za-z-]+(?:\\.[0-9A-Za-z-]+)*))?(?:\\+([0-9A-Za-z-]+(?:\\.[0-9A-Za-z-]+)*))?$'\n    match = re.fullmatch(pattern, version)\n    if not match:\n        raise ValueError(f\"malformed version: {version}\")\n\n    major = int(match.group(1))\n    minor = int(match.group(2))\n    patch = int(match.group(3))\n    prerelease = match.group(4).split('.') if match.group(4) else None\n    build = match.group(5).split('.') if match.group(5) else None\n\n    # Validate no leading zeros in numeric parts\n    if (len(match.group(1)) > 1 and match.group(1)[0] == '0') or \\\n       (len(match.group(2)) > 1 and match.group(2)[0] == '0') or \\\n       (len(match.group(3)) > 1 and match.group(3)[0] == '0'):\n        raise ValueError(f\"malformed version: {version}\")\n\n    return (major, minor, patch, prerelease, build)\n\ndef _compare_versions(a: Tuple[int, int, int, Optional[List[str]], Optional[List[str]]],\n                      b: Tuple[int, int, int, Optional[List[str]], Optional[List[str]]]) -> int:\n    # Compare major, minor, patch\n    if a[0] != b[0]:\n        return a[0] - b[0]\n    if a[1] != b[1]:\n        return a[1] - b[1]\n    if a[2] != b[2]:\n        return a[2] - b[2]\n\n    # Compare prerelease\n    a_prerelease = a[3]\n    b_prerelease = b[3]\n\n    if a_prerelease is None and b_prerelease is None:\n        return 0\n    if a_prerelease is None:\n        return 1\n    if b_prerelease is None:\n        return -1\n\n    # Compare prerelease identifiers\n    for i in range(min(len(a_prerelease), len(b_prerelease))):\n        a_id = a_prerelease[i]\n        b_id = b_prerelease[i]\n\n        a_num = a_id.isdigit()\n        b_num = b_id.isdigit()\n\n        if a_num and b_num:\n            a_val = int(a_id)\n            b_val = int(b_id)\n            if a_val != b_val:\n                return a_val - b_val\n        elif a_num:\n            return -1\n        elif b_num:\n            return 1\n        else:\n            if a_id != b_id:\n                return -1 if a_id < b_id else 1\n\n    # Compare lengths\n    return len(a_prerelease) - len(b_prerelease)\n\ndef _satisfies_comparator_set(version: Tuple[int, int, int, Optional[List[str]], Optional[List[str]]],\n                              comparator_set: str) -> bool:\n    comparators = comparator_set.split()\n    if not comparators:\n        raise ValueError(\"empty comparator set\")\n\n    for comparator in comparators:\n        if not _satisfies_comparator(version, comparator):\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef _satisfies_comparator(version: Tuple[int, int, int, Optional[List[str]], Optional[List[str]]],\n                          comparator: str) -> bool:\n    if comparator == '*':\n        return True\n\n    # Parse operator and version\n    op_match = re.match(r'^([=<>~^~]*)(.*)$', comparator)\n    if not op_match:\n        raise ValueError(f\"malformed comparator: {comparator}\")\n\n    op = op_match.group(1)\n    cmp_version_str = op_match.group(2)\n\n    if not cmp_version_str:\n        raise ValueError(f\"malformed comparator: {comparator}\")\n\n    if op == '^':\n        cmp_version = _parse_version(cmp_version_str)\n        major, minor, patch = cmp_version[0], cmp_version[1], cmp_version[2]\n        if ma"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-003", "category": "coding", "title": "Merge labeled intervals", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3080, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 294, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 189, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1210, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 12, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 12}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0edfdde-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba7-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:02-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals: list[tuple[int, int, str]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, list[str]]]:\n    if not intervals:\n        return []\n\n    # Validate intervals without modifying the input\n    for start, end, _ in intervals:\n        if start >= end:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid interval: start ({start}) must be less than end ({end})\")\n\n    # Sort by start, then end, then label for deterministic merging\n    sorted_intervals = sorted(intervals, key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\n\n    merged: list[tuple[int, int, list[str]]] = []\n\n    for start, end, label in sorted_intervals:\n        if not merged:\n            merged.append((start, end, [label]))\n            continue\n\n        last_start, last_end, last_labels = merged[-1]\n\n        # Overlap or touch: last_end >= start (since half-open, touching means last_end == start)\n        if start <= last_end:\n            new_start = last_start\n            new_end = max(last_end, end)\n            # Merge labels, remove duplicates, sort\n            new_labels = sorted(set(last_labels) | {label})\n            merged[-1] = (new_start, new_end, new_labels)\n        else:\n            merged.append((start, end, [label]))\n\n    return merged\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-018", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Two pipes, a drain and a 3/4 tank", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 19244, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2045, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 109, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 5791, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "540", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "540"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0dbd561-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d82-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:03-0500", "answer": "Alright, let's tackle this problem step by step. I'll try to break it down to understand how the tank fills over time with the different pipes and the drain.\n\n### Understanding the Problem\n\nWe have a tank that's initially empty. There are three pipes involved:\n\n1. **Pipe A**: Fills the tank alone in 6 hours.\n2. **Pipe B**: Fills the tank alone in 9 hours.\n3. **Drain C**: Empties the tank alone in 12 hours.\n\nThe sequence of events is:\n\n1. Pipes A and B are open together for the first 2 hours.\n2. After 2 hours, pipe A is shut off, and drain C is opened, while pipe B continues to run.\n3. We need to find out how many minutes after the start the tank is exactly 3/4 full.\n\n### Calculating Rates of Pipes\n\nFirst, let's determine the rates at which each pipe fills or empties the tank. The rate is typically expressed as the fraction of the tank filled or emptied per hour.\n\n- **Pipe A's filling rate**: If it fills the tank in 6 hours, then in 1 hour, it fills 1/6 of the tank.\n- **Pipe B's filling rate**: Fills the tank in 9 hours, so in 1 hour, it fills 1/9 of the tank.\n- **Drain C's emptying rate**: Empties the tank in 12 hours, so in 1 hour, it empties 1/12 of the tank.\n\n### Phase 1: First 2 Hours (Pipes A and B Open)\n\nFor the first 2 hours, both pipes A and B are open. Their combined filling rate is:\n\nCombined rate = Rate of A + Rate of B = (1/6) + (1/9)\n\nTo add these, let's find a common denominator. The least common multiple of 6 and 9 is 18.\n\n- 1/6 = 3/18\n- 1/9 = 2/18\n\nSo, combined rate = 3/18 + 2/18 = 5/18 of the tank per hour.\n\nIn 2 hours, the amount filled is:\n\nAmount filled = Rate \u00d7 Time = (5/18) \u00d7 2 = 10/18 = 5/9 of the tank.\n\nSo, after 2 hours, the tank is 5/9 full.\n\n### Phase 2: After 2 Hours (Pipe A Off, Drain C On, Pipe B On)\n\nNow, pipe A is shut off, drain C is opened, and pipe B continues to run.\n\nThe new combined rate is:\n\nRate of B - Rate of C = (1/9) - (1/12)\n\nAgain, find a common denominator. The least common multiple of 9 and 12 is 36.\n\n- 1/9 = 4/36\n- 1/12 = 3/36\n\nSo, combined rate = 4/36 - 3/36 = 1/36 of the tank per hour.\n\nThis means that after the first 2 hours, the tank is filling at a rate of 1/36 per hour.\n\n### Determining When the Tank is 3/4 Full\n\nAfter 2 hours, the tank is 5/9 full. We want to find out how much more time is needed to reach 3/4 full.\n\nThe difference between 3/4 and 5/9 is:\n\n3/4 - 5/9\n\nFind a common denominator. The least common multiple of 4 and 9 is 36.\n\n- 3/4 = 27/36\n- 5/9 = 20/36\n\nDifference = 27/36 - 20/36 = 7/36\n\nSo, we need to fill an additional 7/36 of the tank.\n\nThe current filling rate is 1/36 per hour, so the time needed to fill 7/36 is:\n\nTime = Amount / Rate = (7/36) / (1/36) = 7 hours.\n\nWait a minute, that seems like a lot. Let me double-check this calculation because filling 7/36 at a rate of 1/36 per hour should indeed take 7 hours, but that would make the total time 2 + 7 = 9 hours, which seems too long given the rates.\n\nBut let's see:\n\nAfter 2 hours: 5/9 full\nAfter next 7 hours: 5/9 + 7*(1/36) = 5/9 + 7/36 = 20/36 + 7/36 = 27/36 = 3/4 full.\n\nSo, the calculation seems correct. The tank reaches 3/4 full at 9 hours after the start.\n\nBut the answer is supposed to be in minutes. 9 hours is 9 \u00d7 60 = 540 minutes.\n\nHowever, this seems counterintuitive because the tank fills quickly in the first 2 hours (5/9) and then very slowly after that (1/36 per hour). Maybe the initial assumption about the sequence is correct, but let me think if there's another way.\n\nWait, is it possible that the tank reaches 3/4 full during the first phase? Let's check:\n\nAfter 2 hours: 5/9 \u2248 0.555..., and 3/4 = 0.75. So no, it's not 3/4 full after 2 hours.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the drain is more powerful than I thought. Let me re-examine the rates.\n\nPipe A: 1/6 per hour\nPipe B: 1/9 per hour\nDrain C: -1/12 per hour\n\nAfter 2 hours: (1/6 + 1/9)*2 = (5/18)*2 = 10/18 = 5/9\n\nThen, rate is 1/9 - 1/12 = 1/36 per hour.\n\nTo go from 5/9 to 3/4:\n\n3/4 - 5/9 = 27/36 - 20/36 = 7/36\n\nTime = (7/36) / (1/36) = 7 hours.\n\nTotal t"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-001", "category": "coding", "title": "ISO 8601 duration to seconds", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 13303, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1601, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 372, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 6759, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0ffd83f-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c3495-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:05-0500", "answer": "Here's the complete function:\n\n```python\nimport re\n\ndef parse_duration(s: str) -> float:\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a string\")\n\n    # Check for empty string or missing leading P\n    if not s or s[0] != 'P':\n        raise ValueError(\"Duration must start with 'P'\")\n\n    # Check for whitespace anywhere\n    if any(c.isspace() for c in s):\n        raise ValueError(\"Whitespace not allowed\")\n\n    # Check for lowercase letters\n    if any(c.islower() for c in s):\n        raise ValueError(\"Lowercase letters not allowed\")\n\n    # Check for signs\n    if '+' in s or '-' in s:\n        raise ValueError(\"Signs not allowed\")\n\n    # The pattern: P followed by optional date components, then optional T with time components\n    # We need to validate structure carefully\n\n    body = s[1:]  # Remove 'P'\n\n    if not body:\n        raise ValueError(\"No components after 'P'\")\n\n    # Split into date part and time part\n    if 'T' in body:\n        if body.count('T') > 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"Multiple 'T' designators\")\n        date_part, time_part = body.split('T', 1)\n        if not time_part:\n            raise ValueError(\"'T' with no time components\")\n    else:\n        date_part = body\n        time_part = None\n\n    # Parse date part: [nY][nM][nW][nD] in that exact order, each at most once\n    date_components = {}  # 'Y', 'M', 'W', 'D' -> value\n    date_order = ['Y', 'M', 'W', 'D']\n\n    i = 0\n    last_date_idx = -1\n    while i < len(date_part):\n        # Parse number (digits, possibly with . or , for last component)\n        num_start = i\n        while i < len(date_part) and date_part[i].isdigit():\n            i += 1\n\n        # Check for fractional part\n        has_fraction = False\n        if i < len(date_part) and date_part[i] in '.,':\n            has_fraction = True\n            i += 1\n            while i < len(date_part) and date_part[i].isdigit():\n                i += 1\n\n        if i == num_start:\n            raise ValueError(\"Expected number in date part\")\n\n        num_str = date_part[num_start:i]\n        # Validate number format\n        if has_fraction:\n            # Replace comma with dot for float conversion\n            num_str_float = num_str.replace(',', '.')\n            try:\n                value = float(num_str_float)\n            except ValueError:\n                raise ValueError(\"Invalid number format\")\n        else:\n            try:\n                value = float(num_str)\n            except ValueError:\n                raise ValueError(\"Invalid number format\")\n\n        # Now expect a designator\n        if i >= len(date_part):\n            raise ValueError(\"Missing designator in date part\")\n\n        designator = date_part[i]\n        i += 1\n\n        if designator not in date_order:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date designator: {designator}\")\n\n        # Check order\n        designator_idx = date_order.index(designator)\n        if designator_idx <= last_date_idx:\n            raise ValueError(\"Date components out of order or repeated\")\n        last_date_idx = designator_idx\n\n        # Check if this is the last component overall (for fraction rule)\n        # We'll check fraction rule after parsing everything\n\n        date_components[designator] = (value, has_fraction, num_str)\n\n    # Parse time part: [nH][nM][nS] in that exact order, each at most once\n    time_components = {}  # 'H', 'M', 'S' -> value\n    time_order = ['H', 'M', 'S']\n\n    if time_part is not None:\n        i = 0\n        last_time_idx = -1\n        while i < len(time_part):\n            # Parse number\n            num_start = i\n            while i < len(time_part) and time_part[i].isdigit():\n                i += 1\n\n            # Check for fractional part\n            has_fraction = False\n            if i < len(time_part) and time_part[i] in '.,':\n                has_fraction = True\n                i += 1\n                while i < len(time_part) and time_part[i].isdigit():\n                    i += 1\n\n            if i == num_start:\n   "}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-001", "category": "coding", "title": "ISO 8601 duration to seconds", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.5, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 11075, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1131, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 387, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 4620, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.5, "total": 20, "failures": [{"test": "assert parse_duration(\"PT1M\") == 60.0", "line": 10, "error": "ValueError: Invalid time component"}, {"test": "assert parse_duration(\"P1D\") == 86400.0", "line": 11, "error": "ValueError: Invalid date component"}, {"test": "assert parse_duration(\"P1Y2M\") == 425 * 86400.0", "line": 12, "error": "ValueError: Invalid date component"}, {"test": "assert parse_duration(\"P1W\") == 604800.0", "line": 13, "error": "ValueError: Invalid date component"}, {"test": "assert parse_duration(\"PT1H30M\") == 5400.0", "line": 14, "error": "ValueError: Invalid time component"}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 10}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0ffd843-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c3495-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:05-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef parse_duration(s: str) -> float:\n    if not s:\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty string\")\n\n    # Check for leading P and overall structure\n    if not s.startswith('P'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing leading P\")\n    if len(s) == 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"P with no components\")\n\n    # Split into date and time parts\n    if 'T' in s:\n        date_part, time_part = s.split('T', 1)\n        if not time_part:\n            raise ValueError(\"T with nothing after it\")\n    else:\n        date_part, time_part = s, ''\n\n    # Validate date part\n    if date_part != 'P':\n        date_components = date_part[1:]  # Remove P\n        if not date_components:\n            raise ValueError(\"P with no components\")\n\n        # Check for valid date components in order: Y, M, W, D\n        date_pattern = r'^(\\d+(\\.\\d+|,\\d+)?Y)?(\\d+M)?(\\d+W)?(\\d+(\\.\\d+|,\\d+)?D)?$'\n        if not re.fullmatch(date_pattern, date_components):\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid date components\")\n\n        # Check that components are in order and no duplicates\n        date_order = ['Y', 'M', 'W', 'D']\n        last_index = -1\n        for component in date_components:\n            if not component[-1] in date_order:\n                raise ValueError(\"Invalid date component\")\n            current_index = date_order.index(component[-1])\n            if current_index <= last_index:\n                raise ValueError(\"Date components out of order or repeated\")\n            last_index = current_index\n\n        # Check fractional part only on last component\n        if '.' in date_components or ',' in date_components:\n            last_component = date_components.split('Y')[-1].split('M')[-1].split('W')[-1].split('D')[0]\n            if not (last_component.startswith('.') or last_component.startswith(',')):\n                raise ValueError(\"Fractional part only allowed on last component\")\n\n    # Validate time part\n    if time_part:\n        # Check for valid time components in order: H, M, S\n        time_pattern = r'^(\\d+(\\.\\d+|,\\d+)?H)?(\\d+M)?(\\d+(\\.\\d+|,\\d+)?S)?$'\n        if not re.fullmatch(time_pattern, time_part):\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid time components\")\n\n        # Check that components are in order and no duplicates\n        time_order = ['H', 'M', 'S']\n        last_index = -1\n        for component in re.findall(r'\\d+(\\.\\d+|,\\d+)?[HMS]', time_part):\n            component = component[0] if isinstance(component, tuple) else component\n            full_component = component + time_part[time_part.find(component) + len(component)]\n            if not full_component[-1] in time_order:\n                raise ValueError(\"Invalid time component\")\n            current_index = time_order.index(full_component[-1])\n            if current_index <= last_index:\n                raise ValueError(\"Time components out of order or repeated\")\n            last_index = current_index\n\n        # Check fractional part only on last component\n        if '.' in time_part or ',' in time_part:\n            last_component = time_part.split('H')[-1].split('M')[-1].split('S')[0]\n            if not (last_component.startswith('.') or last_component.startswith(',')):\n                raise ValueError(\"Fractional part only allowed on last component\")\n\n    # Now parse the components\n    total_seconds = 0.0\n\n    # Parse date components\n    if date_part != 'P':\n        date_str = date_part[1:]  # Remove P\n        components = re.findall(r'(\\d+(?:[.,]\\d+)?[YMWD])', date_str)\n        for comp in components:\n            num_str = comp[:-1]\n            unit = comp[-1]\n            # Replace comma with dot for float conversion\n            num_str = num_str.replace(',', '.')\n            num = float(num_str)\n            if unit == 'Y':\n                total_seconds += num * 365 * 86400\n            elif unit == 'M':  # months\n                total_seconds += num * 30 * 86400\n            elif unit == 'W':\n                total_seconds += num * 7 * 86400\n            elif unit == 'D':\n                total_se"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-001", "category": "coding", "title": "ISO 8601 duration to seconds", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 9004, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 575, "reasoning_tokens": 154, "input_tokens": 375, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1244, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0ffd840-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c3495-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:07-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\n\n_DURATION_PATTERN = re.compile(\n    r\"P\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)Y)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)M)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)W)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)D)?\"\n    r\"(?:T\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)H)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)M)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)S)?\"\n    r\")?\"\n)\n\n\ndef parse_duration(s: str) -> float:\n    match = _DURATION_PATTERN.fullmatch(s)\n    if match is None:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration: {s!r}\")\n\n    values = match.groups()\n    present = [value for value in values if value is not None]\n\n    if not present:\n        raise ValueError(\"Duration must contain at least one component\")\n    if \"T\" in s and not any(value is not None for value in values[4:]):\n        raise ValueError(\"T must be followed by a time component\")\n    if any(\".\" in value or \",\" in value for value in present[:-1]):\n        raise ValueError(\"Only the last component may have a fractional part\")\n\n    factors = (365 * 86400, 30 * 86400, 7 * 86400, 86400, 3600, 60, 1)\n    return sum(\n        (\n            float(value.replace(\",\", \".\")) * factor\n            for value, factor in zip(values, factors)\n            if value is not None\n        ),\n        0.0,\n    )\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-004", "category": "coding", "title": "Next run time for a cron expression", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": false, "score": 0.9412, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 7351, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1433, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 376, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 5751, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.9412, "total": 17, "failures": [{"test": "assert _raises(next_run, \"5/15 * * * *\", \"2026-10-24 00:00\")", "line": 25, "error": "AssertionError: "}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 16}, "workflow_id": "0sfje175567c-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba6-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:09-0500", "answer": "Here's the complete solution:\n\n```python\nimport re\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef _parse_field(field: str, min_val: int, max_val: int, field_name: str) -> set[int]:\n    \"\"\"Parse a cron field into a set of matching values.\"\"\"\n    if not field:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Empty field: {field_name}\")\n\n    values = set()\n    items = field.split(',')\n\n    for item in items:\n        if not item:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Empty item in field: {field_name}\")\n\n        # Check for step\n        step = 1\n        if '/' in item:\n            parts = item.split('/')\n            if len(parts) != 2:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid step syntax: {item}\")\n            base, step_str = parts\n            if not step_str.isdigit():\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid step value: {step_str}\")\n            step = int(step_str)\n            if step < 1:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Step must be >= 1: {step}\")\n        else:\n            base = item\n\n        # Parse base (either *, number, or range)\n        if base == '*':\n            start, end = min_val, max_val\n        elif '-' in base:\n            range_parts = base.split('-')\n            if len(range_parts) != 2:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid range: {base}\")\n            start_str, end_str = range_parts\n            if not start_str.isdigit() or not end_str.isdigit():\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid range values: {base}\")\n            start, end = int(start_str), int(end_str)\n            if start > end:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Descending range: {base}\")\n            if start < min_val or end > max_val:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Range out of bounds: {base}\")\n        else:\n            if not base.isdigit():\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid number: {base}\")\n            start = int(base)\n            end = start\n            if start < min_val or start > max_val:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Value out of range: {start}\")\n\n        # Generate values with step\n        for v in range(start, end + 1, step):\n            values.add(v)\n\n    return values\n\ndef _is_unrestricted(field: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if field is exactly '*' (unrestricted).\"\"\"\n    return field == '*'\n\ndef next_run(expr: str, after: str) -> str:\n    # Parse expression\n    parts = expr.split()\n    if len(parts) != 5:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Expression must have exactly 5 fields, got {len(parts)}\")\n\n    minute_field, hour_field, dom_field, month_field, dow_field = parts\n\n    # Parse fields\n    minutes = _parse_field(minute_field, 0, 59, \"minute\")\n    hours = _parse_field(hour_field, 0, 23, \"hour\")\n    doms = _parse_field(dom_field, 1, 31, \"day of month\")\n    months = _parse_field(month_field, 1, 12, \"month\")\n    dows = _parse_field(dow_field, 0, 6, \"day of week\")\n\n    # Check if day fields are restricted\n    dom_restricted = not _is_unrestricted(dom_field)\n    dow_restricted = not _is_unrestricted(dow_field)\n\n    # Parse after time\n    try:\n        after_dt = datetime.strptime(after, \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\")\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid after format: {after}\")\n\n    # Start checking from the next minute\n    current = after_dt + timedelta(minutes=1)\n    # Replace seconds and microseconds to be safe\n    current = current.replace(second=0, microsecond=0)\n\n    # Search up to 5 years\n    max_time = after_dt + timedelta(days=365 * 5 + 2)  # +2 for leap years\n\n    while current <= max_time:\n        # Check month\n        if current.month not in months:\n            # Move to first day of next month\n            if current.month == 12:\n                current = current.replace(year=current.year + 1, month=1, day=1, hour=0, minute=0)\n            else:\n                current = current.replace(month=current.month + 1, day=1, hour=0, minute=0)\n            continue\n\n        # Check day\n        dom_match = current.day in doms\n        # Python: Monday=0, Sunday=6; Cron: Sunday=0, Saturday=6\n        cron_dow = (current.weekday() + 1) % 7\n    "}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-004", "category": "coding", "title": "Next run time for a cron expression", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 12290, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1013, "reasoning_tokens": 115, "input_tokens": 377, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3714, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfje175567d-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba6-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:12-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom bisect import bisect_right\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\n\ndef next_run(expr: str, after: str) -> str:\n    def parse_field(field: str, low: int, high: int) -> set[int]:\n        values = set()\n        for item in field.split(\",\"):\n            match = re.fullmatch(\n                r\"(\\*|[0-9]+(?:-[0-9]+)?)(?:/([0-9]+))?\", item\n            )\n            if match is None:\n                raise ValueError(\"Malformed cron field\")\n\n            base, step_text = match.groups()\n            step = int(step_text) if step_text is not None else 1\n            if step < 1:\n                raise ValueError(\"Step must be positive\")\n\n            if base == \"*\":\n                start, end = low, high\n            elif \"-\" in base:\n                start, end = map(int, base.split(\"-\"))\n            else:\n                if step_text is not None:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Steps on single numbers are invalid\")\n                start = end = int(base)\n\n            if not low <= start <= end <= high:\n                raise ValueError(\"Invalid range or out-of-range value\")\n\n            values.update(range(start, end + 1, step))\n        return values\n\n    if not isinstance(expr, str) or not isinstance(after, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"expr and after must be strings\")\n\n    fields = expr.split()\n    if len(fields) != 5:\n        raise ValueError(\"Expected exactly five cron fields\")\n\n    minutes, hours, month_days, months, week_days = (\n        parse_field(field, low, high)\n        for field, (low, high) in zip(\n            fields, ((0, 59), (0, 23), (1, 31), (1, 12), (0, 6))\n        )\n    )\n    dom_restricted = fields[2] != \"*\"\n    dow_restricted = fields[4] != \"*\"\n\n    if re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}\", after) is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid after format\")\n    try:\n        start = datetime.strptime(after, \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\")\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid after date or time\") from exc\n\n    # Use a calendar-year horizon, clamping February 29 to February 28.\n    if start.year + 5 > 9999:\n        limit = datetime(9999, 12, 31, 23, 59)\n    else:\n        try:\n            limit = start.replace(year=start.year + 5)\n        except ValueError:\n            limit = start.replace(year=start.year + 5, day=28)\n\n    times = sorted(hour * 60 + minute for hour in hours for minute in minutes)\n    day = start.date()\n    last_day = limit.date()\n\n    while day <= last_day:\n        if day.month in months:\n            dom_match = day.day in month_days\n            dow_match = (day.weekday() + 1) % 7 in week_days\n\n            if dom_restricted and dow_restricted:\n                day_match = dom_match or dow_match\n            elif dom_restricted:\n                day_match = dom_match\n            elif dow_restricted:\n                day_match = dow_match\n            else:\n                day_match = True\n\n            if day_match:\n                index = (\n                    bisect_right(times, start.hour * 60 + start.minute)\n                    if day == start.date()\n                    else 0\n                )\n                if index < len(times):\n                    hour, minute = divmod(times[index], 60)\n                    candidate = datetime(day.year, day.month, day.day, hour, minute)\n                    if candidate <= limit:\n                        return (\n                            f\"{candidate.year:04d}-{candidate.month:02d}-\"\n                            f\"{candidate.day:02d} {hour:02d}:{minute:02d}\"\n                        )\n\n        if day == last_day:\n            break\n        day += timedelta(days=1)\n\n    raise ValueError(\"No matching time within five years\")\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-019", "category": "reasoning", "title": "ABC strings with no repeats, each letter twice", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 33049, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 3368, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 59, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 12522, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "expected": "294", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "216"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje08034b0-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d84-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:13-0500", "answer": "Alright, I have a problem to solve:\n\n**How many strings of length 8 over the letters A, B, and C satisfy both conditions:**\n1. **No two adjacent letters are equal.**\n2. **Each of the three letters appears at least twice.**\n\n### Understanding the Problem\nFirst, I need to understand the problem clearly:\n- **Strings of length 8**: So, sequences like AAAAAAAA, AAABBBCC, etc., but with 8 characters.\n- **Letters A, B, C**: Only these three letters are allowed.\n- **No two adjacent letters are equal**: So, no AA, BB, or CC anywhere in the string.\n- **Each letter appears at least twice**: So, A, B, and C must each appear at least two times in the string.\n\n### Step 1: Total Number of Strings Without Adjacent Letters Equal\nFirst, I recall that for strings of length n over k letters where no two adjacent letters are the same, the number of possible strings is:\n- First character: k choices (A, B, or C).\n- Each subsequent character: (k-1) choices, because it must be different from the previous character.\n\nFor n=8 and k=3:\n- Total strings = 3 * 2^(8-1) = 3 * 2^7 = 3 * 128 = 384.\n\nBut this is just the first condition. We need to satisfy the second condition as well.\n\n### Step 2: Count Strings with Each Letter Appearing at Least Twice\nThis is more complex. We need to find the number of strings of length 8 with no two adjacent letters equal and each of A, B, C appearing at least twice.\n\n#### Approach: Inclusion-Exclusion Principle\nI think I need to consider all possible distributions of A, B, C in the string.\n\nBut first, I need to find all possible combinations of counts of A, B, C that add up to 8, with each count \u2265 2.\n\nPossible combinations:\n1. (2, 3, 3)\n2. (2, 2, 4)\n3. (2, 4, 2)\n4. (4, 2, 2)\n5. (3, 2, 3)\n6. (3, 3, 2)\n7. (2, 2, 4) is the same as (2, 4, 2) and (4, 2, 2) in terms of counts, but the order matters.\n\nBut, because A, B, C are distinct, we need to consider all permutations.\n\n### Step 3: Enumerate Cases\n#### Case 1: Two letters appear twice, and one appears four times (2,2,4)\n- **Subcases**: (2,2,4), (2,4,2), (4,2,2)\n- **Number of ways to arrange**:\n  - For (2,2,4), we need to count the number of valid strings with 2 A's, 2 B's, and 4 C's, no two adjacent letters equal.\n\nBut, how to count this?\n\n### Using Recurrence Relations or Permutation Counting\nThis seems complex. Maybe I need to think about the number of ways to arrange the letters.\n\n#### General Approach\nFor a string of length n with counts (n_A, n_B, n_C) where n_A + n_B + n_C = n, and no two adjacent letters are equal.\n\nThis is similar to counting the number of ways to arrange the letters with the given constraints.\n\n### Using Multinomial Coefficients and Inclusion-Exclusion\nBut, the no two adjacent letters equal condition complicates things.\n\n### Alternative Approach: Recursion\nPerhaps I can use dynamic programming or recursion to count the number of valid strings.\n\nBut, given the complexity, maybe I should consider all possible cases.\n\n### Case Analysis Based on Counts\n#### Case 1: (4, 2, 2)\n- **Total permutations**: 8! / (4! * 2! * 2!) = 420.\nBut, we need to subtract the cases where two identical letters are adjacent.\n\nThis is similar to the problem of counting permutations with restrictions.\n\nBut, the condition is more about no two identical letters being adjacent.\n\n### Using Inclusion-Exclusion for Non-Adjacent Letters\nThis is non-trivial. Maybe I need to think about the number of ways to arrange the letters.\n\n### Using Graph Theory\nThis reminds me of counting the number of valid colorings of a path graph.\n\nBut, I'm not sure how to apply it here.\n\n### Using Recursion with States\nI recall that for such problems, we can use recursion based on the last character and the counts of remaining letters.\n\nDefine f(n, last_char, counts) as the number of strings of length n ending with last_char and counts of A, B, C remaining.\n\nBut, implementing this seems complex.\n\n### Using Known Results\nI found a similar problem: counting the number of strings of length n over k letters with n"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-001", "category": "coding", "title": "ISO 8601 duration to seconds", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 21439, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1398, "reasoning_tokens": 960, "input_tokens": 375, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1299, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0ffd841-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c3495-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:14-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\n\n_DURATION_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"P\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)Y)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)M)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)W)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)D)?\"\n    r\"(?:T\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)H)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)M)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)S)?\"\n    r\")?\"\n)\n\n\ndef parse_duration(s: str) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Convert a duration to seconds using fixed year and month lengths.\"\"\"\n    match = _DURATION_RE.fullmatch(s)\n    if match is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid duration format\")\n\n    parts = match.groups()\n    if not any(part is not None for part in parts):\n        raise ValueError(\"At least one component is required\")\n\n    if \"T\" in s and not any(part is not None for part in parts[4:]):\n        raise ValueError(\"T must be followed by a time component\")\n\n    scales = (31536000, 2592000, 604800, 86400, 3600, 60, 1)\n    components = [\n        (part, scale)\n        for part, scale in zip(parts, scales)\n        if part is not None\n    ]\n\n    if any(\".\" in part or \",\" in part for part, _ in components[:-1]):\n        raise ValueError(\"Only the last component may have a fractional part\")\n\n    return sum(\n        (float(part.replace(\",\", \".\")) * scale for part, scale in components),\n        0.0,\n    )\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-004", "category": "coding", "title": "Next run time for a cron expression", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.7059, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 12314, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1275, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 387, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 5390, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.7059, "total": 17, "failures": [{"test": "assert next_run(\"0 9 * * 1-5\", \"2026-10-24 10:00\") == \"2026-10-26 09:00\"", "line": 11, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert next_run(\"0 12 13 * 5\", \"2026-10-24 00:00\") == \"2026-10-30 12:00\"", "line": 14, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert next_run(\"5 4 * * 0\", \"2026-10-24 23:59\") == \"2026-10-25 04:05\"", "line": 15, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert next_run(\"0 0 * 2 1\", \"2026-10-24 00:00\") == \"2027-02-01 00:00\"", "line": 20, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert _raises(next_run, \"5/15 * * * *\", \"2026-10-24 00:00\")", "line": 25, "error": "AssertionError: "}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 12}, "workflow_id": "0sfje1752f6a-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba6-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:14-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef next_run(expr: str, after: str) -> str:\n    # Parse the after time\n    try:\n        after_dt = datetime.strptime(after, \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\")\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid after time format\")\n\n    # Parse the cron expression\n    parts = expr.split()\n    if len(parts) != 5:\n        raise ValueError(\"Cron expression must have exactly 5 fields\")\n\n    minute_field, hour_field, day_of_month_field, month_field, day_of_week_field = parts\n\n    # Validate and parse each field\n    def parse_field(field: str, min_val: int, max_val: int, field_name: str) -> list:\n        if not field:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Empty {field_name} field\")\n\n        items = field.split(',')\n        values = set()\n\n        for item in items:\n            if not item:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Empty item in {field_name} field\")\n\n            # Handle step patterns\n            step_match = re.fullmatch(r'(\\*|(\\d+)(?:-(\\d+))?)/(\\d+)', item)\n            if step_match:\n                start, a, b, step = step_match.groups()\n                step = int(step)\n                if step < 1:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Step must be >= 1 in {field_name} field\")\n\n                if start == '*':\n                    a_val = min_val\n                    b_val = max_val\n                else:\n                    a_val = int(a)\n                    if b is not None:\n                        b_val = int(b)\n                    else:\n                        b_val = a_val\n\n                    if a_val < min_val or a_val > max_val or b_val < min_val or b_val > max_val:\n                        raise ValueError(f\"Value out of range in {field_name} field\")\n                    if a_val > b_val:\n                        raise ValueError(f\"Descending range in {field_name} field\")\n\n                for val in range(a_val, b_val + 1, step):\n                    values.add(val)\n                continue\n\n            # Handle range\n            range_match = re.fullmatch(r'(\\d+)-(\\d+)', item)\n            if range_match:\n                a, b = map(int, range_match.groups())\n                if a < min_val or a > max_val or b < min_val or b > max_val:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Value out of range in {field_name} field\")\n                if a > b:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Descending range in {field_name} field\")\n                values.update(range(a, b + 1))\n                continue\n\n            # Handle single number\n            if item == '*':\n                values.update(range(min_val, max_val + 1))\n            else:\n                try:\n                    num = int(item)\n                except ValueError:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Invalid item in {field_name} field\")\n                if num < min_val or num > max_val:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Value out of range in {field_name} field\")\n                values.add(num)\n\n        return sorted(values)\n\n    try:\n        minutes = parse_field(minute_field, 0, 59, \"minute\")\n        hours = parse_field(hour_field, 0, 23, \"hour\")\n        days_of_month = parse_field(day_of_month_field, 1, 31, \"day of month\")\n        months = parse_field(month_field, 1, 12, \"month\")\n        days_of_week = parse_field(day_of_week_field, 0, 6, \"day of week\")\n    except ValueError as e:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid cron expression: {e}\")\n\n    # Check for unrestricted day fields\n    day_of_month_unrestricted = (day_of_month_field == '*')\n    day_of_week_unrestricted = (day_of_week_field == '*')\n\n    # Find the next matching time\n    max_time = after_dt + timedelta(days=5*365)  # 5 years\n    current = after_dt + timedelta(minutes=1)\n\n    while current <= max_time:\n        # Check month\n        if current.month not in months:\n            # Jump to next month\n            if current.month == 12:\n                current = current.replace(year=current.year + 1, month=1, day=1, hour=0, minute=0)\n            else:\n         "}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-003", "category": "coding", "title": "Merge labeled intervals", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.5, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2741, "turns": 1, "retries": 1, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 236, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 193, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1063, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.5, "total": 12, "failures": [{"test": "assert merge_intervals([(1, 3, \"a\"), (2, 5, \"b\")]) == [(1, 5, [\"a\", \"b\"])]", "line": 12, "error": "AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'add'"}, {"test": "assert merge_intervals([(1, 3, \"a\"), (3, 4, \"b\")]) == [(1, 4, [\"a\", \"b\"])]", "line": 13, "error": "AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'add'"}, {"test": "assert merge_intervals([(1, 10, \"b\"), (2, 3, \"a\"), (4, 5, \"b\")]) == [(1, 10, [\"a\", \"b\"])]", "line": 15, "error": "AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'add'"}, {"test": "assert merge_intervals([(1, 2, \"a\"), (1, 2, \"a\")]) == [(1, 2, [\"a\"])]", "line": 16, "error": "AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'add'"}, {"test": "assert merge_intervals([(0, 5, \"z\"), (6, 8, \"z\"), (5, 6, \"m\")]) == [(0, 8, [\"m\", \"z\"])]", "line": 17, "error": "AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'add'"}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 6}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0edfde2-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba7-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:21-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals: list[tuple[int, int, str]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, list[str]]]:\n    if not intervals:\n        return []\n\n    # Validate intervals and prepare for processing\n    processed = []\n    for start, end, label in intervals:\n        if start >= end:\n            raise ValueError(\"Interval start must be less than end\")\n        processed.append((start, end, label))\n\n    # Sort intervals by start time\n    processed.sort()\n\n    merged = []\n    current_start, current_end, current_labels = processed[0]\n\n    for start, end, label in processed[1:]:\n        if start <= current_end:  # Overlapping or touching\n            current_end = max(current_end, end)\n            current_labels.add(label)\n        else:\n            # Finalize the current interval\n            merged.append((current_start, current_end, sorted(current_labels)))\n            current_start, current_end, current_labels = start, end, {label}\n\n    # Add the last interval\n    merged.append((current_start, current_end, sorted(current_labels)))\n\n    return merged\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-002", "category": "coding", "title": "Semantic version range check", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 43537, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 3044, "reasoning_tokens": 2048, "input_tokens": 524, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3917, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 19, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 19}, "workflow_id": "0sfje19a576e-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba8-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:28-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\n\ntype _Version = tuple[int, int, int, tuple[int | str, ...] | None]\n\n_VERSION_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.\"\n    r\"(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.\"\n    r\"(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\"\n    r\"(?:-([A-Za-z0-9-]+(?:\\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)*))?\"\n    r\"(?:\\+[A-Za-z0-9-]+(?:\\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)*)?\"\n)\n\n\ndef _decimal(text: str) -> int:\n    # Avoid Python's limit on converting very long decimal strings.\n    value = 0\n    for start in range(0, len(text), 9):\n        chunk = text[start:start + 9]\n        value = value * (10 ** len(chunk)) + int(chunk)\n    return value\n\n\ndef _parse_version(text: str) -> _Version:\n    match = _VERSION_RE.fullmatch(text)\n    if match is None:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Malformed version: {text!r}\")\n\n    prerelease = match.group(4)\n    identifiers = (\n        None\n        if prerelease is None\n        else tuple(\n            _decimal(part) if part.isdigit() else part\n            for part in prerelease.split(\".\")\n        )\n    )\n    return (\n        _decimal(match.group(1)),\n        _decimal(match.group(2)),\n        _decimal(match.group(3)),\n        identifiers,\n    )\n\n\ndef _compare(left: _Version, right: _Version) -> int:\n    left_core, right_core = left[:3], right[:3]\n    if left_core != right_core:\n        return (left_core > right_core) - (left_core < right_core)\n\n    left_pre, right_pre = left[3], right[3]\n    if left_pre is None:\n        return 0 if right_pre is None else 1\n    if right_pre is None:\n        return -1\n\n    for left_id, right_id in zip(left_pre, right_pre):\n        left_numeric = isinstance(left_id, int)\n        right_numeric = isinstance(right_id, int)\n\n        if left_numeric != right_numeric:\n            return -1 if left_numeric else 1\n        if left_id != right_id:\n            return (left_id > right_id) - (left_id < right_id)\n\n    return (len(left_pre) > len(right_pre)) - (\n        len(left_pre) < len(right_pre)\n    )\n\n\ndef satisfies(version: str, range_expr: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return whether version satisfies range_expr; reject malformed input.\"\"\"\n    parsed_version = _parse_version(version)\n    comparator_sets: list[list[tuple[str, _Version]]] = []\n\n    # Validate the entire range before evaluating any comparator set.\n    for set_expr in range_expr.split(\"||\"):\n        tokens = set_expr.split()\n        if not tokens:\n            raise ValueError(\"Range contains an empty comparator set\")\n\n        comparators: list[tuple[str, _Version]] = []\n        for token in tokens:\n            if token == \"*\":\n                continue\n\n            operator = \"=\"\n            operand = token\n            for candidate in (\">=\", \"<=\", \"=\", \">\", \"<\", \"^\", \"~\"):\n                if token.startswith(candidate):\n                    operator = candidate\n                    operand = token[len(candidate):]\n                    break\n\n            bound = _parse_version(operand)\n\n            if operator in (\"^\", \"~\"):\n                major, minor, patch, _ = bound\n                if operator == \"~\":\n                    upper: _Version = (major, minor + 1, 0, None)\n                elif major > 0:\n                    upper = (major + 1, 0, 0, None)\n                elif minor > 0:\n                    upper = (0, minor + 1, 0, None)\n                else:\n                    upper = (0, 0, patch + 1, None)\n\n                comparators.extend(((\">=\", bound), (\"<\", upper)))\n            else:\n                comparators.append((operator, bound))\n\n        comparator_sets.append(comparators)\n\n    for comparators in comparator_sets:\n        for operator, bound in comparators:\n            comparison = _compare(parsed_version, bound)\n            if not {\n                \"=\": comparison == 0,\n                \">\": comparison > 0,\n                \">=\": comparison >= 0,\n                \"<\": comparison < 0,\n                \"<=\": comparison <= 0,\n            }[operator]:\n                break\n        else:\n            return True\n\n    return False\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-019", "category": "reasoning", "title": "ABC strings with no repeats, each letter twice", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 58125, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 9954, "reasoning_tokens": 9675, "input_tokens": 58, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 954, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 28599, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "294", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "294"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje08034ad-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d84-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:43-0500", "answer": "Total strings of length 8 over A, B, C with no adjacent equal letters:\n\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 2^7 = 384\n\\]\n\nNow subtract strings where at least one letter appears at most once.\n\nCount strings where A appears at most once:\n- A appears 0 times: only B and C, alternating, so 2 strings.\n- A appears 1 time: choose A's position.\n  - If A is at an end: 2 positions, and the remaining 7 letters alternate B/C in 2 ways, giving \\(2 \\cdot 2 = 4\\).\n  - If A is in an interior position: 6 positions, and the two remaining blocks each alternate B/C independently in \\(2 \\cdot 2 = 4\\) ways, giving \\(6 \\cdot 4 = 24\\).\n\nSo A appears at most once in \\(2 + 4 + 24 = 30\\) strings.\n\nBy symmetry, the same count applies to B and C.\n\nIf two letters each appeared at most once, then at least 6 of the 8 letters would be the third letter, forcing adjacent equal letters, impossible. So these cases are disjoint.\n\nThus valid strings:\n\n\\[\n384 - 3 \\cdot 30 = 384 - 90 = 294\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 294"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-004", "category": "coding", "title": "Next run time for a cron expression", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 55337, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 3480, "reasoning_tokens": 2436, "input_tokens": 377, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3905, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfje175567e-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba6-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:17:55-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom bisect import bisect_right\nfrom calendar import monthrange\nfrom datetime import date, datetime\n\n\ndef _cron_field(text: str, low: int, high: int) -> set[int]:\n    values = set()\n\n    for item in text.split(\",\"):\n        match = re.fullmatch(r\"(\\*|[0-9]+(?:-[0-9]+)?)(?:/([0-9]+))?\", item)\n        if match is None:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid cron item: {item!r}\")\n\n        base, step_text = match.groups()\n\n        if base == \"*\":\n            start, end = low, high\n        elif \"-\" in base:\n            left, right = base.split(\"-\")\n            start = int(left.lstrip(\"0\") or \"0\")\n            end = int(right.lstrip(\"0\") or \"0\")\n        else:\n            if step_text is not None:\n                raise ValueError(\"Steps on single numbers are not allowed\")\n            start = end = int(base.lstrip(\"0\") or \"0\")\n\n        if not low <= start <= end <= high:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid cron range: {base!r}\")\n\n        step = 1\n        if step_text is not None:\n            digits = step_text.lstrip(\"0\")\n            if not digits:\n                raise ValueError(\"Cron steps must be positive\")\n\n            # Larger steps all select only the range's first value.\n            width = high - low + 1\n            step = int(digits) if len(digits) <= len(str(width)) else width\n\n        values.update(range(start, end + 1, step))\n\n    return values\n\n\ndef next_run(expr: str, after: str) -> str:\n    if not isinstance(expr, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"Cron expression must be a string\")\n\n    fields = expr.split()\n    if len(fields) != 5:\n        raise ValueError(\"Cron expression must contain exactly five fields\")\n\n    minutes, hours, month_days, months, weekdays = [\n        _cron_field(field, low, high)\n        for field, (low, high) in zip(\n            fields, ((0, 59), (0, 23), (1, 31), (1, 12), (0, 6))\n        )\n    ]\n\n    if not isinstance(after, str) or re.fullmatch(\n        r\"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}\", after\n    ) is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"after must have format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM\")\n\n    start = datetime(\n        int(after[0:4]),\n        int(after[5:7]),\n        int(after[8:10]),\n        int(after[11:13]),\n        int(after[14:16]),\n    )\n\n    # Five calendar years, inclusive; February 29 clips to February 28.\n    if start.year + 5 <= 9999:\n        end_year = start.year + 5\n        deadline = start.replace(\n            year=end_year,\n            day=min(start.day, monthrange(end_year, start.month)[1]),\n        )\n    else:\n        deadline = datetime(9999, 12, 31, 23, 59)\n\n    times = sorted(hour * 60 + minute for hour in hours for minute in minutes)\n    start_minute = start.hour * 60 + start.minute\n    first_day = start.date().toordinal()\n    last_day = deadline.date().toordinal()\n\n    dom_unrestricted = fields[2] == \"*\"\n    dow_unrestricted = fields[4] == \"*\"\n\n    for ordinal in range(first_day, last_day + 1):\n        day = date.fromordinal(ordinal)\n        if day.month not in months:\n            continue\n\n        dom_matches = day.day in month_days\n        dow_matches = (day.weekday() + 1) % 7 in weekdays\n\n        if dom_unrestricted:\n            day_matches = dow_unrestricted or dow_matches\n        elif dow_unrestricted:\n            day_matches = dom_matches\n        else:\n            day_matches = dom_matches or dow_matches\n\n        if not day_matches:\n            continue\n\n        index = bisect_right(times, start_minute) if ordinal == first_day else 0\n        if index == len(times):\n            continue\n\n        hour, minute = divmod(times[index], 60)\n        candidate = datetime(day.year, day.month, day.day, hour, minute)\n\n        if candidate > deadline:\n            break\n\n        return (\n            f\"{day.year:04d}-{day.month:02d}-{day.day:02d} \"\n            f\"{hour:02d}:{minute:02d}\"\n        )\n\n    raise ValueError(\"No matching time within five years after after\")\n```"}
