{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-003", "category": "coding", "title": "Merge labeled intervals", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 177875, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 32000, "reasoning_tokens": 31999, "input_tokens": 189, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 0, "finish_reason": "length", "thinking_chars": 122922, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "total": 12, "pass": false, "passed": 0, "error": "no code block found"}, "workflow_id": "0sfje0edfddf-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba7-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:19:50-0500", "answer": ""}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-002", "category": "coding", "title": "Semantic version range check", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 205092, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 28523, "reasoning_tokens": 27201, "input_tokens": 520, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 4744, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 94588, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 19, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 19}, "workflow_id": "0sfje19a576c-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c5ba8-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:20:08-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom typing import Optional, Tuple\n\n_VERSION_RE = re.compile(\n    r'^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)'\n    r'(?:-([0-9A-Za-z-]+(?:\\.[0-9A-Za-z-]+)*))?'\n    r'(?:\\+([0-9A-Za-z-]+(?:\\.[0-9A-Za-z-]+)*))?\\Z'\n)\n\nclass _Version:\n    __slots__ = ('major', 'minor', 'patch', 'prerelease')\n\n    def __init__(self, major: int, minor: int, patch: int, prerelease: Optional[Tuple[str, ...]]):\n        self.major = major\n        self.minor = minor\n        self.patch = patch\n        self.prerelease = prerelease\n\ndef _parse_version(s: str) -> _Version:\n    m = _VERSION_RE.fullmatch(s)\n    if not m:\n        raise ValueError(f\"invalid version: {s!r}\")\n\n    major = int(m.group(1))\n    minor = int(m.group(2))\n    patch = int(m.group(3))\n    pre = m.group(4)\n    prerelease = tuple(pre.split('.')) if pre is not None else None\n\n    return _Version(major, minor, patch, prerelease)\n\ndef _is_numeric_ident(ident: str) -> bool:\n    return all('0' <= ch <= '9' for ch in ident)\n\ndef _compare(a: _Version, b: _Version) -> int:\n    if a.major != b.major:\n        return -1 if a.major < b.major else 1\n    if a.minor != b.minor:\n        return -1 if a.minor < b.minor else 1\n    if a.patch != b.patch:\n        return -1 if a.patch < b.patch else 1\n\n    a_pre = a.prerelease\n    b_pre = b.prerelease\n\n    if a_pre is None and b_pre is None:\n        return 0\n    if a_pre is None:\n        return 1\n    if b_pre is None:\n        return -1\n\n    for x, y in zip(a_pre, b_pre):\n        x_num = _is_numeric_ident(x)\n        y_num = _is_numeric_ident(y)\n\n        if x_num and y_num:\n            xi = int(x)\n            yi = int(y)\n            if xi != yi:\n                return -1 if xi < yi else 1\n        elif x_num != y_num:\n            return -1 if x_num else 1\n        else:\n            if x != y:\n                return -1 if x < y else 1\n\n    if len(a_pre) != len(b_pre):\n        return -1 if len(a_pre) < len(b_pre) else 1\n\n    return 0\n\ndef _parse_comparator(token: str):\n    if token == '*':\n        return ('*', None)\n\n    if token.startswith('>='):\n        op = '>='; rest = token[2:]\n    elif token.startswith('<='):\n        op = '<='; rest = token[2:]\n    elif token.startswith('='):\n        op = '='; rest = token[1:]\n    elif token.startswith('>'):\n        op = '>'; rest = token[1:]\n    elif token.startswith('<'):\n        op = '<'; rest = token[1:]\n    elif token.startswith('^'):\n        op = '^'; rest = token[1:]\n    elif token.startswith('~'):\n        op = '~'; rest = token[1:]\n    else:\n        op = '='; rest = token\n\n    return (op, _parse_version(rest))\n\ndef _caret_upper(v: _Version) -> _Version:\n    if v.major > 0:\n        return _Version(v.major + 1, 0, 0, None)\n    if v.minor > 0:\n        return _Version(0, v.minor + 1, 0, None)\n    return _Version(0, 0, v.patch + 1, None)\n\ndef _parse_range(range_expr: str):\n    if not isinstance(range_expr, str) or range_expr.strip() == '':\n        raise ValueError(\"empty range\")\n\n    sets = []\n    for set_str in range_expr.split('||'):\n        set_str = set_str.strip()\n        if set_str == '':\n            raise ValueError(\"empty comparator set\")\n\n        comps = []\n        for token in set_str.split():\n            comps.append(_parse_comparator(token))\n        sets.append(comps)\n\n    return sets\n\ndef satisfies(version: str, range_expr: str) -> bool:\n    ver = _parse_version(version)\n    sets = _parse_range(range_expr)\n\n    for comps in sets:\n        ok = True\n\n        for op, ref in comps:\n            if op == '*':\n                continue\n\n            cmp = _compare(ver, ref)\n\n            if op == '=':\n                if cmp != 0:\n                    ok = False\n                    break\n            elif op == '>':\n                if cmp <= 0:\n                    ok = False\n                    break\n            elif op == '>=':\n                if cmp < 0:\n                    ok = False\n                    break\n            elif op == '<':\n                if cmp >= 0:\n                    ok = False"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "reasoning-019", "category": "reasoning", "title": "ABC strings with no repeats, each letter twice", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 210801, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 32000, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 58, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 65890, "finish_reason": "length", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "expected": "294", "answer_line_found": false, "extracted": null}, "workflow_id": "0sfje08034ae-d02a-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdf4c0d84-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:20:11-0500", "answer": "I need to find strings of length 8 over {A, B, C} where no two adjacent letters are equal, and each letter appears at least twice.\n\n## Setting Up\n\nSince no two adjacent letters are equal, this is a proper coloring of a path with 3 colors.\n\nLet me denote the counts of A, B, C as $(a, b, c)$ where $a + b + c = 8$ and $a, b, c \\geq 2$.\n\nPossible partitions of 8 into three parts each \u2265 2:\n- (4, 2, 2) and permutations\n- (3, 3, 2) and permutations\n\n## Counting Valid Strings for Each Type\n\nFor a string with no two adjacent equal, I'll use a dynamic programming approach or direct counting.\n\n**Case 1: Counts (4, 2, 2)** \u2014 one letter appears 4 times, two letters appear 2 times each.\n\nBy symmetry, count for (A=4, B=2, C=2) and multiply by 3.\n\nFor A=4, B=2, C=2: I need to arrange 4 A's, 2 B's, 2 C's with no two adjacent equal.\n\nSince A appears 4 times and total length is 8, the A's must be separated. With 4 A's, we need at least 3 non-A's between them, but we only have 4 non-A's total. The pattern must be: A _ A _ A _ A where the 4 blanks are filled with B,B,C,C.\n\nThe structure is: A x A y A z A w where {x,y,z,w} = {B,B,C,C}.\n\nFor no two adjacent equal: we need x \u2260 A (true), y \u2260 A (true), etc., and also x \u2260 y? No wait, let me check: positions are A,x,A,y,A,z,A,w. Adjacent pairs are (A,x), (x,A), (A,y), (y,A), (A,z), (z,A), (A,w). So we need x,y,z,w \u2260 A, which is satisfied.\n\nBut we also need to check if x=y is allowed? The string is A x A y A z A w. Adjacent letters: A-x, x-A, A-y, y-A, A-z, z-A, A-w. So x and y are not adjacent! They're separated by A.\n\nSo any arrangement of B,B,C,C in positions x,y,z,w works. That's $\\binom{4}{2} = 6$ ways.\n\nWait \u2014 I need to verify no two adjacent are equal. The string is A x A y A z A w. Since x,y,z,w \u2208 {B,C}, and A \u2260 B, A \u2260 C, all adjacent pairs are fine.\n\nSo for (A=4, B=2, C=2): 6 strings.\n\nBy symmetry, for each choice of which letter appears 4 times: 6 strings.\nTotal for (4,2,2): 3 \u00d7 6 = 18.\n\n**Case 2: Counts (3, 3, 2)** \u2014 two letters appear 3 times, one letter appears 2 times.\n\nBy symmetry, count for (A=3, B=3, C=2) and multiply by 3.\n\nI need strings with 3 A's, 3 B's, 2 C's, no two adjacent equal.\n\nLet me use DP. Let $f(n, a, b, c, \\text{last})$ be the count. Or use inclusion-exclusion / direct enumeration.\n\nSince C appears only twice, let me think of placing C's first. The two C's divide the string into 3 blocks (before, between, after), each containing only A's and B's with no two adjacent equal.\n\nActually, let me use a different approach. Let me define states based on last letter and remaining counts.\n\nLet $dp(a,b,c,\\text{last})$ = number of ways to arrange remaining $a$ A's, $b$ B's, $c$ C's given last letter was 'last'.\n\nBase: $dp(0,0,0,\\text{last}) = 1$.\n\nI'll compute $dp(3,3,2,\\text{start})$ where start means no constraint (or we can compute total by summing over first letter choices).\n\nActually, let me define $dp(a,b,c,\\text{last})$ where last \u2208 {A,B,C,\u2205}.\n\n$dp(3,3,2,\\emptyset)$: first letter can be A, B, or C.\n- First A: $dp(2,3,2,A)$\n- First B: $dp(3,2,2,B)$\n- First C: $dp(3,3,1,C)$\n\nBy symmetry $dp(2,3,2,A) = dp(3,2,2,B)$ (swap A\u2194B).\n\nLet me compute systematically. I'll use the recurrence: $dp(a,b,c,\\text{last}) = \\sum_{\\text{next} \\neq \\text{last}} dp(a-\\delta_{A}, b-\\delta_{B}, c-\\delta_{C}, \\text{next})$.\n\nComputing bottom-up:\n\n$dp(0,0,0,\\text{any}) = 1$\n\nFor small values:\n- $dp(1,0,0,A) = 0$ (can't place A after A), $dp(1,0,0,B) = 1$ (place A), $dp(1,0,0,C) = 1$\n- $dp(0,1,0,A) = 1$, $dp(0,1,0,B) = 0$, $dp(0,1,0,C) = 1$\n- $dp(0,0,1,A) = 1$, $dp(0,0,1,B) = 1$, $dp(0,0,1,C) = 0$\n\nLet me write a small table. I'll compute $dp(a,b,c,\\text{last})$ for all needed values.\n\nActually, let me be more careful and compute $dp(3,3,2,\\text{last})$ for each last.\n\nI'll organize by total $a+b+c$.\n\n**Total = 1:**\n- $dp(1,0,0,A)=0, dp(1,0,0,B)=1, dp(1,0,0,C)=1$\n- $dp(0,1,0,A)=1, dp(0,1,0,B)=0, dp(0,1,0,C)=1$\n- $dp(0,0,1,A)=1, dp(0,0,1,B)=1, dp(0,0,1,C)=0$\n\n**Total = 2:**\n- $dp(2,0,0,A)=0, dp(2,0,0,B)=dp"}
