{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-005", "category": "coding", "title": "Strict CSV line parser", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2808, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 403, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 244, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1852, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7aefa8a8-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd7-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:03-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef parse_csv_line(line: str, delimiter: str = \",\") -> list[str]:\n    if not isinstance(delimiter, str) or len(delimiter) != 1 or delimiter == '\"':\n        raise ValueError(\"delimiter must be a single character other than '\\\"'\")\n\n    fields: list[str] = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(line)\n\n    while True:\n        # Start of a field\n        if i < n and line[i] == '\"':\n            # Quoted field\n            i += 1\n            chars: list[str] = []\n            closed = False\n            while i < n:\n                c = line[i]\n                if c == '\"':\n                    if i + 1 < n and line[i + 1] == '\"':\n                        chars.append('\"')\n                        i += 2\n                    else:\n                        # Closing quote\n                        i += 1\n                        closed = True\n                        break\n                else:\n                    chars.append(c)\n                    i += 1\n            if not closed:\n                raise ValueError(\"unterminated quoted field\")\n            # After closing quote must be delimiter or end of line\n            if i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                raise ValueError(\"characters after closing quote\")\n            fields.append(\"\".join(chars))\n        else:\n            # Unquoted field: read until delimiter or end of line\n            start = i\n            while i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                if line[i] == '\"':\n                    raise ValueError(\"quote in unquoted field\")\n                i += 1\n            fields.append(line[start:i])\n\n        # After field, either delimiter or end of line\n        if i < n and line[i] == delimiter:\n            i += 1\n            # If delimiter is at end, next iteration will produce trailing empty field\n            continue\n        else:\n            break\n\n    return fields\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-005", "category": "coding", "title": "Strict CSV line parser", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3189, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 301, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 245, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1322, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7aefa8a9-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd7-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:04-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef parse_csv_line(line: str, delimiter: str = \",\") -> list[str]:\n    if not isinstance(delimiter, str) or len(delimiter) != 1 or delimiter == '\"':\n        raise ValueError('delimiter must be a single character other than \\'\"\\'') \n\n    fields: list[str] = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(line)\n\n    while True:\n        if i < n and line[i] == '\"':\n            i += 1\n            chars: list[str] = []\n\n            while True:\n                if i == n:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Unterminated quoted field\")\n\n                if line[i] != '\"':\n                    chars.append(line[i])\n                    i += 1\n                elif i + 1 < n and line[i + 1] == '\"':\n                    chars.append('\"')\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    i += 1\n                    break\n\n            if i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                raise ValueError(\"Closing quote must be followed by delimiter or end of line\")\n\n            fields.append(\"\".join(chars))\n        else:\n            start = i\n            while i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                if line[i] == '\"':\n                    raise ValueError(\"Quote in unquoted field\")\n                i += 1\n            fields.append(line[start:i])\n\n        if i == n:\n            return fields\n\n        i += 1\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-006", "category": "coding", "title": "RFC 6901 JSON Pointer lookup", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2363, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 358, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 322, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1715, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 18, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 18}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7b71e5b5-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934eb-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:04-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef resolve_pointer(doc, pointer: str):\n    if pointer == \"\":\n        return doc\n\n    if not pointer.startswith(\"/\"):\n        raise ValueError(\"pointer must start with '/' or be empty\")\n\n    tokens = pointer.split(\"/\")[1:]\n\n    current = doc\n    for token in tokens:\n        # Decode ~1 before ~0\n        decoded = []\n        i = 0\n        while i < len(token):\n            ch = token[i]\n            if ch == \"~\":\n                if i + 1 >= len(token):\n                    raise ValueError(\"invalid escape: '~' at end of token\")\n                nxt = token[i + 1]\n                if nxt == \"1\":\n                    decoded.append(\"/\")\n                    i += 2\n                elif nxt == \"0\":\n                    decoded.append(\"~\")\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    raise ValueError(\"invalid escape sequence\")\n            else:\n                decoded.append(ch)\n                i += 1\n        key = \"\".join(decoded)\n\n        if isinstance(current, dict):\n            if key not in current:\n                raise KeyError(key)\n            current = current[key]\n        elif isinstance(current, list):\n            if key == \"-\":\n                raise KeyError(key)\n            # Must be ASCII digits, no leading zeros unless \"0\"\n            if not key.isascii() or not key.isdigit():\n                raise ValueError(\"invalid array index\")\n            if len(key) > 1 and key[0] == \"0\":\n                raise ValueError(\"invalid array index: leading zero\")\n            index = int(key)\n            if index >= len(current):\n                raise KeyError(key)\n            current = current[index]\n        else:\n            raise KeyError(key)\n\n    return current\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-007", "category": "coding", "title": "Glob matching with character classes", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5495, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1075, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 294, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 4794, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7afeb15d-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd8-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:05-0500", "answer": "I'll implement this glob matcher using a recursive approach with memoization for efficiency.\n\n```python\ndef glob_match(pattern: str, name: str) -> bool:\n    from functools import lru_cache\n\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def match(p_idx: int, n_idx: int) -> bool:\n        # Both exhausted: match\n        if p_idx == len(pattern) and n_idx == len(name):\n            return True\n        # Pattern exhausted but name remains: no match\n        if p_idx == len(pattern):\n            return False\n\n        p_char = pattern[p_idx]\n\n        # Handle ** (matches any sequence including /)\n        if p_char == '*' and p_idx + 1 < len(pattern) and pattern[p_idx + 1] == '*':\n            # Try matching 0 characters, or consume one character from name\n            # Skip the ** and try matching rest with same name position\n            if match(p_idx + 2, n_idx):\n                return True\n            # Or consume one character from name and keep **\n            if n_idx < len(name) and match(p_idx, n_idx + 1):\n                return True\n            return False\n\n        # Handle single * (matches any sequence without /)\n        if p_char == '*':\n            # Try matching 0 characters\n            if match(p_idx + 1, n_idx):\n                return True\n            # Or consume one character from name (if not /)\n            if n_idx < len(name) and name[n_idx] != '/' and match(p_idx, n_idx + 1):\n                return True\n            return False\n\n        # Handle ? (matches exactly one character other than /)\n        if p_char == '?':\n            if n_idx < len(name) and name[n_idx] != '/':\n                return match(p_idx + 1, n_idx + 1)\n            return False\n\n        # Handle character class [...]\n        if p_char == '[':\n            # Find closing ]\n            j = p_idx + 1\n            if j < len(pattern) and pattern[j] in ('!', '^'):\n                j += 1\n            # Check if ] is first (after optional ! or ^) - it's literal\n            if j < len(pattern) and pattern[j] == ']':\n                j += 1\n            # Find actual closing ]\n            while j < len(pattern) and pattern[j] != ']':\n                j += 1\n\n            if j >= len(pattern):\n                # No closing ], treat [ as literal\n                if n_idx < len(name) and name[n_idx] == '[':\n                    return match(p_idx + 1, n_idx + 1)\n                return False\n\n            # Parse the character class\n            class_start = p_idx + 1\n            negated = False\n            if class_start < len(pattern) and pattern[class_start] in ('!', '^'):\n                negated = True\n                class_start += 1\n\n            # Build set of characters and ranges\n            chars = set()\n            ranges = []\n            k = class_start\n            # Handle ] as first character (literal)\n            if k < j and pattern[k] == ']':\n                chars.add(']')\n                k += 1\n\n            while k < j:\n                if k + 2 < j and pattern[k + 1] == '-' and pattern[k + 2] != ']':\n                    # Range\n                    start = pattern[k]\n                    end = pattern[k + 2]\n                    if ord(start) <= ord(end):\n                        ranges.append((ord(start), ord(end)))\n                    # else: range matches nothing, skip it\n                    k += 3\n                else:\n                    # Single character\n                    chars.add(pattern[k])\n                    k += 1\n\n            # Check if name character matches\n            if n_idx >= len(name):\n                return False\n            c = name[n_idx]\n            if c == '/':\n                return False  # character class never matches /\n\n            matched = c in chars\n            if not matched:\n                code = ord(c)\n                for start, end in ranges:\n                    if start <= code <= end:\n                        matched = True\n                        break\n\n            if negated:\n                matched = not matched\n\n          "}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-008", "category": "coding", "title": "Subtract IPv4 CIDR blocks", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6842, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1303, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 221, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 4807, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7a7cfe14-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd9-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:06-0500", "answer": "I'll write a function that parses CIDR blocks, validates them strictly, and computes the set difference using interval arithmetic.\n\n```python\nimport ipaddress\n\ndef _parse_cidr(s: str) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Parse and validate a CIDR block. Return (network_int, prefix_len).\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise ValueError(f\"not a string: {s!r}\")\n\n    # Must contain exactly one '/'\n    if s.count('/') != 1:\n        raise ValueError(f\"missing or extra '/': {s!r}\")\n\n    addr_part, prefix_part = s.split('/')\n\n    # Check prefix part: digits only, no leading zeros unless \"0\"\n    if not prefix_part.isdigit():\n        raise ValueError(f\"invalid prefix length: {s!r}\")\n    if len(prefix_part) > 1 and prefix_part[0] == '0':\n        raise ValueError(f\"prefix length has leading zero: {s!r}\")\n    prefix_len = int(prefix_part)\n    if prefix_len > 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"prefix length out of range: {s!r}\")\n\n    # Check address part: exactly 4 octets\n    octets = addr_part.split('.')\n    if len(octets) != 4:\n        raise ValueError(f\"not four octets: {s!r}\")\n\n    addr_int = 0\n    for octet in octets:\n        # Must be digits only\n        if not octet.isdigit():\n            raise ValueError(f\"invalid octet: {s!r}\")\n        # No leading zeros unless the octet is \"0\"\n        if len(octet) > 1 and octet[0] == '0':\n            raise ValueError(f\"octet has leading zero: {s!r}\")\n        val = int(octet)\n        if val > 255:\n            raise ValueError(f\"octet out of range: {s!r}\")\n        addr_int = (addr_int << 8) | val\n\n    # Check host bits are not set\n    host_bits = 32 - prefix_len\n    if host_bits > 0 and (addr_int & ((1 << host_bits) - 1)) != 0:\n        raise ValueError(f\"host bits set: {s!r}\")\n\n    return addr_int, prefix_len\n\ndef _cidr_to_range(network: int, prefix_len: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Convert network/prefix to (start, end) inclusive integer range.\"\"\"\n    host_bits = 32 - prefix_len\n    size = 1 << host_bits\n    return network, network + size - 1\n\ndef _range_to_cidrs(start: int, end: int) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Convert an inclusive integer range to minimal list of CIDR blocks.\"\"\"\n    result = []\n    while start <= end:\n        # Find the largest block starting at 'start' that fits within [start, end]\n        # The block size must be a power of 2, and aligned to its size\n        max_size_by_alignment = start & -start if start != 0 else (1 << 32)\n        max_size_by_remaining = end - start + 1\n\n        # Find largest power of 2 <= min(max_size_by_alignment, max_size_by_remaining)\n        size = 1\n        while size * 2 <= max_size_by_alignment and size * 2 <= max_size_by_remaining:\n            size *= 2\n\n        # size is the number of addresses in this block\n        prefix_len = 32 - (size.bit_length() - 1)\n\n        # Format the network address\n        octets = [\n            (start >> 24) & 0xFF,\n            (start >> 16) & 0xFF,\n            (start >> 8) & 0xFF,\n            start & 0xFF,\n        ]\n        result.append(f\"{octets[0]}.{octets[1]}.{octets[2]}.{octets[3]}/{prefix_len}\")\n\n        start += size\n\n    return result\n\ndef cidr_subtract(base: str, remove: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    # Parse and validate base\n    base_net, base_prefix = _parse_cidr(base)\n    base_start, base_end = _cidr_to_range(base_net, base_prefix)\n\n    # Parse and validate all remove blocks, collect their ranges\n    remove_ranges = []\n    for block in remove:\n        net, prefix = _parse_cidr(block)\n        r_start, r_end = _cidr_to_range(net, prefix)\n        remove_ranges.append((r_start, r_end))\n\n    # Sort remove ranges by start\n    remove_ranges.sort()\n\n    # Merge overlapping/adjacent remove ranges\n    merged = []\n    for r_start, r_end in remove_ranges:\n        if merged and r_start <= merged[-1][1] + 1:\n            # Overlapping or adjacent, merge\n            merged[-1] = (merged[-1][0], max(merged[-1][1], r_end))\n        else:\n            merged.append((r_start, r_end))\n\n    # Subtract merged ranges from base range\n    r"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-011", "category": "coding", "title": "Add business days with holidays", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2264, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 412, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 228, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1727, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 15, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 15}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7b9aca96-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dda-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:06-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom datetime import date, timedelta\n\ndef add_business_days(start: str, days: int, holidays: list[str]) -> str:\n    # Validate format and parse start date\n    date_pattern = re.compile(r'^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$')\n\n    def parse_date(s: str, name: str) -> date:\n        if not isinstance(s, str) or not date_pattern.match(s):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be a valid date in YYYY-MM-DD format\")\n        try:\n            return date.fromisoformat(s)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be a valid date in YYYY-MM-DD format\")\n\n    start_date = parse_date(start, \"start\")\n\n    # Parse and validate holidays\n    holiday_set = set()\n    for h in holidays:\n        holiday_set.add(parse_date(h, \"holiday\"))\n\n    def is_business_day(d: date) -> bool:\n        return d.weekday() < 5 and d not in holiday_set\n\n    if days == 0:\n        # Return start if business day, else first business day after\n        current = start_date\n        while not is_business_day(current):\n            current += timedelta(days=1)\n        return current.isoformat()\n\n    if days > 0:\n        # Move forward, counting business days after start\n        current = start_date\n        count = 0\n        while count < days:\n            current += timedelta(days=1)\n            if is_business_day(current):\n                count += 1\n        return current.isoformat()\n\n    else:  # days < 0\n        # Move backward, counting business days before start\n        current = start_date\n        count = 0\n        target = -days\n        while count < target:\n            current -= timedelta(days=1)\n            if is_business_day(current):\n                count += 1\n        return current.isoformat()\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-011", "category": "coding", "title": "Add business days with holidays", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2622, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 238, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 230, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 959, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 15, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 15}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7b9aa381-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dda-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:06-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom datetime import date, timedelta\n\n\ndef add_business_days(start: str, days: int, holidays: list[str]) -> str:\n    def parse_date(value: str) -> date:\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or re.fullmatch(\n            r\"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}\", value\n        ) is None:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date: {value!r}\")\n        return date.fromisoformat(value)\n\n    current = parse_date(start)\n    holiday_dates = {parse_date(value) for value in holidays}\n\n    def is_business_day(value: date) -> bool:\n        return value.weekday() < 5 and value not in holiday_dates\n\n    if days == 0:\n        while not is_business_day(current):\n            current += timedelta(days=1)\n    else:\n        step = timedelta(days=1 if days > 0 else -1)\n        remaining = abs(days)\n        while remaining:\n            current += step\n            if is_business_day(current):\n                remaining -= 1\n\n    return current.isoformat()\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-011", "category": "coding", "title": "Add business days with holidays", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2837, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 272, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 231, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1095, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 15, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 15}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7b9aa384-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dda-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:06-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef add_business_days(start: str, days: int, holidays: list[str]) -> str:\n    # Validate start date\n    try:\n        current = datetime.strptime(start, \"%Y-%m-%d\").date()\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid start date format\")\n\n    # Validate holiday dates\n    holiday_dates = set()\n    for holiday in holidays:\n        try:\n            holiday_date = datetime.strptime(holiday, \"%Y-%m-%d\").date()\n            holiday_dates.add(holiday_date)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid holiday date format\")\n\n    if days == 0:\n        # Check if start is a business day\n        if current.weekday() < 5 and current not in holiday_dates:\n            return start\n        # Find first business day after start\n        days = 1\n\n    step = 1 if days > 0 else -1\n    business_days = abs(days)\n\n    while business_days > 0:\n        current += timedelta(days=step)\n        if current.weekday() < 5 and current not in holiday_dates:\n            business_days -= 1\n\n    return current.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-012", "category": "coding", "title": "Token bucket rate limiter", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1707, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 240, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 249, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1006, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7da23384-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ee-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:07-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef token_bucket(capacity: int, refill_per_sec: float, requests: list[tuple[float, int]]) -> list[bool]:\n    if capacity < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"capacity must be >= 1\")\n    if refill_per_sec < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"refill_per_sec must be >= 0\")\n\n    tokens = float(capacity)\n    last_time: float | None = None\n    result: list[bool] = []\n\n    for timestamp, cost in requests:\n        if not isinstance(cost, int) or isinstance(cost, bool) or cost < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"cost must be an integer >= 1\")\n        if last_time is not None and timestamp < last_time:\n            raise ValueError(\"timestamps must be non-decreasing\")\n\n        if last_time is not None:\n            elapsed = timestamp - last_time\n            tokens = min(float(capacity), tokens + elapsed * refill_per_sec)\n\n        last_time = timestamp\n\n        if tokens >= cost:\n            tokens -= cost\n            result.append(True)\n        else:\n            result.append(False)\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-012", "category": "coding", "title": "Token bucket rate limiter", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3111, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 272, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 257, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1131, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7da23383-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ee-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:08-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef token_bucket(capacity: int, refill_per_sec: float, requests: list[tuple[float, int]]) -> list[bool]:\n    if capacity < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Capacity must be at least 1\")\n    if refill_per_sec < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Refill rate must be non-negative\")\n\n    if not requests:\n        return []\n\n    # Validate requests\n    prev_time = None\n    for timestamp, cost in requests:\n        if not isinstance(cost, int) or cost < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cost must be an integer >= 1\")\n        if prev_time is not None and timestamp < prev_time:\n            raise ValueError(\"Timestamps must be non-decreasing\")\n        prev_time = timestamp\n\n    tokens = float(capacity)\n    last_time = requests[0][0]\n    results = []\n\n    for timestamp, cost in requests:\n        # Refill tokens since last_time\n        time_elapsed = timestamp - last_time\n        tokens = min(capacity, tokens + refill_per_sec * time_elapsed)\n        last_time = timestamp\n\n        if tokens >= cost:\n            tokens -= cost\n            results.append(True)\n        else:\n            results.append(False)\n\n    return results\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-006", "category": "coding", "title": "RFC 6901 JSON Pointer lookup", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4801, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 429, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 324, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 2013, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 18, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 18}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7b71e5b6-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934eb-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:08-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport json\n\ndef resolve_pointer(doc, pointer: str):\n    if not pointer.startswith('/') and pointer != \"\":\n        raise ValueError(\"Pointer must start with '/' or be empty\")\n\n    if pointer == \"\":\n        return doc\n\n    tokens = pointer.split('/')[1:]  # Skip the leading empty string from split\n\n    current = doc\n    for token in tokens:\n        # Decode ~1 and ~0 in the token\n        decoded_token = []\n        i = 0\n        n = len(token)\n        while i < n:\n            if token[i] == '~':\n                if i + 1 >= n:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Invalid escape sequence in pointer\")\n                if token[i+1] == '0':\n                    decoded_token.append('~')\n                    i += 2\n                elif token[i+1] == '1':\n                    decoded_token.append('/')\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Invalid escape sequence in pointer\")\n            else:\n                decoded_token.append(token[i])\n                i += 1\n        decoded_token = ''.join(decoded_token)\n\n        # Navigate based on the type of current\n        if isinstance(current, dict):\n            if decoded_token not in current:\n                raise KeyError(f\"Key not found: {decoded_token}\")\n            current = current[decoded_token]\n        elif isinstance(current, list):\n            if decoded_token == '-':\n                raise KeyError(\"Index '-' refers to non-existent element\")\n            if not decoded_token.isdigit():\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid list index: {decoded_token}\")\n            if len(decoded_token) > 1 and decoded_token[0] == '0':\n                raise ValueError(f\"List index has leading zeros: {decoded_token}\")\n            index = int(decoded_token)\n            if index >= len(current):\n                raise KeyError(f\"Index out of range: {index}\")\n            current = current[index]\n        else:\n            raise KeyError(\"Cannot apply token to non-dict/list\")\n\n    return current\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-006", "category": "coding", "title": "RFC 6901 JSON Pointer lookup", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 7658, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 399, "reasoning_tokens": 117, "input_tokens": 325, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1237, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 18, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 18}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7b720cc9-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934eb-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:09-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef resolve_pointer(doc, pointer: str):\n    if pointer == \"\":\n        return doc\n    if not pointer.startswith(\"/\"):\n        raise ValueError(\"A non-empty JSON Pointer must start with '/'\")\n\n    tokens = pointer.split(\"/\")[1:]\n    for i, token in enumerate(tokens):\n        if re.search(r\"~(?:[^01]|$)\", token):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid escape in reference token: {token!r}\")\n        tokens[i] = token.replace(\"~1\", \"/\").replace(\"~0\", \"~\")\n\n    current = doc\n    for token in tokens:\n        if isinstance(current, dict):\n            current = current[token]\n        elif isinstance(current, list):\n            if token == \"-\":\n                raise KeyError(token)\n            if re.fullmatch(r\"(?:0|[1-9][0-9]*)\", token) is None:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid array index: {token!r}\")\n\n            # Reject huge indices before int() to avoid its digit limit.\n            length = len(current)\n            if len(token) > len(str(length)):\n                raise KeyError(token)\n            index = int(token)\n            if index >= length:\n                raise KeyError(token)\n            current = current[index]\n        else:\n            raise KeyError(token)\n\n    return current\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-008", "category": "coding", "title": "Subtract IPv4 CIDR blocks", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 9792, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 792, "reasoning_tokens": 184, "input_tokens": 224, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 2080, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7a7cfe13-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd9-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:09-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport ipaddress\nimport re\n\n_CIDR_PATTERN = re.compile(\n    r\"(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,2})\\.\"\n    r\"(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,2})\\.\"\n    r\"(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,2})\\.\"\n    r\"(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,2})/([0-9]+)\"\n)\n\n\ndef _parse_cidr(block: str) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    if not isinstance(block, str):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid IPv4 CIDR: {block!r}\")\n\n    match = _CIDR_PATTERN.fullmatch(block)\n    if match is None:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid IPv4 CIDR: {block!r}\")\n\n    octets = [int(part) for part in match.groups()[:4]]\n    prefix_text = match.group(5).lstrip(\"0\") or \"0\"\n    if any(octet > 255 for octet in octets) or len(prefix_text) > 2:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid IPv4 CIDR: {block!r}\")\n\n    prefix = int(prefix_text)\n    if prefix > 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid IPv4 CIDR: {block!r}\")\n\n    address = 0\n    for octet in octets:\n        address = (address << 8) | octet\n\n    size = 1 << (32 - prefix)\n    if address % size:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Host bits set in IPv4 CIDR: {block!r}\")\n\n    return address, address + size - 1\n\n\ndef cidr_subtract(base: str, remove: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    base_start, base_end = _parse_cidr(base)\n\n    # Validate every removal, including those outside base.\n    intervals = []\n    for block in remove:\n        start, end = _parse_cidr(block)\n        start = max(start, base_start)\n        end = min(end, base_end)\n        if start <= end:\n            intervals.append((start, end))\n    intervals.sort()\n\n    result: list[str] = []\n\n    def emit(start: int, end: int) -> None:\n        result.extend(\n            str(network)\n            for network in ipaddress.summarize_address_range(\n                ipaddress.IPv4Address(start),\n                ipaddress.IPv4Address(end),\n            )\n        )\n\n    cursor = base_start\n    for start, end in intervals:\n        if end < cursor:\n            continue\n        if start > cursor:\n            emit(cursor, start - 1)\n        cursor = end + 1\n        if cursor > base_end:\n            break\n\n    if cursor <= base_end:\n        emit(cursor, base_end)\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-010", "category": "coding", "title": "Optimal string alignment distance", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2952, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 282, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 155, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1054, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7e74d81c-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ec-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:11-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef osa_distance(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    if a == b:\n        return 0\n\n    # Keep the shorter string along the columns for O(min(len(a), len(b))) space.\n    if len(a) < len(b):\n        a, b = b, a\n\n    n = len(b)\n    if n == 0:\n        return len(a)\n\n    previous_previous = None\n    previous = list(range(n + 1))\n\n    for i, char_a in enumerate(a, 1):\n        current = [i] + [0] * n\n        for j, char_b in enumerate(b, 1):\n            current[j] = min(\n                previous[j] + 1,                  # Deletion\n                current[j - 1] + 1,               # Insertion\n                previous[j - 1] + (char_a != char_b),  # Substitution\n            )\n\n            if (\n                i > 1\n                and j > 1\n                and char_a == b[j - 2]\n                and a[i - 2] == char_b\n            ):\n                current[j] = min(\n                    current[j],\n                    previous_previous[j - 2] + 1,\n                )\n\n        previous_previous, previous = previous, current\n\n    return previous[n]\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-012", "category": "coding", "title": "Token bucket rate limiter", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5735, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 363, "reasoning_tokens": 108, "input_tokens": 252, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1096, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7da23385-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ee-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:11-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\n\ndef token_bucket(\n    capacity: int,\n    refill_per_sec: float,\n    requests: list[tuple[float, int]],\n) -> list[bool]:\n    if capacity < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"capacity must be at least 1\")\n    if refill_per_sec < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"refill_per_sec must be non-negative\")\n    if not requests:\n        return []\n\n    rate = Fraction(refill_per_sec)\n    tokens = Fraction(capacity)\n    previous_time = None\n    results: list[bool] = []\n\n    for timestamp, cost in requests:\n        if not isinstance(cost, int) or cost < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"cost must be an integer >= 1\")\n\n        current_time = Fraction(timestamp)\n        if previous_time is not None:\n            if current_time < previous_time:\n                raise ValueError(\"timestamps must be non-decreasing\")\n            tokens = min(capacity, tokens + rate * (current_time - previous_time))\n\n        allowed = tokens >= cost\n        if allowed:\n            tokens -= cost\n\n        results.append(allowed)\n        previous_time = current_time\n\n    return results\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-010", "category": "coding", "title": "Optimal string alignment distance", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4422, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 466, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 154, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1595, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7e74d81d-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ec-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:11-0500", "answer": "Here's the Python function `osa_distance` that computes the Optimal String Alignment (OSA) distance between two strings:\n\n```python\ndef osa_distance(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    len_a = len(a)\n    len_b = len(b)\n\n    # Create a distance matrix with (len_a + 1) rows and (len_b + 1) columns\n    d = [[0] * (len_b + 1) for _ in range(len_a + 1)]\n\n    # Initialize the first row and column\n    for i in range(len_a + 1):\n        d[i][0] = i\n    for j in range(len_b + 1):\n        d[0][j] = j\n\n    # Fill the distance matrix\n    for i in range(1, len_a + 1):\n        for j in range(1, len_b + 1):\n            cost = 0 if a[i - 1] == b[j - 1] else 1\n            d[i][j] = min(\n                d[i - 1][j] + 1,      # deletion\n                d[i][j - 1] + 1,      # insertion\n                d[i - 1][j - 1] + cost  # substitution\n            )\n            # Check for transposition\n            if i > 1 and j > 1 and a[i - 1] == b[j - 2] and a[i - 2] == b[j - 1]:\n                d[i][j] = min(d[i][j], d[i - 2][j - 2] + cost)\n\n    return d[len_a][len_b]\n```\n\nThis function implements the OSA distance by:\n1. Creating a distance matrix initialized with the base cases (empty string to non-empty string)\n2. Filling the matrix by considering the cost of insertions, deletions, substitutions, and transpositions\n3. Returning the value in the bottom-right corner of the matrix, which represents the OSA distance between the two strings\n\nThe transposition check is only performed when there are at least two characters in both strings to compare, and it ensures that no substring is edited more than once."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-005", "category": "coding", "title": "Strict CSV line parser", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 11500, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 651, "reasoning_tokens": 342, "input_tokens": 245, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1355, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7aefa8ab-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd7-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:12-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef parse_csv_line(line: str, delimiter: str = \",\") -> list[str]:\n    if not isinstance(delimiter, str) or len(delimiter) != 1 or delimiter == '\"':\n        raise ValueError('delimiter must be a single character other than \"')\n\n    fields: list[str] = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(line)\n\n    while True:\n        if i < n and line[i] == '\"':\n            i += 1\n            chars: list[str] = []\n\n            while True:\n                if i == n:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Unterminated quoted field\")\n\n                if line[i] != '\"':\n                    chars.append(line[i])\n                    i += 1\n                elif i + 1 < n and line[i + 1] == '\"':\n                    chars.append('\"')\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    i += 1\n                    break\n\n            if i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                raise ValueError(\"Unexpected character after closing quote\")\n\n            fields.append(\"\".join(chars))\n        else:\n            start = i\n            while i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                if line[i] == '\"':\n                    raise ValueError(\"Quote in unquoted field\")\n                i += 1\n            fields.append(line[start:i])\n\n        if i == n:\n            return fields\n\n        i += 1  # Skip the delimiter, allowing a trailing empty field.\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-010", "category": "coding", "title": "Optimal string alignment distance", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5899, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 483, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 152, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1577, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7e74b10a-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ec-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:14-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef osa_distance(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the Optimal String Alignment (OSA) distance between two strings.\n\n    OSA distance is the restricted Damerau-Levenshtein distance: the minimum\n    number of insertions, deletions, substitutions, or transpositions of two\n    adjacent characters needed to turn `a` into `b`, with the restriction that\n    no substring is edited more than once (a transposed pair cannot take part\n    in any further edit).\n\n    Comparison is case-sensitive and operates on Python string characters\n    (Unicode code points).\n    \"\"\"\n    m, n = len(a), len(b)\n\n    # dp[i][j] = OSA distance between a[:i] and b[:j]\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(m + 1)]\n\n    # Base cases: empty string to/from non-empty string requires all insertions/deletions\n    for i in range(m + 1):\n        dp[i][0] = i\n    for j in range(n + 1):\n        dp[0][j] = j\n\n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        for j in range(1, n + 1):\n            cost = 0 if a[i - 1] == b[j - 1] else 1\n\n            # Standard Levenshtein operations\n            dp[i][j] = min(\n                dp[i - 1][j] + 1,      # deletion\n                dp[i][j - 1] + 1,      # insertion\n                dp[i - 1][j - 1] + cost  # substitution (or match)\n            )\n\n            # Transposition of two adjacent characters (OSA restriction)\n            # Check if a[i-1] == b[j-2] and a[i-2] == b[j-1]\n            if i > 1 and j > 1 and a[i - 1] == b[j - 2] and a[i - 2] == b[j - 1]:\n                dp[i][j] = min(dp[i][j], dp[i - 2][j - 2] + 1)\n\n    return dp[m][n]\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-006", "category": "coding", "title": "RFC 6901 JSON Pointer lookup", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 17697, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 937, "reasoning_tokens": 641, "input_tokens": 325, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1279, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 18, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 18}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7b720cc8-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934eb-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:18-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef resolve_pointer(doc, pointer: str):\n    if pointer == \"\":\n        return doc\n    if not pointer.startswith(\"/\"):\n        raise ValueError(\"A non-empty JSON Pointer must start with '/'\")\n\n    tokens = pointer.split(\"/\")[1:]\n    for i, token in enumerate(tokens):\n        if re.search(r\"~(?:[^01]|$)\", token):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid escape in reference token: {token!r}\")\n        tokens[i] = token.replace(\"~1\", \"/\").replace(\"~0\", \"~\")\n\n    current = doc\n    for token in tokens:\n        if isinstance(current, dict):\n            current = current[token]\n        elif isinstance(current, list):\n            if token == \"-\":\n                raise KeyError(token)\n            if re.fullmatch(r\"0|[1-9][0-9]*\", token) is None:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid list index: {token!r}\")\n\n            # Compare before converting to avoid Python's integer-string\n            # conversion limit for arbitrarily long index tokens.\n            limit = str(len(current))\n            if len(token) > len(limit) or (\n                len(token) == len(limit) and token >= limit\n            ):\n                raise KeyError(token)\n            current = current[int(token)]\n        else:\n            raise KeyError(token)\n\n    return current\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-009", "category": "coding", "title": "Exact arithmetic expression evaluator", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.95, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 12498, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1294, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 355, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 5426, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.95, "total": 20, "failures": [{"test": "assert evaluate(\"-2 ** 2\") == -4", "line": 15, "error": "AssertionError: "}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 19}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7ecdab85-d02b-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ed-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:18-0500", "answer": "Here's a Python function that evaluates arithmetic expressions exactly as specified, using the `fractions.Fraction` type and without using `eval`, `exec`, `compile`, or the `ast` module. The solution involves tokenizing the input string, parsing it into an abstract syntax tree (AST) according to the specified precedence and associativity rules, and then evaluating the AST.\n\n```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nfrom typing import List, Union, Tuple\n\ndef evaluate(expr: str) -> Fraction:\n    tokens = tokenize(expr)\n    if not tokens:\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty expression\")\n    ast, remaining = parse_expression(tokens)\n    if remaining:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unexpected tokens at end of expression\")\n    return evaluate_ast(ast)\n\ndef tokenize(expr: str) -> List[str]:\n    tokens = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(expr)\n    while i < n:\n        c = expr[i]\n        if c.isspace():\n            i += 1\n            continue\n        if c in '()+-*/**':\n            if c == '*' and i + 1 < n and expr[i+1] == '*':\n                tokens.append('**')\n                i += 2\n            else:\n                tokens.append(c)\n                i += 1\n            continue\n        if c.isdigit():\n            j = i\n            while j < n and expr[j].isdigit():\n                j += 1\n            tokens.append(expr[i:j])\n            i = j\n            continue\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unknown character: {c}\")\n    return tokens\n\ndef parse_expression(tokens: List[str]) -> Tuple[Union[Fraction, 'AST'], List[str]]:\n    return parse_binary_op(tokens, 0)\n\ndef parse_binary_op(tokens: List[str], min_precedence: int) -> Tuple[Union[Fraction, 'AST'], List[str]]:\n    left, tokens = parse_unary_op(tokens)\n\n    while tokens:\n        op = tokens[0]\n        if op in ('+', '-') and min_precedence <= 1:\n            precedence = 1\n        elif op in ('*', '/') and min_precedence <= 2:\n            precedence = 2\n        elif op == '**' and min_precedence <= 3:\n            precedence = 3\n        else:\n            break\n\n        if op == '**':\n            # Right-associative\n            right, tokens = parse_binary_op(tokens[1:], precedence)\n        else:\n            # Left-associative\n            right, tokens = parse_binary_op(tokens[1:], precedence + 1)\n\n        left = ('binary', op, left, right)\n\n    return left, tokens\n\ndef parse_unary_op(tokens: List[str]) -> Tuple[Union[Fraction, 'AST'], List[str]]:\n    if not tokens:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing operand\")\n\n    if tokens[0] in ('+', '-'):\n        op = tokens[0]\n        operand, tokens = parse_unary_op(tokens[1:])\n        return ('unary', op, operand), tokens\n    else:\n        return parse_primary(tokens)\n\ndef parse_primary(tokens: List[str]) -> Tuple[Union[Fraction, 'AST'], List[str]]:\n    if not tokens:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing operand\")\n\n    token = tokens[0]\n    if token == '(':\n        expr, tokens = parse_expression(tokens[1:])\n        if not tokens or tokens[0] != ')':\n            raise ValueError(\"Unbalanced parentheses\")\n        return expr, tokens[1:]\n    elif token.isdigit():\n        return Fraction(int(token)), tokens[1:]\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unexpected token: {token}\")\n\ndef evaluate_ast(node: Union[Fraction, 'AST']) -> Fraction:\n    if isinstance(node, Fraction):\n        return node\n\n    if node[0] == 'unary':\n        op, operand = node[1], evaluate_ast(node[2])\n        if op == '+':\n            return operand\n        elif op == '-':\n            return -operand\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown unary operator: {op}\")\n\n    elif node[0] == 'binary':\n        op, left, right = node[1], evaluate_ast(node[2]), evaluate_ast(node[3])\n        if op == '+':\n            return left + right\n        elif op == '-':\n            return left - right\n        elif op == '*':\n            return left * right\n        elif op == '/':\n            if right == 0:\n                raise ZeroDivisionError(\"division by zero\")\n            return left / right\n        elif op == '**"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-007", "category": "coding", "title": "Glob matching with character classes", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 17675, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1073, "reasoning_tokens": 295, "input_tokens": 308, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3399, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7afeb15b-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd8-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:18-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef glob_match(pattern: str, name: str) -> bool:\n    tokens = []\n    i = 0\n\n    while i < len(pattern):\n        c = pattern[i]\n\n        if c == \"\\\\\":\n            if i + 1 < len(pattern):\n                tokens.append((\"literal\", pattern[i + 1]))\n                i += 2\n            else:\n                tokens.append((\"literal\", \"\\\\\"))\n                i += 1\n\n        elif c == \"*\":\n            if i + 1 < len(pattern) and pattern[i + 1] == \"*\":\n                tokens.append((\"globstar\", None))\n                i += 2\n            else:\n                tokens.append((\"star\", None))\n                i += 1\n\n        elif c == \"?\":\n            tokens.append((\"any\", None))\n            i += 1\n\n        elif c == \"[\":\n            start = i + 1\n            negated = start < len(pattern) and pattern[start] in \"!^\"\n            if negated:\n                start += 1\n\n            # An initial ']' is a member, not the closing delimiter.\n            search_from = start\n            if search_from < len(pattern) and pattern[search_from] == \"]\":\n                search_from += 1\n\n            end = pattern.find(\"]\", search_from)\n            if end == -1:\n                tokens.append((\"literal\", \"[\"))\n                i += 1\n                continue\n\n            members = pattern[start:end]\n            ranges = []\n            left, right = 0, len(members)\n\n            # Boundary hyphens are always literal members.\n            if left < right and members[left] == \"-\":\n                ranges.append((ord(\"-\"), ord(\"-\")))\n                left += 1\n            if left < right and members[right - 1] == \"-\":\n                ranges.append((ord(\"-\"), ord(\"-\")))\n                right -= 1\n\n            while left < right:\n                if left + 2 < right and members[left + 1] == \"-\":\n                    lo = ord(members[left])\n                    hi = ord(members[left + 2])\n                    if lo <= hi:\n                        ranges.append((lo, hi))\n                    left += 3\n                else:\n                    code = ord(members[left])\n                    ranges.append((code, code))\n                    left += 1\n\n            tokens.append((\"set\", (negated, ranges)))\n            i = end + 1\n\n        else:\n            tokens.append((\"literal\", c))\n            i += 1\n\n    # dp[j]: the processed pattern matches exactly name[:j].\n    n = len(name)\n    dp = [False] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = True\n\n    for kind, value in tokens:\n        next_dp = [False] * (n + 1)\n\n        if kind in (\"star\", \"globstar\"):\n            next_dp[0] = dp[0]\n            crosses_slashes = kind == \"globstar\"\n            for j, char in enumerate(name, 1):\n                next_dp[j] = dp[j] or (\n                    next_dp[j - 1] and (crosses_slashes or char != \"/\")\n                )\n\n        else:\n            for j, char in enumerate(name, 1):\n                if not dp[j - 1]:\n                    continue\n\n                if kind == \"literal\":\n                    matches = char == value\n                elif kind == \"any\":\n                    matches = char != \"/\"\n                else:\n                    negated, ranges = value\n                    code = ord(char)\n                    contained = any(lo <= code <= hi for lo, hi in ranges)\n                    matches = char != \"/\" and (contained != negated)\n\n                next_dp[j] = matches\n\n        dp = next_dp\n\n    return dp[n]\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-012", "category": "coding", "title": "Token bucket rate limiter", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 14393, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 815, "reasoning_tokens": 548, "input_tokens": 252, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1125, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7da281a6-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ee-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:20-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\n\ndef token_bucket(\n    capacity: int,\n    refill_per_sec: float,\n    requests: list[tuple[float, int]],\n) -> list[bool]:\n    if capacity < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"capacity must be at least 1\")\n    if refill_per_sec < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"refill_per_sec must be non-negative\")\n\n    # Preserve the exact real values represented by the input floats.\n    rate = Fraction(refill_per_sec)\n    maximum = Fraction(capacity)\n    tokens = maximum\n    previous: Fraction | None = None\n    results: list[bool] = []\n\n    for timestamp, cost in requests:\n        if not isinstance(cost, int) or cost < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"cost must be an integer at least 1\")\n\n        current = Fraction(timestamp)\n        if previous is not None:\n            if current < previous:\n                raise ValueError(\"timestamps must be non-decreasing\")\n            tokens = min(maximum, tokens + (current - previous) * rate)\n        previous = current\n\n        allowed = tokens >= cost\n        if allowed:\n            tokens -= cost\n        results.append(allowed)\n\n    return results\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-009", "category": "coding", "title": "Exact arithmetic expression evaluator", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 9831, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 707, "reasoning_tokens": 111, "input_tokens": 355, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 2616, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7ecdab84-d02b-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ed-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:21-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\n\ndef evaluate(expr: str) -> Fraction:\n    tokens: list[int | str] = []\n    i = 0\n\n    while i < len(expr):\n        ch = expr[i]\n        if ch.isspace():\n            i += 1\n        elif \"0\" <= ch <= \"9\":\n            value = 0\n            while i < len(expr) and \"0\" <= expr[i] <= \"9\":\n                value = value * 10 + ord(expr[i]) - ord(\"0\")\n                i += 1\n            tokens.append(value)\n        elif expr.startswith(\"**\", i):\n            tokens.append(\"**\")\n            i += 2\n        elif ch in \"+-*/()\":\n            tokens.append(ch)\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown character at position {i}: {ch!r}\")\n\n    pos = 0\n\n    def peek() -> int | str | None:\n        return tokens[pos] if pos < len(tokens) else None\n\n    def primary() -> Fraction:\n        nonlocal pos\n        token = peek()\n        if isinstance(token, int):\n            pos += 1\n            return Fraction(token)\n        if token == \"(\":\n            pos += 1\n            value = expression()\n            if peek() != \")\":\n                raise ValueError(\"Missing closing parenthesis\")\n            pos += 1\n            return value\n        raise ValueError(\"Expected an integer or '('\")\n\n    def power() -> Fraction:\n        nonlocal pos\n        base = primary()\n        if peek() == \"**\":\n            pos += 1\n            exponent = unary()\n            if exponent.denominator != 1:\n                raise ValueError(\"Exponent must be an integer\")\n            return base ** exponent.numerator\n        return base\n\n    def unary() -> Fraction:\n        nonlocal pos\n        negative = False\n        while peek() in (\"+\", \"-\"):\n            if peek() == \"-\":\n                negative = not negative\n            pos += 1\n        value = power()\n        return -value if negative else value\n\n    def term() -> Fraction:\n        nonlocal pos\n        value = unary()\n        while peek() in (\"*\", \"/\"):\n            operator = peek()\n            pos += 1\n            right = unary()\n            if operator == \"*\":\n                value *= right\n            else:\n                value /= right\n        return value\n\n    def expression() -> Fraction:\n        nonlocal pos\n        value = term()\n        while peek() in (\"+\", \"-\"):\n            operator = peek()\n            pos += 1\n            right = term()\n            if operator == \"+\":\n                value += right\n            else:\n                value -= right\n        return value\n\n    result = expression()\n    if pos != len(tokens):\n        raise ValueError(\"Unexpected token\")\n    return result\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-011", "category": "coding", "title": "Add business days with holidays", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 18200, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1026, "reasoning_tokens": 776, "input_tokens": 230, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1035, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 15, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 15}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7b9aa383-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dda-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:22-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom datetime import date, timedelta\n\n\ndef add_business_days(start: str, days: int, holidays: list[str]) -> str:\n    def parse_date(value: str) -> date:\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            raise ValueError(\"Dates must be strings in YYYY-MM-DD format\")\n        parsed = date.fromisoformat(value)\n        if parsed.isoformat() != value:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date format: {value!r}; expected YYYY-MM-DD\")\n        return parsed\n\n    current = parse_date(start)\n    holiday_dates = {parse_date(value) for value in holidays}\n\n    def is_business_day(value: date) -> bool:\n        return value.weekday() < 5 and value not in holiday_dates\n\n    if days == 0:\n        while not is_business_day(current):\n            current += timedelta(days=1)\n        return current.isoformat()\n\n    step = timedelta(days=1 if days > 0 else -1)\n    remaining = abs(days)\n\n    while remaining:\n        current += step\n        if is_business_day(current):\n            remaining -= 1\n\n    return current.isoformat()\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-008", "category": "coding", "title": "Subtract IPv4 CIDR blocks", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 23566, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1374, "reasoning_tokens": 962, "input_tokens": 224, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1623, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7a7cfe15-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd9-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:23-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom ipaddress import IPv4Address, IPv4Network, summarize_address_range\n\n\ndef cidr_subtract(base: str, remove: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    pattern = re.compile(\n        r\"(?:0|[1-9][0-9]{0,2})\"\n        r\"(?:\\.(?:0|[1-9][0-9]{0,2})){3}/[0-9]+\"\n    )\n\n    def parse(block: str) -> IPv4Network:\n        if not isinstance(block, str) or pattern.fullmatch(block) is None:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Malformed IPv4 CIDR block: {block!r}\")\n        return IPv4Network(block, strict=True)\n\n    base_network = parse(base)\n    base_start = int(base_network.network_address)\n    base_end = int(base_network.broadcast_address)\n\n    # Validate every removal block, even if earlier ones cover the whole base.\n    intervals: list[tuple[int, int]] = []\n    for block in remove:\n        network = parse(block)\n        start = max(base_start, int(network.network_address))\n        end = min(base_end, int(network.broadcast_address))\n        if start <= end:\n            intervals.append((start, end))\n\n    intervals.sort()\n    result: list[str] = []\n\n    def append_range(start: int, end: int) -> None:\n        result.extend(\n            str(network)\n            for network in summarize_address_range(\n                IPv4Address(start), IPv4Address(end)\n            )\n        )\n\n    cursor = base_start\n    for start, end in intervals:\n        if end < cursor:\n            continue\n        if start > cursor:\n            append_range(cursor, start - 1)\n        cursor = end + 1\n        if cursor > base_end:\n            break\n\n    if cursor <= base_end:\n        append_range(cursor, base_end)\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-010", "category": "coding", "title": "Optimal string alignment distance", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 16655, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 815, "reasoning_tokens": 512, "input_tokens": 155, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1162, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7e74b109-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ec-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:24-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef osa_distance(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the optimal string alignment distance between two strings.\"\"\"\n    if a == b:\n        return 0\n\n    # Keep the shorter string on the columns to minimize memory usage.\n    if len(a) < len(b):\n        a, b = b, a\n\n    n = len(b)\n    if n == 0:\n        return len(a)\n\n    previous = list(range(n + 1))\n    previous_previous = previous\n\n    for i, char_a in enumerate(a, start=1):\n        current = [i] + [0] * n\n\n        for j, char_b in enumerate(b, start=1):\n            current[j] = min(\n                previous[j] + 1,                  # Deletion\n                current[j - 1] + 1,               # Insertion\n                previous[j - 1] + (char_a != char_b),  # Substitution\n            )\n\n            if (\n                i > 1\n                and j > 1\n                and char_a == b[j - 2]\n                and a[i - 2] == char_b\n            ):\n                current[j] = min(\n                    current[j],\n                    previous_previous[j - 2] + 1,  # Adjacent transposition\n                )\n\n        previous_previous, previous = previous, current\n\n    return previous[n]\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-009", "category": "coding", "title": "Exact arithmetic expression evaluator", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 19355, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2975, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 349, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 11753, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7ecd8471-d02b-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ed-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:29-0500", "answer": "I'll write a recursive descent parser for this arithmetic expression evaluator.\n\n```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\ndef evaluate(expr: str) -> Fraction:\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluate an arithmetic expression exactly, returning a Fraction.\n    Supports +, -, *, /, ** with correct precedence and associativity.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Tokenizer\n    tokens = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(expr)\n    while i < n:\n        c = expr[i]\n        if c.isspace():\n            i += 1\n            continue\n        if c.isdigit():\n            j = i\n            while j < n and expr[j].isdigit():\n                j += 1\n            tokens.append(('NUM', int(expr[i:j])))\n            i = j\n        elif c in '+-*/()':\n            if c == '*':\n                if i + 1 < n and expr[i+1] == '*':\n                    tokens.append(('OP', '**'))\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    tokens.append(('OP', '*'))\n                    i += 1\n            else:\n                tokens.append(('OP', c))\n                i += 1\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown character: {c!r}\")\n\n    if not tokens:\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty expression\")\n\n    pos = [0]  # mutable position for nested functions\n\n    def peek():\n        if pos[0] < len(tokens):\n            return tokens[pos[0]]\n        return None\n\n    def advance():\n        tok = tokens[pos[0]]\n        pos[0] += 1\n        return tok\n\n    def expect_op(op):\n        tok = peek()\n        if tok is None or tok[0] != 'OP' or tok[1] != op:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Expected {op!r}\")\n        advance()\n\n    # Grammar (precedence climbing / recursive descent):\n    # expr    := term (('+' | '-') term)*\n    # term    := factor (('*' | '/') factor)*\n    # factor  := unary ('**' factor)?    -- right associative, binds tighter than unary on left\n    # unary   := ('+' | '-')* power\n    # power   := primary ('**' factor)?  -- actually need to handle ** carefully\n    # primary := NUM | '(' expr ')'\n\n    # Let me restructure based on the spec:\n    # Precedence: ** > unary +/- > * / > binary + -\n    # ** is right-associative, binds tighter than unary minus in front\n    # -2 ** 2 = -(2 ** 2) = -4\n    # 2 ** -1 = 2 ** (-1) = 1/2\n\n    # So the structure is:\n    # expr    := term (('+' | '-') term)*\n    # term    := unary (('*' | '/') unary)*\n    # unary   := ('+' | '-') unary | power\n    # power   := primary ('**' unary)?   -- right operand can have unary, and ** is right-assoc\n\n    # Wait, let me check: 2 ** 3 ** 2 = 2 ** (3 ** 2) = 2 ** 9 = 512\n    # So power := primary '**' power | primary, but the right side needs to allow unary\n    # Actually: power := primary ('**' unary)? where unary handles the sign and then power again?\n\n    # Let me think more carefully:\n    # -2 ** 2: unary minus applies to (2 ** 2), so unary := ('+'|'-') unary | power\n    # 2 ** -1: the -1 is part of the right operand of **\n    # 2 ** 3 ** 2: right associative, so 2 ** (3 ** 2)\n\n    # So: power := primary ('**' unary)?\n    # But then 2 ** 3 ** 2: primary=2, then **, then unary which is power which is 3 ** 2\n    # unary := ('+'|'-') unary | power\n    # power := primary ('**' unary)?\n\n    # Check: 2 ** 3 ** 2\n    # power: primary=2, sees **, parses unary\n    #   unary: no sign, so power\n    #     power: primary=3, sees **, parses unary\n    #       unary: no sign, so power\n    #         power: primary=2, no **, returns 2\n    #       returns 2\n    #     3 ** 2 = 9\n    #   returns 9\n    # 2 ** 9 = 512 \u2713\n\n    # Check: -2 ** 2\n    # unary: sees -, parses unary\n    #   unary: no sign, so power\n    #     power: primary=2, sees **, parses unary\n    #       unary: no sign, power: primary=2, returns 2\n    #     2 ** 2 = 4\n    #   returns 4\n    # negate: -4 \u2713\n\n    # Check: 2 ** -1\n    # power: primary=2, sees **, parses unary\n    #   unary: sees -, parses unary\n    #     unary: no sign, power: primary=1, returns 1\n    #   returns -1\n    # 2 ** (-1) = 1/2 \u2713\n\n    def parse_expr():\n        # expr := term (('+' | '-') term)*\n        resu"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-009", "category": "coding", "title": "Exact arithmetic expression evaluator", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 44260, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2305, "reasoning_tokens": 1536, "input_tokens": 355, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3473, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7ecd8473-d02b-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ed-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:21:51-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\n\ndef evaluate(expr: str) -> Fraction:\n    precedence = {\"+\": 1, \"-\": 1, \"*\": 2, \"/\": 2,\n                  \"u+\": 3, \"u-\": 3, \"**\": 4}\n    output: list[Fraction | str] = []\n    operators: list[str] = []\n    expecting_operand = True\n    i = 0\n    n = len(expr)\n\n    # Validate the entire expression and convert it to postfix notation.\n    while i < n:\n        c = expr[i]\n\n        if c.isspace():\n            i += 1\n            continue\n\n        if \"0\" <= c <= \"9\":\n            if not expecting_operand:\n                raise ValueError(\"Expected an operator\")\n\n            # Avoid the interpreter's limit on decimal string-to-int conversion.\n            number = 0\n            while i < n and \"0\" <= expr[i] <= \"9\":\n                number = number * 10 + ord(expr[i]) - ord(\"0\")\n                i += 1\n\n            output.append(Fraction(number))\n            expecting_operand = False\n            continue\n\n        if c == \"(\":\n            if not expecting_operand:\n                raise ValueError(\"Expected an operator before '('\")\n            operators.append(c)\n            i += 1\n            continue\n\n        if c == \")\":\n            if expecting_operand:\n                raise ValueError(\"Missing operand before ')'\")\n\n            while operators and operators[-1] != \"(\":\n                output.append(operators.pop())\n            if not operators:\n                raise ValueError(\"Unmatched ')'\")\n\n            operators.pop()\n            expecting_operand = False\n            i += 1\n            continue\n\n        if c not in \"+-*/\":\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown character: {c!r}\")\n\n        op = c\n        i += 1\n        if c == \"*\" and i < n and expr[i] == \"*\":\n            op = \"**\"\n            i += 1\n\n        if expecting_operand:\n            if op not in (\"+\", \"-\"):\n                raise ValueError(\"Missing operand\")\n            # Prefix operators must not pop a preceding power operator.\n            operators.append(\"u\" + op)\n            continue\n\n        while operators and operators[-1] != \"(\":\n            top = operators[-1]\n            if (precedence[top] > precedence[op]\n                    or (precedence[top] == precedence[op] and op != \"**\")):\n                output.append(operators.pop())\n            else:\n                break\n\n        operators.append(op)\n        expecting_operand = True\n\n    if expecting_operand:\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty expression or missing operand\")\n    if \"(\" in operators:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unmatched '('\")\n\n    output.extend(reversed(operators))\n\n    # Evaluate only after syntax validation has succeeded.\n    values: list[Fraction] = []\n    for token in output:\n        if isinstance(token, Fraction):\n            values.append(token)\n        elif token == \"u+\":\n            continue\n        elif token == \"u-\":\n            values[-1] = -values[-1]\n        else:\n            right = values.pop()\n            left = values.pop()\n\n            if token == \"+\":\n                result = left + right\n            elif token == \"-\":\n                result = left - right\n            elif token == \"*\":\n                result = left * right\n            elif token == \"/\":\n                result = left / right\n            else:  # **\n                if right.denominator != 1:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Exponent must be an integer\")\n                result = left ** right.numerator\n\n            values.append(result)\n\n    return values[0]\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-005", "category": "coding", "title": "Strict CSV line parser", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.9412, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5892, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 570, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 246, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 2664, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.9412, "total": 17, "failures": [{"test": "assert _raises(parse_csv_line, ' \"a\",b')", "line": 23, "error": "AssertionError: "}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 16}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7aefcfbc-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd7-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:22:07-0500", "answer": "Here's the Python function `parse_csv_line` that adheres to the specified strict CSV parsing rules:\n\n```python\ndef parse_csv_line(line: str, delimiter: str = \",\") -> list[str]:\n    if len(delimiter) != 1 or delimiter == '\"':\n        raise ValueError(\"Delimiter must be a single character other than '\\\"'\")\n\n    fields = []\n    current_field = []\n    in_quotes = False\n    i = 0\n    n = len(line)\n\n    while i < n:\n        if not in_quotes:\n            if line[i] == '\"':\n                in_quotes = True\n                i += 1\n                # Check if this is an empty quoted field\n                if i < n and line[i] == '\"':\n                    # Handle empty quoted field or escaped quote\n                    pass\n            elif line[i] == delimiter:\n                fields.append(''.join(current_field))\n                current_field = []\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                if line[i] == '\"':\n                    raise ValueError(\"Unquoted field contains '\\\"'\")\n                current_field.append(line[i])\n                i += 1\n        else:\n            if line[i] == '\"':\n                if i + 1 < n and line[i + 1] == '\"':\n                    current_field.append('\"')\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    in_quotes = False\n                    i += 1\n                    # Check what comes after the closing quote\n                    if i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                        if line[i] == ' ':\n                            raise ValueError(\"Space after closing quote\")\n                        else:\n                            raise ValueError(\"Invalid character after closing quote\")\n                    # If we're at the end, we'll add the field in the next iteration\n            else:\n                current_field.append(line[i])\n                i += 1\n\n    # Add the last field\n    fields.append(''.join(current_field))\n\n    # Handle empty line case\n    if n == 0:\n        return [\"\"]\n\n    # Check for unterminated quoted field\n    if in_quotes:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unterminated quoted field\")\n\n    return fields\n```\n\nThis function:\n1. Validates the delimiter is a single character and not a quote\n2. Processes the line character by character, tracking whether we're in a quoted field\n3. Handles escaped quotes (`\"\"`) within quoted fields\n4. Validates proper closing of quoted fields (must be followed by delimiter or end of line)\n5. Raises ValueError for any invalid CSV format according to the rules\n6. Returns the parsed fields as a list of strings\n\nThe function handles all the specified cases including empty lines, trailing delimiters, and proper quote escaping."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-007", "category": "coding", "title": "Glob matching with character classes", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.85, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6907, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 683, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 299, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3166, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.85, "total": 20, "failures": [{"test": "assert glob_match(\"[]]x\", \"]x\")", "line": 11, "error": "PatternError: unterminated character set at position 1"}, {"test": "assert glob_match(\"[a-]x\", \"-x\")", "line": 12, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert not glob_match(\"a[/]b\", \"a/b\")", "line": 16, "error": "AssertionError: "}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7afeb15a-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd8-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:22:09-0500", "answer": "Here's the Python function `glob_match` that implements the specified glob pattern matching:\n\n```python\nimport re\n\ndef glob_match(pattern: str, name: str) -> bool:\n    def compile_pattern(p: str) -> str:\n        i = 0\n        n = len(p)\n        res = []\n        while i < n:\n            c = p[i]\n            if c == '\\\\':\n                if i + 1 < n:\n                    res.append(re.escape(p[i+1]))\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    res.append(re.escape('\\\\'))\n                    i += 1\n            elif c == '?':\n                res.append('[^/]')\n                i += 1\n            elif c == '*':\n                if i + 1 < n and p[i+1] == '*':\n                    res.append('.*')\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    res.append('[^/]*')\n                    i += 1\n            elif c == '[':\n                j = i + 1\n                if j >= n:\n                    res.append(re.escape('['))\n                    i += 1\n                    continue\n                negate = False\n                if p[j] in '!^':\n                    negate = True\n                    j += 1\n                if j >= n:\n                    res.append(re.escape('['))\n                    i += 1\n                    continue\n                chars = []\n                while j < n and p[j] != ']':\n                    if p[j] == '\\\\':\n                        if j + 1 < n:\n                            chars.append(re.escape(p[j+1]))\n                            j += 2\n                        else:\n                            chars.append(re.escape('\\\\'))\n                            j += 1\n                    elif j + 2 < n and p[j+1] == '-':\n                        start = p[j]\n                        end = p[j+2]\n                        if start > end:\n                            chars.append(re.escape(start + '-' + end))\n                        else:\n                            chars.append(f'{re.escape(start)}-{re.escape(end)}')\n                        j += 3\n                    else:\n                        chars.append(re.escape(p[j]))\n                        j += 1\n                if j >= n:\n                    res.append(re.escape('['))\n                    i += 1\n                else:\n                    if negate:\n                        res.append(f'[^{\"\".join(chars)}]')\n                    else:\n                        res.append(f'[{\"\".join(chars)}]')\n                    i = j + 1\n            else:\n                res.append(re.escape(c))\n                i += 1\n        return '^' + ''.join(res) + '$'\n\n    regex = compile_pattern(pattern)\n    return bool(re.fullmatch(regex, name))\n```\n\nThis function works by:\n1. Converting the glob pattern into a regular expression pattern\n2. Using the `re.fullmatch` function to check if the entire name matches the converted pattern\n\nThe conversion handles all the specified glob syntax:\n- `?` becomes `[^/]`\n- `*` becomes `[^/]*`\n- `**` becomes `.*`\n- `[...]` sets are properly converted with all their special cases\n- Backslashes are handled for escaping\n- All other characters are treated literally\n\nThe function is case-sensitive as required."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-011", "category": "coding", "title": "Add business days with holidays", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 65381, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 8399, "reasoning_tokens": 8027, "input_tokens": 228, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1453, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 32779, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 15, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 15}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7b9aa382-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dda-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:22:09-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom datetime import date, datetime, timedelta\n\n_DATE_RE = re.compile(r\"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}\")\n\n\ndef _parse_date(value: str) -> date:\n    if not isinstance(value, str) or not _DATE_RE.fullmatch(value):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date: {value!r}\")\n    try:\n        return datetime.strptime(value, \"%Y-%m-%d\").date()\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date: {value!r}\") from exc\n\n\ndef add_business_days(start: str, days: int, holidays: list[str]) -> str:\n    start_date = _parse_date(start)\n    holiday_set = {_parse_date(h) for h in holidays}\n\n    def is_business_day(d: date) -> bool:\n        return d.weekday() < 5 and d not in holiday_set\n\n    if days > 0:\n        current = start_date\n        remaining = days\n        while remaining > 0:\n            current += timedelta(days=1)\n            if is_business_day(current):\n                remaining -= 1\n        return current.isoformat()\n\n    if days < 0:\n        current = start_date\n        remaining = -days\n        while remaining > 0:\n            current -= timedelta(days=1)\n            if is_business_day(current):\n                remaining -= 1\n        return current.isoformat()\n\n    # days == 0\n    if is_business_day(start_date):\n        return start_date.isoformat()\n\n    current = start_date\n    while True:\n        current += timedelta(days=1)\n        if is_business_day(current):\n            return current.isoformat()\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-007", "category": "coding", "title": "Glob matching with character classes", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 75001, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 3623, "reasoning_tokens": 2925, "input_tokens": 308, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3016, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7afeb15e-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd8-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:22:15-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef glob_match(pattern: str, name: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return whether the entire name matches the case-sensitive glob.\"\"\"\n    n = len(name)\n    m = len(pattern)\n    reachable = bytearray(n + 1)\n    reachable[0] = 1\n    last_close = pattern.rfind(\"]\")\n    i = 0\n\n    while i < m:\n        char = pattern[i]\n        i += 1\n\n        if char == \"*\":\n            # Any uninterrupted run of at least two stars is equivalent to **.\n            crosses_slashes = i < m and pattern[i] == \"*\"\n            while i < m and pattern[i] == \"*\":\n                i += 1\n\n            for j in range(1, n + 1):\n                reachable[j] = reachable[j] or (\n                    reachable[j - 1]\n                    and (crosses_slashes or name[j - 1] != \"/\")\n                )\n            continue\n\n        kind = \"literal\"\n        intervals: list[tuple[int, int]] = []\n        negated = False\n\n        if char == \"\\\\\":\n            if i < m:\n                char = pattern[i]\n                i += 1\n        elif char == \"?\":\n            kind = \"any\"\n        elif char == \"[\":\n            start = i\n            if start < m and pattern[start] in \"!^\":\n                negated = True\n                start += 1\n\n            # An initial ] is a member, not the closing delimiter.\n            search_from = start\n            if search_from < m and pattern[search_from] == \"]\":\n                search_from += 1\n\n            end = (\n                pattern.find(\"]\", search_from)\n                if search_from <= last_close\n                else -1\n            )\n\n            if end != -1:\n                kind = \"class\"\n                k = start\n                while k < end:\n                    if k + 2 < end and pattern[k + 1] == \"-\":\n                        low = ord(pattern[k])\n                        high = ord(pattern[k + 2])\n                        if low <= high:\n                            intervals.append((low, high))\n                        k += 3\n                    else:\n                        code = ord(pattern[k])\n                        intervals.append((code, code))\n                        k += 1\n                i = end + 1\n            # Otherwise only the opening [ is consumed, as a literal.\n\n        # A non-star token consumes exactly one character. Work backwards\n        # so reachable[j - 1] still belongs to the previous pattern prefix.\n        for j in range(n, 0, -1):\n            if not reachable[j - 1]:\n                reachable[j] = 0\n                continue\n\n            current = name[j - 1]\n            if kind == \"literal\":\n                matched = current == char\n            elif kind == \"any\":\n                matched = current != \"/\"\n            elif current == \"/\":\n                matched = False\n            else:\n                code = ord(current)\n                contained = any(low <= code <= high for low, high in intervals)\n                matched = contained != negated\n\n            reachable[j] = matched\n\n        reachable[0] = 0\n\n    return bool(reachable[n])\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-005", "category": "coding", "title": "Strict CSV line parser", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 94142, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 16164, "reasoning_tokens": 15826, "input_tokens": 244, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1570, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 58810, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7aefa8aa-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd7-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:22:36-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef parse_csv_line(line: str, delimiter: str = \",\") -> list[str]:\n    if len(delimiter) != 1 or delimiter == '\"':\n        raise ValueError(\"delimiter must be a single character other than '\\\"'\")\n\n    fields: list[str] = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(line)\n\n    while True:\n        if i < n and line[i] == '\"':\n            i += 1\n            buf: list[str] = []\n            closed = False\n\n            while i < n:\n                c = line[i]\n                if c == '\"':\n                    if i + 1 < n and line[i + 1] == '\"':\n                        buf.append('\"')\n                        i += 2\n                    else:\n                        i += 1\n                        closed = True\n                        break\n                else:\n                    buf.append(c)\n                    i += 1\n\n            if not closed:\n                raise ValueError(\"unterminated quoted field\")\n\n            if i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                raise ValueError(\"unexpected character after closing quote\")\n\n            fields.append(\"\".join(buf))\n\n            if i < n:\n                i += 1\n                continue\n            else:\n                break\n        else:\n            start = i\n            while i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                if line[i] == '\"':\n                    raise ValueError(\"unquoted field contains a quote\")\n                i += 1\n\n            fields.append(line[start:i])\n\n            if i < n:\n                i += 1\n                continue\n            else:\n                break\n\n    return fields\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-008", "category": "coding", "title": "Subtract IPv4 CIDR blocks", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.3529, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3532, "turns": 1, "retries": 3, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 283, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 227, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1203, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.3529, "total": 17, "failures": [{"test": "assert cidr_subtract(\"10.0.0.0/24\", [\"10.0.0.0/25\"]) == [\"10.0.0.128/25\"]", "line": 11, "error": "AttributeError: 'IPv4Network' object has no attribute 'is_disjoint'"}, {"test": "assert cidr_subtract(\"10.0.0.0/24\", [\"10.0.0.0/24\"]) == []", "line": 12, "error": "AttributeError: 'IPv4Network' object has no attribute 'is_disjoint'"}, {"test": "assert cidr_subtract(\"10.0.0.0/24\", [\"10.0.0.0/16\"]) == []", "line": 13, "error": "AttributeError: 'IPv4Network' object has no attribute 'is_disjoint'"}, {"test": "assert cidr_subtract(\"10.0.0.0/24\", [\"10.0.0.64/26\"]) == [\"10.0.0.0/26\", \"10.0.0.128/25\"]", "line": 14, "error": "AttributeError: 'IPv4Network' object has no attribute 'is_disjoint'"}, {"test": "assert cidr_subtract(\"10.0.0.0/30\", [\"10.0.0.1/32\"]) == [\"10.0.0.0/32\", \"10.0.0.2/31\"]", "line": 15, "error": "AttributeError: 'IPv4Network' object has no attribute 'is_disjoint'"}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 6}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7a7cfe16-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd9-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:23:23-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport ipaddress\n\ndef cidr_subtract(base: str, remove: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    try:\n        base_net = ipaddress.IPv4Network(base, strict=True)\n    except ValueError as e:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid base CIDR block: {e}\")\n\n    remove_nets = []\n    for cidr in remove:\n        try:\n            net = ipaddress.IPv4Network(cidr, strict=True)\n        except ValueError as e:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid remove CIDR block '{cidr}': {e}\")\n        remove_nets.append(net)\n\n    # Start with the base network\n    remaining = [base_net]\n\n    for net in remove_nets:\n        new_remaining = []\n        for current in remaining:\n            # If current is completely outside net, keep it as is\n            if current.is_disjoint(net):\n                new_remaining.append(current)\n            else:\n                # Otherwise, subtract net from current\n                new_remaining.extend(current.address_exclude(net))\n        remaining = new_remaining\n        if not remaining:\n            return []\n\n    # Convert to strings and sort by network address\n    result = [str(net) for net in sorted(remaining, key=lambda n: (n.network_address, n.prefixlen))]\n    return result\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-008", "category": "coding", "title": "Subtract IPv4 CIDR blocks", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 183444, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 32000, "reasoning_tokens": 31999, "input_tokens": 221, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 0, "finish_reason": "length", "thinking_chars": 104370, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "total": 17, "pass": false, "passed": 0, "error": "no code block found"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7a7d2527-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a590dd9-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:24:03-0500", "answer": ""}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "coding-010", "category": "coding", "title": "Optimal string alignment distance", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 177274, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 27167, "reasoning_tokens": 26862, "input_tokens": 152, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 846, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 77099, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7e74d81b-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7a5934ec-d02b-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:24:07-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef osa_distance(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the optimal string alignment (restricted Damerau-Levenshtein) distance.\"\"\"\n    m, n = len(a), len(b)\n    d = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(m + 1)]\n\n    for i in range(m + 1):\n        d[i][0] = i\n    for j in range(n + 1):\n        d[0][j] = j\n\n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        ai = a[i - 1]\n        for j in range(1, n + 1):\n            cost = 0 if ai == b[j - 1] else 1\n            best = min(\n                d[i - 1][j] + 1,      # deletion\n                d[i][j - 1] + 1,      # insertion\n                d[i - 1][j - 1] + cost  # substitution/match\n            )\n\n            if i > 1 and j > 1 and a[i - 2] == b[j - 1] and ai == b[j - 2]:\n                best = min(best, d[i - 2][j - 2] + 1)  # adjacent transposition\n\n            d[i][j] = best\n\n    return d[m][n]\n```"}
