{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "agentic-012", "category": "agentic", "title": "Route support tickets by tier and priority", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6832, "turns": 4, "retries": null, "usage": {"search_calls": 0, "output_tokens": 520, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3247, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 984}, "answer_chars": 744, "finish_reason": null, "thinking_chars": null, "detail": {"final_include_failed": [], "missing_required": [], "pass": true, "forbidden_made": [], "within_max_turns": true, "final_exclude_failed": []}, "workflow_id": "0sfjee7eb719-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9e7d5a-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:30-0500", "answer": "All three tickets have been routed. Here's the summary:\n\n| Ticket | Customer | Tier | Priority | Queue | TAM Paged |\n|--------|----------|------|----------|-------|-----------|\n| T-5501 | Acme Freight | Enterprise | P1 | **tier2-escalations** | \u2705 r.singh (page PG-41120) |\n| T-5502 | Globex Retail | Business | P1 | **tier2** | \u2014 (not Enterprise, no page) |\n| T-5503 | Initech | Enterprise | P3 | **tier1** | \u2014 (P3, no page) |\n\n- **T-5501** (SSO login failing for all users) went to tier2-escalations, and Acme Freight's TAM **r.singh** was paged.\n- **T-5502** (Order sync API 500s) went to tier2 \u2014 P1 but Business tier, so no escalation page.\n- **T-5503** (CSV export question) went to tier1 \u2014 P3 tickets always go to tier1 regardless of tier."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "agentic-010", "category": "agentic", "title": "Roll firmware out only to eligible thermostats", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6553, "turns": 3, "retries": null, "usage": {"search_calls": 0, "output_tokens": 846, "reasoning_tokens": 315, "input_tokens": 2328, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 995, "finish_reason": null, "thinking_chars": null, "detail": {"final_include_failed": [], "missing_required": [], "pass": true, "forbidden_made": [], "within_max_turns": true, "final_exclude_failed": []}, "workflow_id": "0sfjee6a31eb-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9e5648-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:31-0500", "answer": "Rollout complete. Summary:\n\n**Scheduled for firmware 4.2.0 (during next maintenance window):**\n- **TH-101** (thermostat, hw rev C, 78% battery, 4.1.2 \u2192 4.2.0) \u2014 job `fw-6001`\n- **TH-106** (thermostat, hw rev D, 44% battery, 4.0.0 \u2192 4.2.0) \u2014 job `fw-6002`\n\n**Skipped, with reasons:**\n- **TH-102** \u2014 hardware revision B is not compatible (4.2.0 requires rev C or D)\n- **TH-103** \u2014 battery 35% is below the 40% minimum, and current firmware 4.1.0 is below the 4.0.0 minimum required... actually 4.1.0 > 4.0.0, so the blocker is the low battery (35% < 40%)\n- **TH-104** \u2014 under maintenance lock (even though it otherwise qualifies)\n- **TH-105** \u2014 current firmware 3.9.8 is below the minimum 4.0.0 required for upgrade\n- **GW-01** \u2014 gateway, not a thermostat; 4.2.0 targets thermostats only\n- **SN-201** \u2014 sensor, not a thermostat; 4.2.0 targets thermostats only\n\nNote: TH-104 can be upgraded once its maintenance lock is lifted, and TH-103 should be scheduled after its battery is charged above 40%."}
