{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-002", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 9143, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 2, "output_tokens": 206, "reasoning_tokens": 88, "input_tokens": 13250, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 4497}, "answer_chars": 513, "finish_reason": "completed", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 1, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics (light-gated ion channels)", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; light-gated ion channels and optogenetics"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjefeccb7c-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9ecb7e-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:34-0500", "answer": "The **2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine** was awarded jointly to **Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, and Georg Nagel** for discoveries concerning **light-gated ion channels and optogenetics**. Optogenetics enables researchers to control nerve-cell activity using light, helping reveal how the brain works. ([elsevier.com](https://www.elsevier.com/connect/honoring-the-2026-nobel-laureates?utm_source=openai))\n\nANSWER: Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; light-gated ion channels and optogenetics"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-002", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 12061, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 3, "output_tokens": 462, "reasoning_tokens": 326, "input_tokens": 18149, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 4497}, "answer_chars": 632, "finish_reason": "completed", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 2, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics (light-gated ion channels)", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; light-gated ion channels and optogenetics"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjefecf290-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9ecb7e-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:37-0500", "answer": "The **2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine** was awarded jointly to **Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, and Georg Nagel**. ([nsf.gov](https://www.nsf.gov/science-matters/nsf-supported-researchers-honored-2026-nobel-prizes))\n\nThe prize recognized their discoveries concerning **light-gated ion channels and optogenetics**\u2014a technique that uses light-sensitive proteins to control nerve-cell activity and investigate brain function. ([lindau-nobel.org](https://www.lindau-nobel.org/news-nobel-prize-in-physiology-or-medicine-2026/))\n\nANSWER: Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; light-gated ion channels and optogenetics"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-001", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physics", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 16747, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 604, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 802, "search_tokens": 31259, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1734, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 5, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjedddb23f-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9e7d5b-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:38-0500", "answer": "Based on my web search, I found clear and consistent information from the official Nobel Prize website and multiple news sources.\n\n**The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physics** was awarded to **Francis Halzen** (University of Wisconsin\u2013Madison, USA) on October 6, 2026. The official citation reads: *\"for decisive contributions to the IceCube Neutrino Observatory and the discovery of high-energy neutrinos of astrophysical origin.\"*\n\nThe prize citation is built around the **IceCube Neutrino Observatory** \u2014 a cubic kilometre of Antarctic ice at the South Pole equipped with light sensors, which Halzen first proposed in 1988 and which was completed in 2011. The observatory detects high-energy neutrinos from distant cosmic sources, opening a new window on the universe.\n\n**Sources cited:**\n- NobelPrize.org \u2014 Official press release: \"Press release: Nobel Prize in Physics 2026\" (https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/physics/2026/press-release/)\n- NobelPrize.org \u2014 Popular information page (https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/physics/2026/popular-information/)\n- BBC News \u2014 \"'Ghost particles' from space telescope wins 2026 Nobel Prize in Physics\" (https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cq203mymlvkeo)\n- Nature \u2014 \"Nobel physics prize awarded for detection of cosmic neutrinos\" (https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03092-1)\n- IceCube/University of Wisconsin\u2013Madison \u2014 \"Francis Halzen, IceCube principal investigator, wins 2026 Physics Nobel Prize\" (https://icecube.wisc.edu/news/awards/2026/10/francis-halzen-icecube-principal-investigator-wins-2026-physics-nobel-prize/)\n- Scientific American \u2014 \"2026 Nobel Prize in Physics awarded to Francis Halzen for discovery of high-energy neutrinos\"\n\nANSWER: Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-002", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 13308, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 605, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 807, "search_tokens": 24478, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1599, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 3, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics (light-gated ion channels)", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjefeccb7e-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9ecb7e-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:39-0500", "answer": "The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine was announced on 5 October 2026 by the Nobel Assembly at Karolinska Institutet. It was awarded jointly to three laureates, each receiving one-third of the prize:\n\n- **Karl Deisseroth** \u2014 Howard Hughes Medical Institute and Stanford University, USA\n- **Peter Hegemann** \u2014 Humboldt University of Berlin, Germany\n- **Georg Nagel** \u2014 University of W\u00fcrzburg, Germany\n\nThe prize recognized **\u201ctheir discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics.\u201d** In essence, Hegemann and Nagel discovered the light-sensitive protein channelrhodopsin in the single-celled alga *Chlamydomonas*, and Deisseroth adapted it into a light-controlled switch that lets researchers turn individual nerve cells on or off in the living brain \u2014 the technique known as optogenetics, which has transformed neuroscience and opened new avenues for studying and potentially treating neurological and psychiatric disorders [1][2][3].\n\n**Sources:**\n1. NobelPrize.org \u2014 Press release: The Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine 2026 (5 October 2026): https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/press-release/\n2. NobelPrize.org \u2014 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine 2026 summary: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/summary/\n3. Chemical & Engineering News (C&EN) \u2014 \u201cOptogenetics researchers win Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine\u201d (5 October 2026): https://cen.acs.org/people/nobel-prize/nobel-2026-physiology-medicine/104/web/2026/10\n\nANSWER: Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-003", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Literature and Peace laureates", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 12886, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 1385, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 802, "search_tokens": 15843, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1853, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 3115, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 8, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjeff2aff3-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9ea46d-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:40-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the 2026 Nobel Prize laureates in Literature and Peace.The search results are consistent across multiple sources. Let me verify directly against the official Nobel Prize press releases.Both laureates are confirmed by the official Nobel Prize press releases, with consistent reporting across multiple outlets.\n\n**2026 Nobel Prize in Literature \u2014 Anne Carson**\nThe Swedish Academy announced on **8 October 2026** that the prize goes to the Canadian author **Anne Carson**, \u201cfor her bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature.\u201d [NobelPrize.org \u2014 Literature 2026 press release](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/literature/2026/press-release/); corroborated by [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Nobel_Prize_in_Literature) and [Britannica\u2019s 2026 winners list](https://www.britannica.com/topic/2026-Nobel-Prize-winners).\n\n**2026 Nobel Peace Prize \u2014 Navi Pillay**\nThe Norwegian Nobel Committee announced on **9 October 2026** that the prize goes to South African jurist **Navanethem \u201cNavi\u201d Pillay**, \u201cfor her efforts to promote peace and international law,\u201d recognizing her career defending human rights and advancing international justice (ICTY/ICTR/ICC, UN High Commissioner for Human Rights, and the ICJ Myanmar genocide case). [NobelPrize.org \u2014 Peace 2026 press release](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/2026/press-release/); corroborated by [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Nobel_Peace_Prize), [Al Jazeera](https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/9/who-is-navi-pillay-winner-of-the-2026-nobel-peace-prize), [PBS/AP](https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-live-winner-of-the-2026-nobel-peace-prize-is), and [UN News](https://news.un.org/en/story/2026/10/1168558).\n\nANSWER: Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-003", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Literature and Peace laureates", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 16018, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 3, "output_tokens": 487, "reasoning_tokens": 344, "input_tokens": 29635, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 4494}, "answer_chars": 645, "finish_reason": "completed", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 2, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navanethem \u201cNavi\u201d Pillay"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjeff2d707-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9ea46d-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:42-0500", "answer": "- **2026 Nobel Prize in Literature: Anne Carson**, the Canadian poet and writer. The award was announced on **October 8, 2026**. ([investing.com](https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/canadian-writer-anne-carson-wins-2026-nobel-prize-in-literature-4938559))\n- **2026 Nobel Peace Prize: Navanethem \u201cNavi\u201d Pillay**, the former UN High Commissioner for Human Rights. Announced on **October 9, 2026**, the prize recognized her efforts to promote peace and international law. ([nobelpeaceprize.org](https://www.nobelpeaceprize.org/press/press-releases/nobel-peace-prize-for-2026))\n\nANSWER: Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navanethem \u201cNavi\u201d Pillay"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-003", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Literature and Peace laureates", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 17065, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 5, "output_tokens": 1082, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 802, "search_tokens": 27866, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 2521, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 9, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navanethem \"Navi\" Pillay"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjeff2aff4-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9ea46d-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:42-0500", "answer": "Based on my web searches, here are the 2026 Nobel Prize winners:\n\n**2026 Nobel Prize in Literature: Anne Carson**\nThe Canadian poet, essayist, classicist, and translator Anne Carson was awarded the 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature on October 8, 2026, \"for her bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature\" [NobelPrize.org](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/literature/2026/press-release/) [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Nobel_Prize_in_Literature) [Al Jazeera](https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/8/canadian-anne-carson-wins-2026-nobel-prize-in-literature) [Britannica](https://www.britannica.com/topic/2026-Nobel-Prize-winners).\n\n**2026 Nobel Peace Prize: Navanethem \"Navi\" Pillay**\nThe South African-born jurist and former UN High Commissioner for Human Rights, Navanethem \"Navi\" Pillay, was awarded the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize on October 9, 2026, \"for her efforts to promote peace and international law\" [NobelPrize.org](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/2026/press-release/) [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Nobel_Peace_Prize) [Al Jazeera](https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/9/2026-nobel-peace-prize-awarded-to-navi-pillay) [PBS/AP](https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-live-winner-of-the-2026-nobel-peace-prize-is) [BBC](https://www.bbc.com/news/live/ck5yng9zz8pyt).\n\n**Sources cited:**\n- NobelPrize.org (official): [Literature 2026 Press Release](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/literature/2026/press-release/), [Peace 2026 Press Release](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/2026/press-release/)\n- Wikipedia: [2026 Nobel Prize in Literature](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Nobel_Prize_in_Literature), [2026 Nobel Peace Prize](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Nobel_Peace_Prize)\n- Al Jazeera: [Anne Carson wins 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature](https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/8/canadian-anne-carson-wins-2026-nobel-prize-in-literature), [2026 Nobel Peace Prize awarded to Navi Pillay](https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/9/2026-nobel-peace-prize-awarded-to-navi-pillay)\n- Britannica: [2026 Nobel Prize winners](https://www.britannica.com/topic/2026-Nobel-Prize-winners)\n- PBS News/AP: [Navi Pillay wins Nobel Peace Prize](https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-live-winner-of-the-2026-nobel-peace-prize-is)\n- BBC News: [Nobel Peace Prize live coverage](https://www.bbc.com/news/live/ck5yng9zz8pyt)\n\nANSWER: Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navanethem \"Navi\" Pillay"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-004", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 US Open men's singles final", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 18735, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 744, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 805, "search_tokens": 33548, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1697, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 7, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjef6016a4-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9ea46c-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:43-0500", "answer": "Alexander Zverev won the men's singles title at the 2026 US Open, defeating American Ben Shelton in the final 6\u20133, 7\u20136(7\u20132), 5\u20137, 6\u20132 on Sunday, September 13, 2026, at Arthur Ashe Stadium in New York. It was Zverev's second Grand Slam title of 2026 (after the French Open) and his first US Open title \u2014 the first German man to win the US Open since Boris Becker in 1989. Shelton, playing in his first major final, had earlier upset defending champion Carlos Alcaraz in the quarterfinals.\n\nSources:\n- US Open official site: \"Alexander Zverev defeats Ben Shelton to win 2026 US Open\" \u2014 https://www.usopen.org/en_US/news/articles/2026-09-13/alexander_zverev_defeats_ben_shelton_to_win_2026_us_open.html\n- US Open official draw (PDF): \"US Open 2026 Men's Singles Champion: ZVEREV, Alexander GER \u2014 6-3 | 7-6(2) | 5-7 | 6-2\" \u2014 https://www.usopen.org/en_US/scores/draws/2026_MS_draw.pdf\n- ATP Tour: \"What were the US Open results?\" \u2014 https://www.atptour.com/en/news/us-open-2026-results\n- ESPN: \"Zverev dashes American hopes, beats Shelton in US Open final for 2nd major\" \u2014 https://www.espn.com/tennis/story/_/id/49933388/alexander-zverev-beats-ben-shelton-4-sets-win-2026-us-open\n- BBC Sport: \"US Open 2026 results: Alexander Zverev beats Ben Shelton for second Grand Slam title\" \u2014 https://www.bbc.com/sport/tennis/articles/c1wx9qpxjg3o\n- Associated Press: \"Alexander Zverev beats Ben Shelton to win the US Open title and extend a drought by American men\" \u2014 https://apnews.com/article/us-open-mens-final-shelton-zverev-58fc12d28293dd33806e4d07242681d1\n- Wikipedia: \"2026 US Open \u2013 Men's singles\" \u2014 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_US_Open_%E2%80%93_Men's_singles\n\nANSWER: Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-002", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 22547, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 1401, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 807, "search_tokens": 16148, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 2795, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2475, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 6, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics (light-gated ion channels)", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjefeccb7d-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9ecb7e-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:49-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine laureates.The search results are clear, but let me verify against the official Nobel Prize press release to confirm the exact citation.The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine was announced on **5 October 2026** by the Nobel Assembly at Karolinska Institutet. It was awarded jointly to three laureates, each receiving a 1/3 share of the 12 million SEK prize:\n\n**Laureates**\n1. **Karl Deisseroth** \u2014 Howard Hughes Medical Institute and Stanford University, USA (D.H. Chen Professor of Bioengineering and of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences)\n2. **Peter Hegemann** \u2014 Humboldt University of Berlin, Germany (Hertie Senior Professor of Neuroscience; the prize-winning discoveries were made at the Max Planck Institute for Biochemistry, Martinsried)\n3. **Georg Nagel** \u2014 University of W\u00fcrzburg, Germany (Professor of Molecular Plant Physiology; the prize-winning discoveries were made at the Max Planck Institute for Biophysics, Frankfurt)\n\n**Research area recognized**\nThe prize was awarded *\"for their discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics.\"* Hegemann and Nagel discovered the protein **channelrhodopsin** in the single-celled alga *Chlamydomonas*, which opens an ion channel when illuminated by blue light. Deisseroth then introduced the channelrhodopsin gene into rat nerve cells (2005) and made the light-controlled switch work in the brains of living mice (2007), creating the technique now known as **optogenetics** \u2014 a method to control and map nerve-cell activity with light that has laid the foundation of a new era in neuroscience, with applications ranging from mapping circuits behind memories and behaviors to clinical attempts to restore sight.\n\n**Sources**\n- NobelPrize.org \u2014 official press release, 5 October 2026: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/press-release/\n- NobelPrize.org \u2014 prize summary page: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/summary/\n- C&EN (Chemical & Engineering News), \"Optogenetics researchers win Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine,\" 5 Oct 2026: https://cen.acs.org/people/nobel-prize/nobel-2026-physiology-medicine/104/web/2026/10\n- TIME, \"Meet the 2026 Nobel Prize Winners,\" 5 Oct 2026: https://time.com/article/2026/10/05/nobel-prize-2026-winners/\n- The Independent, \"Winners of the 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine \u2013 revealed\": https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/news/nobel-prize-neuroscience-karl-deisseroth-hegemann-nagel-b3061929.html\n- SPIE, \"Optogenetics wins the 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine\": https://spie.org/news/optogenetics-wins-the-2026-nobel-prize-in-physiology-or-medicine\n\nANSWER: Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-004", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 US Open men's singles final", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 28363, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 5, "output_tokens": 1863, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 805, "search_tokens": 27208, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 2253, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 3128, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 5, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjef6016a5-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjed9ea46c-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:31:53-0500", "answer": "**Alexander Zverev** won the men's singles title at the 2026 US Open, defeating American **Ben Shelton** in the final on Sunday, September 13, 2026, with a score of **6\u20133, 7\u20136(7\u20132), 5\u20137, 6\u20132** [search-result://CW98vzT1,search-result://HudOpRhU,search-result://1oC2JZMW,search-result://y5SKJjRz,search-result://AYFjOCeM].\n\nKey details:\n- The final was played on Sunday, September 13, 2026, at the USTA Billie Jean King National Tennis Center in Flushing Meadows, New York [search-result://HudOpRhU,search-result://nI9Oy9Eb,search-result://DuRx7Xwq].\n- It was Zverev's second Grand Slam title and second major of 2026 (following his French Open win in June), making him the fourth man in the Open Era to win his first two majors in the same year [search-result://CW98vzT1,search-result://1oC2JZMW,search-result://y5SKJjRz].\n- It was the first US Open men's singles title won by a German since Boris Becker in 1989 [search-result://CW98vzT1,search-result://HudOpRhU].\n- Shelton was playing in his first major final, and was vying to become the first American man to win a Grand Slam since Andy Roddick in 2003 [search-result://HudOpRhU,search-result://DuRx7Xwq].\n- Defending champion Carlos Alcaraz lost in the quarterfinals to Shelton [search-result://CW98vzT1,search-result://y5SKJjRz].\n\n**Sources:**\n1. Official US Open website \u2014 \"Alexander Zverev defeats Ben Shelton to win 2026 US Open\" (Sept 13, 2026): https://www.usopen.org/en_US/news/articles/2026-09-13/alexander_zverev_defeats_ben_shelton_to_win_2026_us_open.html [search-result://AYFjOCeM]\n2. Wikipedia \u2014 \"2026 US Open \u2013 Men's singles\": https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_US_Open_%E2%80%93_Men%27s_singles [search-result://CW98vzT1,search-result://1oC2JZMW,search-result://y5SKJjRz]\n3. Wikipedia \u2014 \"2026 US Open (tennis)\": https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_US_Open_(tennis) [search-result://HudOpRhU,search-result://TgJpFi7G]\n4. Topend Sports \u2014 \"US Open Men's Singles Winners - Complete List From 1881\": https://www.topendsports.com/events/tennis-grand-slam/us-open/winners-men.htm [search-result://9F0ECsH3]\n5. US Open Tennis Info \u2014 \"US Open Tennis 2026 Results\": https://usopentennisinfo.com/results/ [search-result://nI9Oy9Eb,search-result://61USijx6]\n\nANSWER: Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton"}
