{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-010", "category": "grounding", "title": "Vega-C flight VV30 payloads", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5104, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 1, "output_tokens": 125, "reasoning_tokens": 33, "input_tokens": 12740, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 4489}, "answer_chars": 357, "finish_reason": "completed", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 1, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer); Copernicus Sentinel-3C", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "FLEX; Copernicus Sentinel-3C"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj19af902f-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3792e-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:43-0500", "answer": "Vega-C flight VV30 launched **FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)** and **Copernicus Sentinel-3C**. ESA\u2019s launch record identifies both satellites, and CNES independently confirms their successful deployment on September 14\u201315, 2026. ([esa.int](https://www.esa.int/ESA_Multimedia/Images/2026/09/Vega-C_VV30?utm_source=openai))\n\nANSWER: FLEX; Copernicus Sentinel-3C"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-011", "category": "grounding", "title": "US 2025 median household income and poverty rate", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 11188, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 506, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 822, "search_tokens": 23381, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1001, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 3, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "$87,460; 10.2%", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "$87,460; 10.2%"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj18146ec0-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3792f-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:44-0500", "answer": "According to the U.S. Census Bureau's September 15, 2026 release of the 2025 income and poverty data (based on the 2026 Current Population Survey Annual Social and Economic Supplement):\n\n- **Real median household income in 2025:** $87,460 \u2014 up 2.6% from the 2024 estimate of $85,210, and the highest on record dating back to 1967.\n- **Official poverty rate in 2025:** 10.2% \u2014 down 0.5 percentage points from 2024, with 34.5 million people in poverty.\n\nSources:\n1. U.S. Census Bureau press release, \"Income, Poverty and Health Insurance Coverage in the United States: 2025\" (Sept. 15, 2026): https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/income-poverty-health-insurance-coverage.html\n2. U.S. Census Bureau report, \"Income in the United States: 2025\" (P60-289): https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-289.html\n3. U.S. Census Bureau report, \"Poverty in the United States: 2025\" (P60-290): https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-290.html\n\nANSWER: $87,460; 10.2%"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-010", "category": "grounding", "title": "Vega-C flight VV30 payloads", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 7763, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 2, "output_tokens": 205, "reasoning_tokens": 88, "input_tokens": 15450, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 4489}, "answer_chars": 413, "finish_reason": "completed", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 1, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer); Copernicus Sentinel-3C", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Copernicus Sentinel-3C; FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj19af691c-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3792e-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:45-0500", "answer": "Vega-C flight VV30 launched **Copernicus Sentinel-3C** and **FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)**. Both ESA\u2019s launch record and CNES\u2019s Guiana Space Centre report confirm the two payloads. Liftoff occurred on September 15, 2026, European time (September 14 locally in French Guiana). ([esa.int](https://www.esa.int/ESA_Multimedia/Images/2026/09/Vega-C_VV30))\n\nANSWER: Copernicus Sentinel-3C; FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-011", "category": "grounding", "title": "US 2025 median household income and poverty rate", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 13625, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 1294, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 822, "search_tokens": 17552, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 2109, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1980, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 4, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "$87,460; 10.2%", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "$87,460; 10.2%"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj18146ec1-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3792f-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:46-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the U.S. Census Bureau's September 2026 income and poverty report.The search results are consistent. Let me verify by opening the official Census Bureau press release directly.I've verified the figures directly from the official U.S. Census Bureau sources. Here's the summary:\n\n## Findings from the September 2026 Census Bureau Report\n\nOn **September 15, 2026**, the U.S. Census Bureau released its annual income and poverty data (press release CB26-151), based on the 2026 Current Population Survey Annual Social and Economic Supplement (CPS ASEC), which covers calendar year 2025. The findings come from three reports: *\"Income in the United States: 2025\"* (P60-289), *\"Poverty in the United States: 2025\"* (P60-290), and *\"Health Insurance Coverage in the United States: 2025.\"*\n\n**Key figures for 2025:**\n\n- **Real median household income: $87,460** \u2014 the highest on record dating back to 1967, an increase of 2.6% from the 2024 estimate of $85,210.\n- **Official poverty rate: 10.2%** \u2014 a decline of 0.5 percentage points from 2024, with 34.5 million people in poverty. (The child poverty rate fell to a historic low of 13.4%, and the Hispanic poverty rate fell to a historic low of 13.9%.)\n- For context, the Supplemental Poverty Measure (SPM) rate was 13.1% in 2025, not statistically different from 2024.\n\n## Sources\n\n1. U.S. Census Bureau, Press Release CB26-151, \"Income, Poverty and Health Insurance Coverage in the United States: 2025\" (Sept. 15, 2026): https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/income-poverty-health-insurance-coverage.html\n2. U.S. Census Bureau, \"Income in the United States: 2025\" (P60-289, Sept. 15, 2026): https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-289.html\n3. U.S. Census Bureau, \"Poverty in the United States: 2025\" (P60-290, Sept. 15, 2026): https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-290.html\n4. Corroborating coverage: CNBC, \"Americans' incomes rose and poverty fell in 2025, Census Bureau says\" (Sept. 15, 2026): https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/15/income-poverty-census-fed-interest-rates.html\n\nANSWER: $87,460; 10.2%"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-007", "category": "grounding", "title": "Python 3.15.0 release date and release manager", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 16028, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 685, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 814, "search_tokens": 19185, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1645, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 4, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj1826e561-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f35219-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:49-0500", "answer": "Based on my research, here are the findings:\n\n**Python 3.15.0 final release date:** The official Python.org release page for Python 3.15.0 states the **release date as October 9, 2026** [COaisabK, xtuY075j]. This is confirmed by PEP 790 (Python 3.15 Release Schedule), which lists \"3.15.0 final: Friday, 2026-10-09\" under the \"Actual\" schedule [T6YDwDZ5, 1N3c0h3K]. The final release was delayed from the original October 1 date due to a surprise third release candidate (rc3) on October 2, 2026, to address last-minute lazy-import bugs [AE79Q2Xz, DVcRgpON].\n\n**Release manager for Python 3.15:** **Hugo van Kemenade** is the release manager for Python 3.15. This is confirmed by:\n- PEP 790, which explicitly states \"3.15 release manager: Hugo van Kemenade\" [T6YDwDZ5]\n- The official Python 3.15.0 release page, which thanks \"the Sovereign Tech Agency for supporting Hugo van Kemenade's work as release manager for Python 3.14 and 3.15\" [COaisabK, xtuY075j]\n- The Python Insider blog announcement signed by \"Your release team, Hugo van Kemenade, Ned Deily, Steve Dower\" [eBrn5SmF, flKhTSBT]\n\n**Sources cited:**\n- [COaisabK, xtuY075j] Python Release Python 3.15.0 | Python.org \u2014 https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3150/\n- [T6YDwDZ5, 1N3c0h3K] PEP 790 \u2013 Python 3.15 Release Schedule \u2014 https://peps.python.org/pep-0790/\n- [eBrn5SmF, flKhTSBT] Python 3.15.0 (final) is here! | Python Insider \u2014 https://blog.python.org/2026/10/python-3150-final-is-here/\n- [AE79Q2Xz, DVcRgpON] TechAIWire article on the delay \u2014 https://techaiwire.com/articles/python-3-15-0-final-delayed-october-9-rc3-lazy-imports/\n\nANSWER: 2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-008", "category": "grounding", "title": "Kubernetes v1.37 release name and date", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 11509, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 428, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 804, "search_tokens": 18018, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1155, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 3, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Garhwal; 2026-08-26", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Garhwal; 2026-08-26"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj193b62fc-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3521a-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:49-0500", "answer": "Based on my web search and verification from official sources:\n\n**Release name:** Kubernetes v1.37 is codenamed **\"Garhwal\"** (\u0917\u0922\u093c\u0935\u093e\u0932, pronounced *ga\u1e5bhv\u0101l*), named after the Himalayan region of Uttarakhand, India. This is confirmed by the official Kubernetes blog post titled \"Kubernetes v1.37: Garhwal\" [kubernetes.io](https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/).\n\n**Release date:** v1.37.0 was released on **August 26, 2026**. This is confirmed by:\n- The official Kubernetes blog post dated \"Wednesday, August 26, 2026\" [kubernetes.io](https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/)\n- The GitHub release page for v1.37.0 showing \"k8s-release-robot released this 26 Aug\" with source code assets timestamped `2026-08-26T10:44:20Z` [github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/releases/tag/v1.37.0](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/releases/tag/v1.37.0)\n- The Kubernetes sig-release repository schedule showing \"Wednesday 26th August 2026: Week 15 \u2014 Kubernetes v1.37.0 released\" [github.com/kubernetes/sig-release](https://github.com/kubernetes/sig-release/tree/master/releases/release-1.37)\n\nANSWER: Garhwal; 2026-08-26"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-010", "category": "grounding", "title": "Vega-C flight VV30 payloads", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 11565, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 3, "output_tokens": 637, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 798, "search_tokens": 18135, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1713, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 4, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer); Copernicus Sentinel-3C", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Copernicus Sentinel-3C; FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj19af902e-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3792e-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:49-0500", "answer": "Europe's Vega-C rocket launched two satellites on flight VV30 in September 2026:\n\n1. **Copernicus Sentinel-3C** \u2013 the third satellite of the Sentinel-3 mission of the European Union's Copernicus programme, dedicated to monitoring oceans, land, ice and the atmosphere. It is managed by EUMETSAT on behalf of the European Commission.\n\n2. **FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)** \u2013 ESA's eighth Earth Explorer mission, designed to monitor vegetation health from space by detecting the faint fluorescence emitted by plants during photosynthesis.\n\nThe launch took place on **15 September 2026 at 03:21 CEST** (14 September at 22:21 local time) from Europe's Spaceport in Kourou, French Guiana. It was the eighth Vega-C launch overall and the second of 2026, operated solely by the Italian company Avio.\n\n**Sources:**\n- ESA \u2013 \"Vega-C flight VV30 with FLEX and Sentinel-3C\" (https://www.esa.int/ESA_Multimedia/Images/2026/09/Vega-C_flight_VV30_with_FLEX_and_Sentinel-3C)\n- Spaceflight Now \u2013 \"Avio launches pair of climate monitoring European spacecraft to study plants, oceans and atmospheric changes\" (https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/09/15/avio-launches-pair-of-climate-monitoring-european-spacecraft-to-study-plants-oceans-and-atmospheric-changes/)\n- Avio press release \u2013 \"AVIO TO LAUNCH COPERNICUS SENTINEL-3C AND FLEX SATELLITES ON SEPTEMBER 14th 2026 ON VEGA C\" (https://www.avio.com/press-release/avio-to-launch-copernicus-sentinel-3-c-and-flex-satellites-on-september-14th-2026-on-vega-c)\n- NASASpaceFlight.com \u2013 \"Vega C set to launch the ESA Sentinel-3C and FLEX missions from Kourou\" (https://www.nasaspaceflight.com/2026/09/vega-c-launch-sentinel-3c-flex/)\n\nANSWER: Copernicus Sentinel-3C; FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-012", "category": "grounding", "title": "Mistral Large 4 announcement and size", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 16478, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 586, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 813, "search_tokens": 28148, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1800, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 4, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "2026-10-06; 1 trillion total; 52 billion active", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "2026-10-06; 1 trillion (1.05T) total; 52 billion active"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj188ef62e-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3792d-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:49-0500", "answer": "Based on my research, here's what I found:\n\n**Announcement Date:** Mistral AI announced Mistral Large 4 (nicknamed \"Le Chonk\") on **October 6, 2026**, launching it as a public preview through the Mistral Studio API.\n\n**Parameters:** According to Mistral's official announcement and documentation:\n- **Total parameters:** 1 trillion (the official model documentation specifies **1.05 trillion** total parameters)\n- **Active parameters:** **52 billion** active parameters\n\nNote: There was some initial confusion in early coverage, with some sources reporting 49 billion active parameters. However, Mistral's current official announcement states \"ML4 is a 1 trillion-parameter natively multimodal model with **52 billion active parameters**,\" and the official model documentation confirms \"52B active parameters and 1.05T total parameters.\" The 49B figure appears to refer specifically to active expert parameters, while 52B includes embeddings and output layers.\n\n**Sources:**\n1. Mistral AI official announcement: https://mistral.ai/news/mistral-large-4/ \u2014 \"ML4 is a 1 trillion-parameter natively multimodal model with 52 billion active parameters\" (dated October 6, 2026)\n2. Mistral AI official documentation: https://docs.mistral.ai/models/mistral-large-4 \u2014 \"It features 52B active parameters and 1.05T total parameters, and a 1.6B vision encoder\" (dated October 6, 2026)\n3. Mixed-News analysis: https://mixed-news.com/en/mistral-large-4-49-billion-52-billion-active-parameters-blog-docs/ \u2014 discusses the discrepancy between announcement and docs figures\n4. Kingy AI analysis: https://kingy.ai/blog/mistral-large-4-specs-benchmarks-pricing/ \u2014 clarifies that 49B refers to active experts, while 52B includes embeddings and output layers\n\nANSWER: 2026-10-06; 1 trillion (1.05T) total; 52 billion active"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-009", "category": "grounding", "title": "Latest stable Conductor OSS release (Oct 2026)", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 18009, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 10, "output_tokens": 696, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 816, "search_tokens": 43280, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1308, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 2, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "v3.32.5", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "v3.32.5"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj1850dba2-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f37930-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:51-0500", "answer": "Based on my research of the official GitHub releases page for `conductor-oss/conductor`:\n\n**Key findings:**\n\n1. The releases page at https://github.com/conductor-oss/conductor/releases shows the release list with the most recent entries being:\n   - `v3.33.0-rc13` (released Oct 14, 2026) \u2014 **pre-release**\n   - `v3.33.0-rc12` (released Oct 12, 2026) \u2014 **pre-release**\n   - `v3.33.0-rc11` (released Oct 5, 2026) \u2014 **pre-release**\n   - ...and several other `v3.33.0-rc*` pre-releases\n\n2. The most recent **stable (non-prerelease)** release is **`v3.32.5`**, which is explicitly labeled with the **\"Latest\"** badge on GitHub (indicating it's the latest stable release). It was released on **September 25, 2026** by @nthmost-orkes.\n\n3. All releases newer than `v3.32.5` (i.e., `v3.33.0-rc5` through `v3.33.0-rc13`) are marked as **\"Pre-release\"** on GitHub, so they don't qualify as stable releases.\n\n**Sources:**\n- [GitHub Releases page for conductor-oss/conductor](https://github.com/conductor-oss/conductor/releases) \u2014 shows `v3.32.5` with the \"Latest\" badge and all `v3.33.0-rc*` releases marked as \"Pre-release\"\n- [Release v3.32.5 \u00b7 conductor-oss/conductor](https://github.com/conductor-oss/conductor/releases/tag/v3.32.5) \u2014 confirms this is the latest stable release, released Sep 25, 2026\n\nANSWER: v3.32.5"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-012", "category": "grounding", "title": "Mistral Large 4 announcement and size", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 18155, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 1224, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 813, "search_tokens": 18621, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1686, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 3073, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 3, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "2026-10-06; 1 trillion total; 52 billion active", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "2026-10-06; 1 trillion total; 52 billion active"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj188ef62f-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3792d-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:51-0500", "answer": "I'll search for information about Mistral Large 4's announcement.The search results show a discrepancy between Mistral's announcement and its docs, so let me verify the exact wording from Mistral's official announcement.I found the answer by checking Mistral's official announcement directly.\n\n**Announcement date:** Mistral AI published \"Introducing Mistral Large 4\" on **October 6, 2026**, opening a public preview via the Mistral Studio API. [Source: Mistral AI, \"Introducing Mistral Large 4\"](https://mistral.ai/news/mistral-large-4/)\n\n**Parameters (per the announcement):** The announcement states: *\"ML4 is a 1 trillion-parameter natively multimodal model with 52 billion active parameters.\"* [Source: Mistral AI announcement](https://mistral.ai/news/mistral-large-4/)\n\nSo according to Mistral's announcement: **1 trillion total parameters** and **52 billion active parameters** (a granular Mixture-of-Experts model).\n\nWorth noting: there is some inconsistency across Mistral's own materials and early coverage \u2014 Mistral's technical docs/model card list **1.05T total / 52B active** plus a 1.6B vision encoder [Source: Mistral Docs](https://docs.mistral.ai/models/mistral-large-4), and several outlets reporting on launch day (Oct 6) quoted the announcement as saying **49 billion active**, which appears to have been the figure in the original version of the post before Mistral updated it [Source: mixed-news analysis of the discrepancy](https://mixed-news.com/en/mistral-large-4-49-billion-52-billion-active-parameters-blog-docs/). But the announcement as it currently stands says 1 trillion total and 52 billion active.\n\nANSWER: 2026-10-06; 1 trillion total; 52 billion active"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-008", "category": "grounding", "title": "Kubernetes v1.37 release name and date", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 15345, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 964, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 804, "search_tokens": 17805, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1282, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1635, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 3, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Garhwal; 2026-08-26", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Garhwal; 2026-08-26"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj193b8a0e-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3521a-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:52-0500", "answer": "The search results are consistent. Let me verify against the official Kubernetes blog and the GitHub release page to confirm the exact date.I have confirmed the details from the official Kubernetes blog and the GitHub release page.\n\n**Findings:**\n\n- **Release name (codename):** Kubernetes v1.37 is named **\"Garhwal\"** (\u0917\u0922\u093c\u0935\u093e\u0932, pronounced *ga\u1e5bhv\u0101l*), after the Himalayan region of Uttarakhand, India. The official release announcement is titled \"Kubernetes v1.37: Garhwal\" [1].\n- **Release date of v1.37.0:** **August 26, 2026** (Wednesday). The official blog post is dated Wednesday, August 26, 2026 [1], the GitHub release `v1.37.0` was published by k8s-release-robot on 26 Aug with assets timestamped 2026-08-26T10:44:20Z [2], and the sig-release schedule confirms \"Wednesday 26th August 2026: Week 15 \u2014 Kubernetes v1.37.0 released\" [3].\n\n**Sources used:**\n1. Kubernetes Blog \u2014 \"Kubernetes v1.37: Garhwal\" (official release announcement): https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/\n2. GitHub \u2014 kubernetes/kubernetes Release v1.37.0: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/releases/tag/v1.37.0\n3. GitHub \u2014 kubernetes/sig-release, release-1.37 schedule: https://github.com/kubernetes/sig-release/tree/master/releases/release-1.37\n\nANSWER: Garhwal; 2026-08-26"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-010", "category": "grounding", "title": "Vega-C flight VV30 payloads", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 15807, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 3, "output_tokens": 1161, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 798, "search_tokens": 15951, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1403, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2824, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "citation_count": 0, "pass": false, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer); Copernicus Sentinel-3C", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": false, "extracted": "Copernicus Sentinel-3C; FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj19af420b-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3792e-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:54-0500", "answer": "I'll search for details on Vega-C flight VV30.Vega-C flight VV30 lifted off from Europe\u2019s Spaceport in French Guiana on the night of 14\u201315 September 2026 (22:21 local / 01:21 UTC on 15 Sep; 03:21 CEST). It was a dual Earth-observation launch operated by Avio, carrying two spacecraft fitted in the fairing on a Vespa secondary payload adapter, with Sentinel-3C deploying first and FLEX about an hour later.\n\nThe two satellites were:\n- **Copernicus Sentinel-3C** \u2014 the third Sentinel-3 satellite, for the European Commission/Copernicus programme (operations by EUMETSAT), monitoring oceans, land, ice and atmosphere.\n- **FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)** \u2014 ESA\u2019s Earth Explorer satellite for monitoring plant health via chlorophyll fluorescence.\n\nSources: ESA (\u201cVega-C flight VV30 with FLEX and Sentinel-3C\u201d; ESA Vega page) [search-result://f7860IG3, search-result://nHqNWkZy, search-result://UAtOy4W6]; Avio press release, 30 Jul 2026 [search-result://shyLnnyt, search-result://Wgw6PqeO]; CNES/Centre Spatial Guyanais \u201cVV30 mission in a nutshell\u201d and CNES launch recap [search-result://cylS6QNI, search-result://Q4aESdAe]; Spaceflight Now launch report and preview [search-result://mQO8wHdM, search-result://R49Ldwjo, search-result://sU94WiMn, search-result://FCE9oUBN, search-result://adeqKe6h]; NASASpaceFlight.com [search-result://Ahg0CmpR].\n\nANSWER: Copernicus Sentinel-3C; FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-006", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Asian Games medal table leader", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 21666, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 1460, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 814, "search_tokens": 12800, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1823, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2943, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 5, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "China; 169", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "China; 169"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj19007cc8-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3521b-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:56-0500", "answer": "Based on my web research, I found consistent reporting across multiple sources about the final medal table at the 20th Asian Games (Aichi\u2013Nagoya 2026), held 19 September \u2013 4 October 2026.\n\n**Findings:**\n- **China** finished at the top of the medal table, extending its streak to 12 consecutive Asian Games atop the standings (since 1982).\n- China's final tally: **169 gold**, 89 silver, and 83 bronze medals \u2014 **341 medals in total**.\n- Host nation Japan finished second with 83 gold (269 total), followed by South Korea (39 gold) and India (21 gold).\n\n**Sources cited:**\n1. Wikipedia \u2013 \"2026 Asian Games medal table\" (top row: 169 gold / 89 silver / 83 bronze / 341 total) \u2014 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games_medal_table\n2. Sports League \u2013 \"Asian Games 2026 Final Medal Tally\" (\"China topped the table for the 12th Games in a row with 169 gold and 341 medals in total\") \u2014 https://www.isportsleague.com/asian-games-2026-medal-tally/\n3. Khel Now \u2013 \"Final medal tally of Asian Games 2026\" (\"China topped the final medal standings with 169 gold, 89 silver and 83 bronze medals, for a total of 341 medals\") \u2014 https://khelnow.com/asian-games/final-medal-tally-asian-games-202610\n4. Times of India \u2013 Asian Games 2026 Medal Tally (\"1. China: 169 Gold | 89 Silver | 83 Bronze | Total: 341\") \u2014 https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/asian-games/medal-tally\n5. Indian Express \u2013 \"China or Japan, who was the biggest winner of the 2026 Asian Games\" (\"claiming a whopping 341 medals, 169 of them gold\") \u2014 https://indianexpress.com/article/sports/china-japan-biggest-winner-asian-games-2026-medal-tally-analysis-10906462/\n\n(Note: one outlet, insidethegames.biz, reported \"189 gold,\" but this appears to be a typo \u2014 it contradicts the 341 total and every other source, all of which agree on 169 gold.)\n\nANSWER: China; 169"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-007", "category": "grounding", "title": "Python 3.15.0 release date and release manager", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 24520, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 7, "output_tokens": 1391, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 814, "search_tokens": 21050, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 575, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 3925, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 3, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj1826e563-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f35219-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:57-0500", "answer": "Python\u2019s official 3.15.0 release page lists **\u201cRelease date: Oct. 9, 2026\u201d** and calls it the **stable release of Python 3.15.0** [python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3150/). PEP 790 lists **\u201c3.15 release manager: Hugo van Kemenade\u201d** and schedules **\u201c3.15.0 final: Friday, 2026-10-09\u201d** [PEP 790](https://peps.python.org/pep-0790/). The Python Insider final announcement is also signed by the release team including Hugo van Kemenade [Python Insider](https://blog.python.org/2026/10/python-3150-final-is-here/).\n\nANSWER: 2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-005", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 US Open women's singles final score", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 24308, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 1335, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 809, "search_tokens": 25278, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1435, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2862, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "citation_count": 0, "pass": false, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Elena Rybakina def. Aryna Sabalenka 6-4, 5-7, 6-2", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": false, "extracted": "Elena Rybakina def. Aryna Sabalenka 6-4, 5-7, 6-2"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj192ccb81-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3792c-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:32:58-0500", "answer": "I'll search the web for the 2026 US Open women's singles final result.The search results are highly consistent. Let me verify with the official US Open source and the BBC live coverage to confirm the details.**Elena Rybakina of Kazakhstan won the 2026 US Open women's singles title**, defeating two-time defending champion **Aryna Sabalenka** (top seed) in the final on Saturday, September 12, 2026, at Arthur Ashe Stadium in Flushing Meadows. The score was **6\u20134, 5\u20137, 6\u20132**.\n\nThe result was confirmed by multiple independent sources:\n- The **official US Open website** (usopen.org): \"Elena Rybakina won the 2026 US Open women's singles title on Saturday, defeating two-time defending champion Aryna Sabalenka, 6-4, 5-7, 6-2.\"\n- **BBC Sport** live coverage (12 September 2026): set-by-set confirmation of 6\u20134, 5\u20137, 6\u20132, with Sabalenka listed as the (1) seed and Rybakina as the (2) seed.\n- **Wikipedia** (2026 US Open \u2013 Women's singles) and the official US Open women's draw PDF both record the same champion and score.\n- **Sports Illustrated** and **USA Today** also report Rybakina's win over Sabalenka in the same three-set score.\n\nThe victory was Rybakina's first US Open title and her third Grand Slam singles title overall (adding to her 2022 Wimbledon crown and her 2026 Australian Open win over the same opponent), and it lifted her to world No. 1 for the first time.\n\nANSWER: Elena Rybakina def. Aryna Sabalenka 6-4, 5-7, 6-2"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-005", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 US Open women's singles final score", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 32320, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 9, "output_tokens": 976, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 809, "search_tokens": 37495, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1866, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 6, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "Elena Rybakina def. Aryna Sabalenka 6-4, 5-7, 6-2", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "Elena Rybakina def. Aryna Sabalenka 6-4, 5-7, 6-2"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj192ca470-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3792c-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:07-0500", "answer": "**Elena Rybakina of Kazakhstan won the 2026 US Open women's singles title**, defeating two-time defending champion **Aryna Sabalenka of Belarus** in the final on Saturday, September 12, 2026, at Arthur Ashe Stadium in New York. The final score was **6\u20134, 5\u20137, 6\u20132**.\n\nThe win gave Rybakina her first US Open title and third Grand Slam singles title overall (she also won Wimbledon 2022 and the 2026 Australian Open). The victory also confirmed her rise to world No. 1, ending Sabalenka's 99-week run at the top of the rankings, and denied Sabalenka a third consecutive US Open title.\n\n**Sources:**\n- US Open official site: \"Rybakina defeats two-time defending champion Sabalenka to win 2026 US Open\" (Sept. 12, 2026) \u2014 https://www.usopen.org/en_US/news/articles/2026-09-12/rybakina_defeats_two-time_defending_champion_sabalenka_to_win_2026_us_open.html\n- BBC Sport: \"US Open 2026 results: Elena Rybakina beats Aryna Sabalenka to win New York title\" (Sept. 12\u201313, 2026) \u2014 https://www.bbc.com/sport/tennis/articles/clym434j01xo\n- AP News: \"Elena Rybakina beats Aryna Sabalenka to win the US Open title\" (Sept. 12, 2026) \u2014 https://apnews.com/article/us-open-womens-final-sabalenka-rybakina-521adac24c4f6350c07bdd914cd83b97\n- USA Today: \"US Open women's final: Elena Rybakina wins to deny Aryna Sabalenka three-peat\" (Sept. 12, 2026) \u2014 https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/tennis/open/2026/09/12/us-open-womens-final-result-highlights-sabalenka-rybakina--live/91715481007/\n- Al Jazeera: \"Elena Rybakina defeats Aryna Sabalenka in US Open women's singles final\" (Sept. 12, 2026) \u2014 https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/9/12/elena-rybakina-defeats-aryna-sabalenka-in-us-open-womens-singles-final\n- Wikipedia: \"2026 US Open \u2013 Women's singles\" \u2014 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_US_Open_%E2%80%93_Women's_singles\n\nANSWER: Elena Rybakina def. Aryna Sabalenka 6-4, 5-7, 6-2"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-009", "category": "grounding", "title": "Latest stable Conductor OSS release (Oct 2026)", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 34055, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 9, "output_tokens": 2640, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 816, "search_tokens": 39060, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 714, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 7998, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 4, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "v3.32.5", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "v3.32.5"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj1850dba3-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f37930-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:07-0500", "answer": "I checked the GitHub releases list and API. GitHub\u2019s `/releases/latest` endpoint returns `tag_name: v3.32.5` with `prerelease: false` and `published_at: 2026-09-25`; the release page also labels `v3.32.5` as \u201cLatest.\u201d The newer October tag `v3.33.0-rc13` was published 2026-10-14 but is an RC build, so it is excluded as a prerelease. Sources: [GitHub releases list](https://github.com/conductor-oss/conductor/releases), [GitHub API latest release](https://api.github.com/repos/conductor-oss/conductor/releases/latest), [v3.32.5 release](https://github.com/conductor-oss/conductor/releases/tag/v3.32.5), [v3.33.0-rc13 release](https://github.com/conductor-oss/conductor/releases/tag/v3.33.0-rc13).\n\nANSWER: v3.32.5"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "grounding-006", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Asian Games medal table leader", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 35400, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 15, "output_tokens": 1207, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 814, "search_tokens": 66212, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 2297, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "citation_count": 6, "pass": true, "pattern_misses": [], "expected": "China; 169", "answer_line_found": true, "cited": true, "extracted": "China; 169"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj19007cc6-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj17f3521b-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:10-0500", "answer": "Based on my web searches, I have found consistent and corroborating information from multiple reliable sources about the final medal standings at the 2026 Asian Games in Aichi-Nagoya, Japan.\n\n**Key findings:**\n\nThe 20th Asian Games (Aichi-Nagoya 2026) were held from 19 September to 4 October 2026, featuring 469 events across 43 sports. Multiple independent sources confirm the final medal table:\n\n1. **Xinhua News Agency** (China's state news agency) reported: \"China topping the gold medal table for the 12th consecutive edition, and finishing with **169 gold**, 89 silver and 83 bronze medals\" [Source: english.news.cn]\n\n2. **Kyodo News / The Mainichi** (Japanese news agency) reported: \"China finished comfortably atop the medal standings with 341 medals, including **169 golds**\" [Source: mainichi.jp]\n\n3. **Times of India** reported: \"China topped the medal tally with 341 medals, including **169 gold**, followed by hosts Japan with 269 medals, including 83 gold\" [Source: timesofindia.indiatimes.com]\n\n4. **Khel Now** (Indian sports portal) reported: \"China topped the final medal standings with **169 gold**, 89 silver and 83 bronze medals, for a total of 341 medals\" [Source: khelnow.com]\n\n5. **Indian Express** reported: \"China conquered the Asian Games in Aichi-Nagoya, claiming a whopping 341 medals, **169 of them gold**\" [Source: indianexpress.com]\n\n6. **Wikipedia's 2026 Asian Games medal table** also confirms China at rank 1 with 169 gold, 89 silver, 83 bronze (341 total) [Source: en.wikipedia.org]\n\nAll sources agree that **China (People's Republic of China)** topped the medal table for the 12th consecutive Asian Games with **169 gold medals**.\n\n**Sources cited:**\n- Xinhua News Agency: https://english.news.cn/20261004/0d5d63d5f50a41a28f9cf40229426dcf/c.html\n- The Mainichi (Kyodo News): https://mainichi.jp/english/articles/20261005/p2g00m0sp002000c\n- Times of India: https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/asian-games/medal-tally\n- Khel Now: https://khelnow.com/asian-games/final-medal-tally-asian-games-202610\n- Indian Express: https://indianexpress.com/article/sports/china-japan-biggest-winner-asian-games-2026-medal-tally-analysis-10906462/\n- Wikipedia - 2026 Asian Games medal table: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games_medal_table\n\nANSWER: China; 169"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-001", "category": "your_data", "title": "SEV-1 status page cadence", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1327, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 37, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 156, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 56, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4337, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4334}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer matches the documented SEV-1 cadence: first update within 20 minutes of declaration, then every 30 minutes until resolved.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj2efe5f36-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a4f-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:15-0500", "answer": "The first status page update must go out **within 20 minutes of declaration**. After that, post updates **every 30 minutes until the incident is resolved**."}
