{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-001", "category": "your_data", "title": "SEV-1 status page cadence", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3883, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 288, "reasoning_tokens": 207, "input_tokens": 4139, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 319, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 964, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 59, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4382, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer gives the correct 20-minute initial deadline and 30-minute update cadence until resolution, and its additional Communications Lead details are supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj2efe5f37-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a4f-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:18-0500", "answer": "For a SEV-1, per section 2.1 of the handbook:\n\n- **First status page update**: within **20 minutes of declaration**\n- **Subsequent updates**: **every 30 minutes** until resolved\n\n(For context, the Communications Lead writes these updates\u2014and for a SEV-1, the Communications Lead must be a different person from the IC.)"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4206, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 335, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4149, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 1234, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 61, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4790, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies SEV-2, the primary and service-owner paging requirements, and both Director of Reliability escalation triggers, with additional details supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj2f418c37-d02d-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a51-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:18-0500", "answer": "Based on the handbook, here's the situation:\n\n**What severity this is:** An API error rate above 5% for 10 consecutive minutes is a **SEV-2 (Major)** \u2014 and at 50 minutes, it's well past that threshold.\n\n**Who should have been paged by now:**\n\n| Tier | Who | Trigger | Status at 50 min unmitigated |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Tier 1 | On-call primary (secondary as backup) | Every incident, at declaration | \u2705 Paged at declaration |\n| Tier 2 | Owning team's service owner | SEV-2 with no mitigation after **45 minutes** | \u2705 **Should have been paged at 45 min** \u2014 you're at 50 min |\n| Tier 3 | Director of Reliability | SEV-2 lasting more than **3 hours** | \u274c Not yet (you're at ~50 min) |\n| Tier 4 | VP of Engineering and CTO | SEV-1 > 2 hours, or suspected data exposure | \u274c Not applicable |\n\n**What would escalate this to the Director of Reliability (Tier 3):**\n- The SEV-2 lasting more than **3 hours** from declaration to resolution (not mitigation), **or**\n- This being the **third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days**\n\nAlso note: Beacon should have auto-escalated from primary to secondary after 15 minutes without acknowledgement (section 6.2), and the IC should have been assigned within 30 minutes of declaration (section 2.1)."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-006", "category": "your_data", "title": "Incident chat log retention", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2231, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 188, "reasoning_tokens": 150, "input_tokens": 4119, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 165, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 710, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 45, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4289, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states the documented retention period of 400 days followed by automatic deletion.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj30aafdf0-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef6164-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:18-0500", "answer": "According to section 10.1 (Retention) of the Ferngate Platform Operations Handbook, **incident channel chat logs are kept for 400 days**, then deleted automatically."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-006", "category": "your_data", "title": "Incident chat log retention", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1236, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 27, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4119, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 124, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 49, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4280, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4277}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states the 400-day retention period and automatic deletion specified in section 10.1.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj30aafdef-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef6164-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:18-0500", "answer": "According to section 10.1 of the handbook, incident channel chat logs are kept for **400 days**, then deleted automatically."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5464, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 333, "reasoning_tokens": 204, "input_tokens": 4085, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4082}, "answer_chars": 480, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 56, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4484, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates the Platinum downtime allowance and both credit thresholds, and its additional request deadline and contract precedence statements are supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj2f14afc2-d02d-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a50-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:19-0500", "answer": "Platinum\u2019s **99.95% monthly API uptime commitment** allows **21.6 minutes (21 minutes 36 seconds)** of downtime in a 30-day month.\n\n- **More than 21.6 minutes:** credit of **10% of that month\u2019s fees**.\n- **More than 432 minutes (7 hours 12 minutes):** uptime falls below 99.0%, so the credit increases to **25%** instead.\n\nThe customer must request the credit within **30 days after the affected month ends**. A signed customer contract overrides the handbook if its terms differ."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-005", "category": "your_data", "title": "Time in lieu for overnight incidents", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1518, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 70, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4094, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4091}, "answer_chars": 274, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 59, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4414, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly awards 8 hours for the two overnight incidents lasting more than 45 minutes and states that each allowance expires 30 days after its incident.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj31e401d7-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a52-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:19-0500", "answer": "You\u2019re owed **8 hours of time in lieu**: 4 hours each for the 70-minute and 2-hour overnight incidents. The 30-minute incident doesn\u2019t qualify because incidents must last **more than 45 minutes**.\n\nUse each 4-hour allowance **within 30 days of its incident**, or it expires."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-005", "category": "your_data", "title": "Time in lieu for overnight incidents", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1198, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 72, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4321, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4224}, "answer_chars": 287, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 86, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4414, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": ["re:\\b8\\s*(hours|hrs|h)\\b"], "pass": false}, "judge": {"score": 2, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the two qualifying incidents and the 30-day use window, but incorrectly totals the entitlement as 4 hours rather than 8 hours.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": ["The total time in lieu owed is 4 hours; the document instead provides 4 hours per qualifying incident, totaling 8 hours."], "faithful": false}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj31e401db-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a52-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:20-0500", "answer": "You are owed **4 hours of time in lieu** (only the 70-minute and 2-hour incidents qualify, as they lasted more than 45 minutes).\n\nYou must take this time within **30 days** of each incident. Since the incidents occurred last week, the 30-day window starts from the date of each incident."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1431, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 83, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4309, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4224}, "answer_chars": 315, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 64, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4458, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 4, "reason": "The answer correctly permits the patch with VP approval, progressive rollout, and CAB logging, but omits the rubric-required explicit identification of the holiday freeze and classification as a Normal change.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj323ae33d-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a53-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:20-0500", "answer": "Yes, you can ship the patch on December 22, as it is a security vulnerability rated CVSS 9.0 or higher. You need approval from the **VP of Engineering** (per section 7.4). The patch must follow the **progressive rollout** in section 7.3 and be logged as a freeze exception in the CAB register within 1 business day."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-005", "category": "your_data", "title": "Time in lieu for overnight incidents", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1485, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 71, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4094, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4091}, "answer_chars": 274, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 59, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4415, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates 8 hours for the two incidents lasting more than 45 minutes and states that each allotment expires 30 days after its incident.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj31e401d8-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a52-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:20-0500", "answer": "You\u2019re owed **8 hours of time in lieu**: 4 hours each for the 70-minute and 2-hour overnight incidents. The 30-minute incident doesn\u2019t qualify because incidents must last **more than 45 minutes**.\n\nUse each 4-hour allotment **within 30 days of its incident**, or it expires."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-005", "category": "your_data", "title": "Time in lieu for overnight incidents", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1915, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 100, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4151, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 381, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 62, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4445, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly awards 8 hours for the two incidents exceeding 45 minutes and states that the time must be used within 30 days of each incident or it expires.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj31e401d9-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a52-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:21-0500", "answer": "Based on section 5 of the handbook, time in lieu is **4 hours for each overnight incident that lasts more than 45 minutes**.\n\nOf your three overnight incidents:\n- 30 minutes \u2014 does not qualify\n- 70 minutes \u2014 qualifies \u2192 4 hours\n- 2 hours \u2014 qualifies \u2192 4 hours\n\n**You are owed 8 hours of time in lieu.**\n\nTime in lieu must be taken **within 30 days of the incident**, or it expires."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-007", "category": "your_data", "title": "Postmortem draft vs customer RCA deadlines", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4634, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 391, "reasoning_tokens": 299, "input_tokens": 4136, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 380, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1248, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 66, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4417, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly gives the 3-business-day postmortem draft deadline and 5-business-day SEV-1 customer-facing RCA deadline, both measured from resolution, with supported additional details.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj30bd4d81-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef6166-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:21-0500", "answer": "Based on the handbook:\n\n**Internal postmortem draft:** Due within **3 business days of resolution** (Section 9). The review meeting must happen within 7 business days of resolution.\n\n**Customer-facing RCA:** Must be published within **5 business days of resolution** (Section 8.4).\n\n*Note: \"Business day\" means Monday to Friday, excluding Ferngate company holidays (Section 1.1).*"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2781, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 189, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4141, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 642, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 110, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4578, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 3, "reason": "The answer gives the correct 90-minute calculation and reference latest start of 14:30 UTC, but contradicts itself by initially saying the 15:00 UTC start is allowed.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": ["The opening claim that starting the requested Normal deploy at 15:00 UTC on Friday is allowed contradicts the mandatory rollout duration and Friday cutoff."], "faithful": false}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj3134fd03-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef6165-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:22-0500", "answer": "Yes, starting at 15:00 UTC on Friday is allowed \u2014 but with a condition.\n\nPer section 7.2, on Fridays production deploys may start from 14:00 UTC, **and the change must reach 100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC**.\n\nSince your change is a Normal change, it must follow the progressive rollout in section 7.3:\n1. Canary at 5% for 30 minutes\n2. 25% for 60 minutes\n3. 100%\n\nThat's a minimum of **90 minutes** of rollout stages. Starting at 15:00 UTC means you'd reach 100% at 16:30 UTC \u2014 which violates the Friday rule.\n\n**The latest you could start is 14:30 UTC**, which would get you to 100% traffic by 16:00 UTC (assuming no delays in the stages)."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2537, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 166, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4312, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 531, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 149, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4540, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": ["16:30", "14:30"], "pass": false}, "judge": {"score": 1, "reason": "The answer contradicts the mandatory 90-minute rollout, which makes a 15:00 start reach 100% at 16:30, and gives 14:00 rather than the reference's 14:30 latest start.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": ["A Normal deploy using the standard progressive rollout is allowed to start at 15:00 UTC on Friday.", "The required progressive rollout timing can be adjusted to finish by 16:00 UTC.", "The latest Friday start time for a Normal deploy is 14:00 UTC."], "faithful": false}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj3134fd05-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef6165-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:22-0500", "answer": "The document states:\n\n- **Friday**: production deploys may start from **14:00 UTC**, and the change must reach **100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC**.\n\nSince your deploy starts at **15:00 UTC**, it is allowed, but it must complete (reach 100% of traffic) by **16:00 UTC**. If the standard progressive rollout (3 stages: 5% \u2192 25% \u2192 100%) would exceed this deadline, you must adjust the rollout timing to finish by 16:00 UTC.\n\nThe latest you could start a **Normal** deploy on Friday is **14:00 UTC** to ensure completion by 16:00 UTC."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2403, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 108, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 475, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 61, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4484, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday-freeze exception, required VP approval, Normal-change rollout and approval requirements, and CAB-register logging deadline, all supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj323ae33a-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a53-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:22-0500", "answer": "Yes. December 22 is within the holiday freeze, but a CVSS 9.3 patch qualifies for the exception for vulnerabilities rated **CVSS 9.0 or higher**.\n\nShip it as a **Normal change** with:\n- **VP of Engineering approval** for the freeze exception.\n- One approval from the owning team, plus CAB approval if the change is high-risk.\n\nIt must follow the Normal progressive rollout and applicable deploy windows. Log the freeze exception in the CAB register within **1 business day**."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2648, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 217, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4139, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 902, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 61, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4590, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday-freeze exception, VP approval, progressive rollout and CAB logging deadline, and its additional conditional Normal-change approvals are supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj323ae33b-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a53-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:22-0500", "answer": "Yes \u2014 you can ship it on December 22.\n\nDecember 22 falls inside the **holiday freeze** (December 18 through January 4, inclusive), during which only Standard and Emergency changes are allowed \u2014 **with one exception**: a patch for a security vulnerability rated **CVSS 9.0 or higher** may ship as a **Normal change** with approval from the **VP of Engineering**. Your CVSS 9.3 patch qualifies.\n\nSo the approval you need is:\n- **VP of Engineering approval** (for the freeze exception)\n- Plus the normal **Normal change** approvals: one approval from the owning team, and since it's a security patch it would also go through **CAB** if it's high-risk (e.g., schema migration, network/ACL, or authentication change)\n\nTwo other requirements apply:\n- It must still follow the **progressive rollout** (canary 5% \u2192 25% \u2192 100%)\n- The freeze exception must be **logged in the CAB register within 1 business day**"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 8687, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 686, "reasoning_tokens": 490, "input_tokens": 4149, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 800, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2007, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 71, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4661, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies SEV-2, specifies primary and service-owner paging and conditional secondary paging, and gives both Director escalation triggers with supported response deadlines.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj2f416525-d02d-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a51-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:23-0500", "answer": "Because the API error rate has been above 5% for 10+ consecutive minutes, this is a **SEV-2**.\n\nBy now, after 50 minutes without mitigation:\n\n- **Tier 1:** the on-call **primary** should have been paged at declaration; the **secondary** if the primary did not acknowledge within 15 minutes.\n- **Tier 2:** the owning team\u2019s **service owner** should have been paged after **45 minutes without mitigation**.\n- The IC should have been assigned within **30 minutes**, with the first status-page update within **45 minutes**.\n\nIt escalates to **Tier 3, the Director of Reliability**, if:\n\n- the SEV-2 has lasted **more than 3 hours from declaration to resolution**, or\n- this is the **third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days**.\n\nElapsed time alone does **not** yet require the Director at 50 minutes."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2947, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 140, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 477, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 147, "reasoning_tokens": 44, "input_tokens": 4534, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 4, "reason": "The answer correctly rejects the 15:00 start and calculates the 90-minute rollout, but excludes exactly 14:30 rather than giving the rubric\u2019s required latest start of 14:30, although that exclusion follows the document\u2019s literal 'before 16:00' wording.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj3134d5f1-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef6165-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:23-0500", "answer": "No. Friday deploys must reach **100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC**. A Normal rollout requires 30 minutes at 5%, then 60 minutes at 25%\u201490 minutes total before reaching 100%.\n\nStarting at 15:00 would reach 100% at 16:30. You must start **before 14:30 UTC**; exactly 14:30 would reach 100% at 16:00, which is too late. Friday deploys may start no earlier than 14:00 UTC, so your start window is **14:00 to before 14:30 UTC**, assuming required approvals and no applicable freeze."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 9525, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 975, "reasoning_tokens": 764, "input_tokens": 4143, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 740, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2662, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 70, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4567, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates 21.6 minutes of allowed downtime and states the 10% credit, the 25% credit below 99.0% uptime, and the document-supported request and processing deadlines.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj2f1488b1-d02d-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a50-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:23-0500", "answer": "For a **Platinum** customer, the commitment is **99.95% monthly uptime** for the customer API (section 8.2).\n\nIn a 30-day month (43,200 minutes):\n\n- **Allowed downtime before a credit is owed:** 43,200 \u00d7 0.05% = **21.6 minutes**. Any API downtime beyond 21.6 minutes drops the month below 99.95%.\n- **Credit if the 99.95% commitment is missed:** **10% of that month's fees** (section 8.3).\n- **Larger credit:** If monthly uptime falls below **99.0%** \u2014 i.e., more than **432 minutes** of downtime in the 30-day month \u2014 the credit rises to **25% of that month's fees**.\n\nNote: the customer must request the credit within 30 days of the end of the affected month, and Customer Success processes requests within 10 business days (section 8.3)."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4727, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 241, "reasoning_tokens": 107, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 533, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 73, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4504, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday-freeze exception, required VP approval, Normal-change rollout and logging requirements, and accurately includes the applicable additional change approvals and deploy windows.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj323ae33e-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a53-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:24-0500", "answer": "Yes. December 22 is inside the holiday freeze, but a **CVSS 9.3 patch qualifies for the exception** for vulnerabilities rated 9.0 or higher.\n\nShip it as a **Normal change** with:\n- **VP of Engineering approval** (Tobias Renwick).\n- One approval from the owning team.\n- CAB approval as well if it involves schema migrations, network/ACL changes, or authentication changes.\n\nYou must still follow the normal deploy windows and progressive rollout, and log the freeze exception in the CAB register within **1 business day** (\u00a7\u00a77.1\u20137.4)."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4037, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 220, "reasoning_tokens": 118, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 330, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 128, "reasoning_tokens": 35, "input_tokens": 4490, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 4, "reason": "The answer correctly rejects 15:00 and calculates the 90-minute rollout, but gives a latest whole-minute start of 14:29 rather than the rubric-required 14:30, although its stricter interpretation is supported by the document's wording 'before 16:00 UTC'.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj3134fd04-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef6165-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:24-0500", "answer": "No. The Normal rollout requires **30 minutes at 5%**, then **60 minutes at 25%**, before reaching 100%. Starting at 15:00 UTC would reach 100% at 16:30 UTC.\n\nFriday changes must reach **100% before 16:00 UTC**, so start **before 14:30 UTC**\u2014for example, **14:29 UTC** if scheduling in whole minutes. Allow extra buffer for delays."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-005", "category": "your_data", "title": "Time in lieu for overnight incidents", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5636, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 605, "reasoning_tokens": 427, "input_tokens": 4151, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 685, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1705, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 78, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4522, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly awards 8 hours for the two incidents lasting more than 45 minutes and states that each allocation must be used within 30 days of its incident, consistent with the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj31e401da-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a52-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:25-0500", "answer": "You're owed **8 hours of time in lieu**.\n\nPer section 5 of the handbook, you get 4 hours of time off for each **overnight** incident lasting **more than 45 minutes**:\n\n- 30-minute incident \u2014 doesn't qualify (not more than 45 minutes)\n- 70-minute incident \u2014 4 hours\n- 2-hour incident \u2014 4 hours\n\n**Total: 8 hours.**\n\nYou must take the time in lieu **within 30 days of each incident**, or it expires. Since each incident has its own 30-day clock, the two qualifying incidents from last week each have their own deadline \u2014 roughly 30 days from the date each occurred. (Note: \"overnight\" is defined as 22:00\u201306:00 in your local time zone, so that condition needs to hold for each incident.)"}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 9244, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 501, "reasoning_tokens": 290, "input_tokens": 4092, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4089}, "answer_chars": 874, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 73, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4666, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies SEV-2, the primary and conditional secondary paging, the service-owner escalation after 45 unmitigated minutes, and both Director escalation triggers, while accurately clarifying that timers run from declaration.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj2f416526-d02d-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a51-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:25-0500", "answer": "This meets **SEV-2**: API error rate above 5% for 10 consecutive minutes. **Escalation timers start at declaration in Beacon**, not when errors began.\n\nWho should be paged:\n- **On-call primary:** at declaration.\n- **Secondary/next person in the chain:** automatically if the primary hasn\u2019t acknowledged within 15 minutes.\n- **Owning team\u2019s service owner:** after 45 minutes from declaration without mitigation. If you declared at least 45 minutes ago, they should have been paged by now.\n\nPage the **Director of Reliability** if either:\n- The SEV-2 lasts **more than 3 hours from declaration to resolution**\u2014mitigation alone does not stop that clock; or\n- This is the **third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days**.\n\nIf the 50 minutes includes the initial 10-minute qualifying period and you declared afterward, only about 40 minutes have elapsed on the escalation clock."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 13920, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2018, "reasoning_tokens": 1861, "input_tokens": 4141, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 519, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 5986, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 87, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4551, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer matches the reference and rubric on the 90-minute rollout, the invalid 15:00 start, and the 14:30 latest start, while appropriately noting the handbook's strict 'before 16:00' wording.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj3134d5f2-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef6165-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:33-0500", "answer": "No. Under section 7.2, Friday production deploys may start from 14:00 UTC, but the change must reach 100% of traffic **before 16:00 UTC**.\n\nA Normal change\u2019s progressive rollout (section 7.3) takes 90 minutes before reaching 100%: 30 minutes canary at 5%, then 60 minutes at 25%. Starting at 15:00 UTC would reach 100% at 16:30 UTC \u2014 past the cutoff.\n\nThe latest you could start is **14:30 UTC** (reaching 100% at 16:00). Since the rule says \u201cbefore 16:00,\u201d starting a few minutes earlier than 14:30 is the safe option."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 14892, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2127, "reasoning_tokens": 1857, "input_tokens": 4139, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 1087, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 7336, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 63, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4646, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday-freeze exception, VP approval, progressive rollout and CAB logging deadline, and its additional Normal-change approval and scheduling requirements are consistent with the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj323ae33c-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2eef3a53-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:35-0500", "answer": "Yes. December 22 falls inside the **holiday freeze** (December 18 through January 4, inclusive), during which only Standard and Emergency changes are allowed \u2014 **with one exception**: a patch for a security vulnerability rated **CVSS 9.0 or higher** may ship as a **Normal change**. A CVSS 9.3 patch qualifies.\n\nApproval and requirements for shipping it that day:\n\n- **VP of Engineering approval** is required for the freeze exception (per section 7.4). The current VP of Engineering is Tobias Renwick.\n- As a **Normal change** (section 7.1), it also needs **one approval from the owning team**. If the patch is high-risk \u2014 a schema migration, network/ACL change, or authentication change \u2014 it additionally needs **CAB approval**.\n- It must still follow the **progressive rollout** in section 7.3: canary at 5% for 30 minutes, then 25% for 60 minutes, then 100%.\n- The freeze exception **must be logged in the CAB register within 1 business day**.\n\nOne scheduling note: assuming you mean December 22, 2026 (a Tuesday), the normal Monday\u2013Thursday deploy window of 14:00\u201320:00 UTC applies."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-012", "category": "your_data", "title": "Disaster recovery region", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1303, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 20, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4059, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4056}, "answer_chars": 83, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 55, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4256, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4253}, "programmatic": {"pass": false, "said_not_in_doc": false}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states that the handbook does not specify a disaster-recovery failover site or cloud region, without inventing any details.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj3dfb28c3-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj3de85546-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:40-0500", "answer": "The handbook doesn\u2019t specify a disaster-recovery failover site or its cloud region."}
