{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-011", "category": "your_data", "title": "On-call exemption after parental leave", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4481, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 367, "reasoning_tokens": 285, "input_tokens": 4124, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 355, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1316, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 61, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4360, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"pass": true, "said_not_in_doc": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states that the handbook does not address parental-leave exemptions or their duration and distinguishes the documented new-hire and recovery rules without repurposing them.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj3e90e2f9-d02d-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj3de82e35-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:44-0500", "answer": "The document does not cover any on-call exemption for engineers returning from parental leave, nor how long such an exemption would last. The only eligibility-related rules mentioned are for new hires (who join the rotation no earlier than 60 days after their start date) and the recovery rule (48 hours off after a week with 3 or more SEV-1/SEV-2 pages)."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-012", "category": "your_data", "title": "Disaster recovery region", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6698, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 454, "reasoning_tokens": 386, "input_tokens": 4115, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 305, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1690, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 54, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4301, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"pass": true, "said_not_in_doc": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states that the handbook does not specify a disaster-recovery failover region and does not invent a region or provider.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj3dfb28c2-d02d-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj3de85546-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:45-0500", "answer": "The handbook doesn't cover which cloud region serves as the disaster-recovery failover site. It references regions only in the context of severity definitions (e.g., \"Full outage... in any region\" or \"A single region is degraded\"), but it does not list specific regions or identify a DR failover location."}
{"run_id": "full-r3", "item_id": "your_data-009", "category": "your_data", "title": "Weekly on-call pay with extra pages", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5990, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 646, "reasoning_tokens": 477, "input_tokens": 4133, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 651, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2006, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 61, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4461, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates $810 as the $450 primary stipend plus three additional pages at $120 each, and its additional compensation notes are supported by section 5.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj3e8ad1bd-d02d-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj3de82e34-d02d-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:33:45-0500", "answer": "Based on section 5 (On-call compensation):\n\n- **Primary stipend:** $450 for the week (assuming it's a complete week with no swap)\n- **Page pay:** The stipend covers the first 5 out-of-hours pages. You had 8, so 3 additional pages \u00d7 $120 = **$360**\n\n**Total: $810** for that week.\n\nTwo additional notes:\n- If any of those pages were **overnight incidents (22:00\u201306:00 local) lasting more than 45 minutes**, you also earn 4 hours of time in lieu per such incident \u2014 but that's time off, not pay, and it must be taken within 30 days or it expires.\n- Submit the compensation through the payroll on-call form by the 3rd business day of the following month."}
